window.TTBX={"meta":{"title":"Neon Ledger","subtitle":"An expansion for The Technomancer's Textbook","author":"Written for Alex","note":"Original material. Designed against the conventions of fifth edition and the lore of the cyberpunk tabletop tradition, Cyberpunk 2020/RED's roles and Humanity loss, Shadowrun's Essence, Gibson's ICE, and Altered Carbon's stacks and sleeves, but written from scratch rather than reproduced from any of them."},"classes":[{"name":"Wirewalker","hit":"d6","primary":["Int"],"saves":["Dex","Int"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Deception","Insight","Investigation","Perception","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Dart gun, machine pistol, pistol, plus any simple firearm","tools":"Hacking tools, electrician's tools","resource":"Bandwidth","tagline":"Walks into a building through its cabling and out through its bank account.","description":["There is a moment, about a second and a half after the jack seats, when the room you are sitting in stops being the room you are in. The Wirewalker lives for that second and a half. Everything after it is work, architecture unfolding in front of you floor by floor, ICE circling the edges of your attention like something that has not eaten in a while, and somewhere at the bottom a file worth more than the building.","Wirewalkers are not technicians. A technician fixes the network; a Wirewalker treats it as terrain. They map it, walk it, and leave through a door that did not exist before they got there. The good ones are never detected. The famous ones always are, which is how they became famous, and why so few of them are still breathing.","The body is the weak point and every Wirewalker knows it. While you are in the NET your meat is a slumped shape in a chair with an expensive cable coming out of it, and the crew standing over it is the only reason you will wake up."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Bandwidth","Programs Known","Max Tier"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Interface, Programs","3","3","1"],["2nd","+2","Trace Cleaning","4","4","1"],["3rd","+2","Deck Architecture","6","5","2"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","8","6","2"],["5th","+3","Cascade Run","11","7","3"],["6th","+3","Deck Architecture feature","13","8","3"],["7th","+3","Hot Sim","15","9","3"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","17","10","3"],["9th","+4","Ghost Protocol","20","11","4"],["10th","+4","Deck Architecture feature","22","12","4"],["11th","+4","Deep Dive","24","13","4"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","26","14","4"],["13th","+5","Overclock","29","15","5"],["14th","+5","Deck Architecture feature","31","16","5"],["15th","+5","Cold Read","33","16","5"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","35","17","5"],["17th","+6","Deck Architecture feature","38","17","5"],["18th","+6","Total Immersion","40","18","5"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","42","18","5"],["20th","+6","Root Access","45","19","5"]]},"features":[{"name":"Interface","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your deck is jacked to your nervous system, and Intelligence is the ability that moves it. You use Intelligence whenever a program calls for an attack roll or forces a saving throw."},{"type":"ul","items":["Interface attack bonus = your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier","Interface save DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier"]},{"type":"p","text":"You can only reach an architecture you have a physical or wireless path into. Everything a program does happens at the speed of thought, a full NET run takes seconds of real time, which is why your crew is usually still arguing about the plan when you tell them the door is open."},{"type":"table","title":"Interface","headers":["Your Level","What You Can Reach"],"rows":[["1st","Any system on the same local network, by cable or by standing next to it"],["5th","Any system within 1 mile that is connected to a public network"],["11th","Any system on the continent you can name and route to"],["17th","Any system, anywhere, that has ever touched the NET"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Programs","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know three programs from the program list, and learn more as you level. Running a program costs Bandwidth equal to twice its tier. Your Bandwidth pool is shown on the class table; you regain all of it on a long rest and half of it, rounded down, on a short rest spent jacked out and cooling."},{"type":"p","text":"Whenever you gain a level in this class you can also swap one program you know for another of the same tier or lower, decks are rewritten between jobs as a matter of hygiene."},{"type":"table","title":"Program List","headers":["Tier","Program","Effect"],"rows":[["1","Ping","You learn the number, rough position and alert state of every node and construct on the floor you occupy."],["1","Sleight","One camera, lock, turnstile or sensor within the architecture obeys one instruction for 1 minute."],["1","Scramble","A construct you can reach has disadvantage on its next attack against you, and cannot report you until the end of your next turn."],["2","Icepick","Make an Interface attack against one ICE. On a hit it takes 3d8 damage and its next action is lost to error handling."],["2","Skim","Copy one file, account or credential you have located. The theft is not noticed until the next audit."],["2","Deadbolt","Seal one physical door, vehicle or weapon's smartlink against its owner for 10 minutes."],["3","Meltdown","One machine, drone or vehicle within the architecture's physical reach takes 6d6 fire damage as you drive its power cell past tolerance."],["3","Wraith","You become invisible to the architecture's logs for 1 hour. Nothing you do this hour can be traced to you afterward."],["3","Puppet Thread","A drone or automated turret under the architecture's control fights for you for 1 minute."],["4","Cascade","Every ICE on your current floor makes a saving throw against your Interface DC. On a failure it is disabled for 1 minute."],["4","Blackout","All powered light, comms and sensors in a 120-foot radius of a node you control fail for 10 minutes."],["4","Rewrite","Alter one record, a warrant, a debt, a clearance, a death certificate, convincingly enough to survive casual inspection."],["5","Ghost in the Wire","You leave your body and exist purely as data for up to 1 hour, moving through any connected system at the speed of its cabling. Your body is unconscious and helpless. If it dies while you are out, you have until the end of the hour to find a new host."],["5","Root","You seize an entire architecture. For 1 hour every door, camera, drone and account inside it answers to you, and the corporation that owns it does not yet know."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Trace Cleaning","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes and 2 Bandwidth scrubbing your passage through a system. Any attempt to identify, locate or attribute your intrusion after the fact is made with disadvantage, and automatically fails unless the investigator's passive Intelligence (Technology) equals or exceeds your Interface save DC."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deck Architecture","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You settle into a way of running. Choose Icebreaker or Wraith Protocol, detailed below. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each. As normal you can't increase a score above 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cascade Run","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you run a program of tier 2 or lower, you can immediately run a second program of tier 1 as part of the same action, paying its Bandwidth normally. You can do this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once) per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hot Sim","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can run the interface hot, with the safety governors off. While hot, you add your Intelligence modifier to any damage a program deals, and your Interface save DC increases by 2."},{"type":"p","text":"The cost is that feedback reaches you. While hot, any damage dealt to you by ICE is doubled, and you cannot benefit from resistance to it. You can go hot or cold as a bonus action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ghost Protocol","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your body is no longer a liability while you run. While you are jacked in, you remain aware of your physical surroundings, you can take reactions with your body, and attacks against your body do not have advantage from your condition."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deep Dive","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can descend past the layer an architecture admits to having. Once per long rest you can spend 10 Bandwidth to reach a system's root layer directly, skipping every intervening floor and every piece of ICE standing on them. What waits at the root is the DM's business, and it is rarely just a file."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Overclock","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can push the deck past its rating, gaining 10 temporary Bandwidth that lasts for 1 minute. When the minute ends, you take 4d10 psychic damage and gain one level of exhaustion. You can do this once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cold Read","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have run enough architectures to recognise the hand that built one. On first entering an architecture you learn its owner, its rough age, whether it holds black ICE, and one thing its architect was trying to hide, usually the floor they over-defended."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Total Immersion","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You no longer need a deck. Your nervous system is the deck. You can interface with any system you touch, you cannot be locked out by removing hardware from you, and you have resistance to damage dealt by ICE."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Root Access","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can take 1 minute to seize an architecture outright, as though you had run the Root program, without spending Bandwidth and without a check. For the next hour the system is yours: its doors, its drones, its accounts, its cameras, its records."},{"type":"p","text":"Systems you have rooted remember you. You can re-enter any architecture you have ever rooted at will, from anywhere, for as long as it stands."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["wirewalker-icebreaker","wirewalker-wraith-protocol"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Puppeteer","hit":"d8","primary":["Int"],"saves":["Con","Int"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Athletics","Investigation","Perception","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Survival","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial firearms","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms","tools":"Tinker's tools, electrician's tools, land vehicles","resource":"Uplink","tagline":"Leaves the body in the van and goes to work in something better armoured.","description":["A Puppeteer does not drive. Driving is what you do with your hands. A Puppeteer jumps, drops their sense of self into a frame of ceramic and servo and wakes up as a four-wheeled thing doing ninety through a service tunnel, or as something the size of a wasp hovering behind a security officer's ear.","The rig makes the distinction between operator and machine an administrative one. Puppeteers describe the switch the way other people describe waking up: not a change of location but a change of what it feels like to have a body. Most of them keep at least one frame running at all times, and a fair number have stopped bothering to specify which body they mean when they say 'I'.","Their weakness is the same as the Wirewalker's and they resent the comparison. While you are out in a frame, the thing you were born in is sitting somewhere with its eyes rolled back. Every Puppeteer has a story about coming home to find someone standing over it."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Uplink","Frames","Frame Tier"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Jump Rig, Frame","2","1","1"],["2nd","+2","Remote Body","3","1","1"],["3rd","+2","Rig Doctrine","3","1","1"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","1","1"],["5th","+3","Split Attention","5","2","2"],["6th","+3","Rig Doctrine feature","5","2","2"],["7th","+3","Hardened Uplink","6","2","2"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","7","2","2"],["9th","+4","Field Fabrication","7","2","3"],["10th","+4","Rig Doctrine feature","8","2","3"],["11th","+4","Deep Jump","9","3","3"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","9","3","3"],["13th","+5","Swarm Logic","10","3","4"],["14th","+5","Rig Doctrine feature","11","3","4"],["15th","+5","Redundant Cortex","11","3","4"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","12","3","4"],["17th","+6","Rig Doctrine feature","13","4","5"],["18th","+6","Fleet Command","13","4","5"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","14","4","5"],["20th","+6","Second Body","15","4","5"]]},"features":[{"name":"Jump Rig","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a neural rig that lets you occupy a machine. As an action you can jump into any frame you control within 1 mile. While jumped in:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You see, hear and act through the frame, and your own body is unconscious.","You use your own Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma, and the frame's Strength, Dexterity and Constitution.","You use your own proficiency bonus, saving throw proficiencies and skills.","Damage to the frame does not harm you. If the frame is destroyed while you are in it you are ejected, take 2d6 psychic damage, and cannot jump again until you finish a short rest."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can jump back to your own body as a bonus action, or automatically when your body takes damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Frame","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have built one frame, a drone, a crawler, a rotor, a wheeled chassis, whatever the job wanted. It uses the Puppeteer Frame statistics, scaled by its tier on the class table. Building a replacement takes 8 hours and 500\u20b5 per tier."},{"type":"table","title":"Puppeteer Frame","headers":["Tier","AC","Hit Points","Speed","Str/Dex/Con","Attack"],"rows":[["1","13","10 + 5 per Puppeteer level","40 ft.","12 / 14 / 12","+Int, 1d8"],["2","15","15 + 6 per Puppeteer level","40 ft.","14 / 16 / 14","+Int, 1d10"],["3","17","20 + 7 per Puppeteer level","50 ft.","16 / 18 / 16","+Int, 2d6"],["4","18","25 + 8 per Puppeteer level","50 ft.","18 / 18 / 18","+Int, 2d8"],["5","20","30 + 9 per Puppeteer level","60 ft.","20 / 20 / 20","+Int, 2d10"]]},{"type":"p","text":"A frame is a construct. It is immune to poison and psychic damage, does not breathe, eat or sleep, and is vulnerable to the effects of EMP. You can spend Uplink to give a frame extra capability, see Remote Body."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Remote Body","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Uplink shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. While jumped in, you can spend Uplink as a bonus action for one of the following:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Burn (1), the frame's speed doubles until the end of your turn.","Harden (1), the frame gains resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.","Overclock Servos (2), the frame makes one extra attack this turn.","Sensor Sweep (1), the frame detects every powered object and living creature within 120 feet, through walls.","Emergency Eject (2), when the frame would be destroyed, it instead drops to 1 hit point and you are not ejected."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rig Doctrine","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Swarm Handler or Panzer Jockey. Your doctrine grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Split Attention","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can control a second frame. While jumped in, you can command your other frames with a bonus action; they act on your initiative and can each take one action. Only the frame you are jumped into uses your full ability scores and proficiency, the others act with their own statistics."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardened Uplink","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your connection cannot be casually severed. You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would eject you from a frame, jamming has no effect on your control, and your jump range increases to 10 miles."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Fabrication","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can build or rebuild a frame in 1 hour instead of 8 using scavenged material, and you can repair a destroyed frame for half the cost of a new one. Over a long rest you can also reconfigure a frame's chassis entirely, changing its shape, movement type and attack."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deep Jump","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can jump into machines you did not build. As an action you can attempt to seize any vehicle, drone or construct you can see: it makes a Charisma saving throw against your Uplink DC (8 + proficiency + Intelligence), and on a failure you control it as a frame for 10 minutes. Unattended and unintelligent machines fail automatically."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Swarm Logic","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frames coordinate without you. Frames you are not jumped into now act on their own initiative, take full turns, and add your Intelligence modifier to their attack and damage rolls."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Redundant Cortex","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your sense of self is backed up across every frame you run. You no longer take psychic damage when a frame is destroyed, and if your own body is killed while you are jumped in, you continue to exist in the frame indefinitely, your mind simply does not come back to a corpse."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Fleet Command","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can control any number of frames within range, and as an action you can give all of them the same order, which each carries out on your initiative."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Body","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One frame becomes indistinguishable from you in every way that matters. Choose a frame: it gains your Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores permanently, acts with your full proficiency whether or not you are jumped in, and can act independently while you occupy another frame."},{"type":"p","text":"If your original body dies, you wake up in this one, and the transition is so smooth that you may not notice for some hours which of you is doing the noticing."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["puppeteer-swarm-handler","puppeteer-panzer-jockey"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Chromehound","hit":"d10","primary":["Str","Dex"],"saves":["Str","Con"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Intimidation","Investigation","Perception","Stealth","Survival"],"armor":"All armor, shields","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial weapons","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms, plus heavy weapons","tools":"One set of artisan's tools of your choice","resource":"Adrenaline","tagline":"Traded most of a person for the reflexes to survive the trade.","description":["Every Chromehound started as someone who decided their body was not adequate to the problem in front of it. The first implant is always practical, a hand that doesn't shake, an eye that ranges. The tenth is practical too, and by then the arithmetic has stopped being about capability and started being about how much of the original owner is still on the premises.","They are the best close-quarters operators the city produces, and the shortest-lived. Corporations retain them and quietly budget for replacement. Crews want one on the team and want them sitting where they can be seen. The Chromehound knows all of this and takes the work anyway, because the work is the only place the wiring makes sense.","This class is built to be played against the Humanity track. A Chromehound gets stronger as they hollow out, and the strongest ones are perhaps four bad decisions from becoming something the rest of the party has to put down."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Adrenaline","Die","Tolerance"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Combat Awareness, Chrome Tolerance","2","d6","5"],["2nd","+2","Adrenaline Surge","2","d6","5"],["3rd","+2","Combat Doctrine","3","d6","10"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","3","d6","10"],["5th","+3","Extra Attack","3","d8","10"],["6th","+3","Combat Doctrine feature","4","d8","15"],["7th","+3","Threat Assessment","4","d8","15"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","4","d8","15"],["9th","+4","Pain Editor","5","d8","20"],["10th","+4","Combat Doctrine feature","5","d10","20"],["11th","+4","Extra Attack (2)","5","d10","20"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","5","d10","20"],["13th","+5","Hardware Sync","6","d10","25"],["14th","+5","Combat Doctrine feature","6","d10","25"],["15th","+5","Nothing Left to Lose","6","d10","25"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","6","d10","25"],["17th","+6","Combat Doctrine feature","6","d10","25"],["18th","+6","Last Stand","7","d12","30"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","7","d12","30"],["20th","+6","Apex Predator","8","d12","40"]]},"features":[{"name":"Combat Awareness","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your wiring runs threat assessment below the level of thought. You add your Constitution modifier to initiative rolls, you cannot be surprised while conscious, and you always know the direction of the nearest hostile creature within 60 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chrome Tolerance","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your nervous system has been rebuilt to carry load that would break a civilian. You gain a tolerance buffer equal to the Tolerance column of the class table. The buffer is spent last: your Humanity falls exactly as it would for anyone else, and you pass through Dissociated, Fraying and Flatlining on the same schedule, but once your Humanity reaches zero, the buffer keeps you on your feet until it too is gone."},{"type":"p","text":"In plain terms: you can carry more chrome than anyone else before the wheels come off. This is not a kindness. It means you will be the one still standing when you should have stopped."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adrenaline Surge","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Adrenaline dice shown on the class table, regained on a short or long rest. You can spend them as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Burst. When you make an attack roll, ability check or saving throw, spend one die after seeing the roll and add it to the result.","Sync. As a bonus action, spend one die and add it to your speed in feet times two, and to your AC until the start of your next turn.","Clot. As a bonus action, spend one die and regain hit points equal to the roll plus your Constitution modifier."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Combat Doctrine","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Reflex Arsenal or Bulwark Protocol. Your doctrine grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Threat Assessment","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can designate one creature you can see as a threat. Until the end of your next turn you have advantage on attack rolls against it, and it has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pain Editor","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your implants filter what reaches you. You have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage while you are below half your hit point maximum, and you are immune to the frightened condition."},{"type":"p","text":"You also no longer notice injury in time to be sensible about it. You do not know your own hit point total; the DM tracks it, and tells you only when you are reduced to 0."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack (2)","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardware Sync","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Every piece of cyberware you carry is now driven from the same tuned controller. For each 25 Humanity you have spent on installed ware, you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with weapons, to a maximum of +3."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nothing Left to Lose","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The emptier you are, the harder you are to stop. While your Humanity is at or below 39% of your starting score, you have advantage on all attack rolls and immunity to the charmed condition."},{"type":"p","text":"While your Humanity is at or below 19%, you also do not die at 0 hit points: you drop to 1 instead, once per long rest. The thing that stands back up is increasingly difficult for the people who knew you to talk to."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Last Stand","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can choose to keep acting. For 1 minute you act normally with 0 hit points, cannot be reduced below 0, and cannot be killed. At the end of the minute you drop, unconscious and dying, unless you have been healed above 0. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Predator","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Strength and Dexterity scores increase by 4, to a maximum of 24. You have advantage on initiative, and on the first round of any combat you can take an additional action."},{"type":"p","text":"Your tolerance buffer increases by a further 40, you are, at this point, more installed equipment than person, and the equipment is exceptional."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["chromehound-reflex-arsenal","chromehound-bulwark-protocol"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Streetdoc","hit":"d8","primary":["Wis"],"saves":["Int","Wis"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Deception","Insight","Investigation","Medicine","Nature","Perception","Persuasion","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Dart gun, machine pistol, pistol, revolver","tools":"Herbalism kit, tinker's tools, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Trauma Dice","tagline":"Keeps people alive in rooms that were not designed for it.","description":["There is a tier of medicine below the hospitals and above the vending machine that sells antibiotics, and the Streetdoc owns it. A back room with good light. A table that has been bleached more times than it has been replaced. A practitioner who will not ask where the bullet came from and will not file anything anywhere.","Some of them trained properly and lost the licence. Some never trained at all and are better than the ones who did. All of them do three jobs that the legitimate system refuses to: they patch trauma without paperwork, they install chrome that has not been approved by anyone, and they pull people back from the far end of the Humanity track when nobody else will take the appointment.","A Streetdoc in a crew is the difference between a hard job and a funeral. They know it. They charge accordingly, and most of them still end up working for free more often than not, which is the quiet tragedy of the profession."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Trauma Dice","Die","Ampules"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Trauma Kit, Field Medicine","4","d6","2"],["2nd","+2","Chem Cook","5","d6","2"],["3rd","+2","Practice","6","d6","3"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","7","d6","3"],["5th","+3","Combat Triage","8","d8","3"],["6th","+3","Practice feature","9","d8","4"],["7th","+3","Counsellor's Licence","10","d8","4"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","11","d8","4"],["9th","+4","Hardline Stabilise","12","d8","5"],["10th","+4","Practice feature","13","d10","5"],["11th","+4","Transplant","14","d10","5"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","15","d10","5"],["13th","+5","Adrenal Override","16","d10","6"],["14th","+5","Practice feature","17","d10","6"],["15th","+5","Crash Cart","18","d10","6"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","19","d10","6"],["17th","+6","Practice feature","20","d10","6"],["18th","+6","Miracle Worker","21","d12","7"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","22","d12","7"],["20th","+6","Death Is Negotiable","24","d12","8"]]},"features":[{"name":"Trauma Kit","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Trauma Dice shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. As an action, or as a bonus action on a creature you are already touching, you can spend any number of them: the target regains hit points equal to the total rolled plus your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"Trauma Dice are not magic. They work on the living, they do not regrow what is gone, and a creature that has been dead for more than a minute is beyond them."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Medicine","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can stabilise a dying creature as a bonus action. When you do, it regains 1 hit point instead of merely stabilising, if you spend at least one Trauma Die."},{"type":"p","text":"You also always know a creature's exact hit point total, conditions, and the nature of any poison, disease, drug or implant affecting it, simply by looking at it for 6 seconds."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chem Cook","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a long rest you can prepare a number of ampules shown on the class table, using a herbalism kit or artisan's tools. An ampule can be administered to a willing creature as an action, or thrown up to 20 feet as an improvised weapon. Choose each ampule's type when you prepare it:"},{"type":"table","title":"Ampules","headers":["Ampule","Effect"],"rows":[["Stim","The target gains advantage on attack rolls and saving throws for 1 minute, then one level of exhaustion."],["Coag","The target regains 2d8 + your Wisdom modifier hit points and stops bleeding."],["Clarity","The target ends one effect causing it to be charmed, frightened or poisoned, and has advantage on Wisdom saves for 10 minutes."],["Downer","A creature within 20 feet makes a Constitution saving throw against your Medicine DC or is poisoned for 1 minute; on a failure by 5 or more it also falls unconscious for 1 minute."],["Burnout","The target's next weapon attack this turn deals an extra 3d6 damage, and the target takes 1d6 necrotic damage it cannot reduce."],["Scrub","The target is cured of one disease, one poison, or one drug's addiction progress."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Medicine DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier. Unused ampules spoil when you next prepare a batch."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Practice","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Ripperdoc or Trauma Team. Your practice grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Combat Triage","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When an ally within 30 feet of you drops to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to spend one Trauma Die and bring them to 1 hit point, plus the die roll. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Counsellor's Licence","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are one of the few practitioners willing to treat Humanity loss, and one of the fewer who is any good at it. Therapy you administer costs half the usual credits and restores 2 Humanity per day instead of 1."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can spend 10 minutes and one Trauma Die talking a creature down from a Fraying or Flatlining episode: it is treated as one Humanity state higher until its next long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardline Stabilise","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allies within 30 feet of you that you can see have advantage on death saving throws, and a creature you have treated within the last hour cannot be reduced below 1 hit point by a source of damage that is not a critical hit."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Transplant","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a short rest you can perform surgery to install, remove or replace one piece of cyberware or one augment, without a clinic and without the usual surgery fee."},{"type":"p","text":"Ware you install personally costs 1 less Humanity, to a minimum of 1."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adrenal Override","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can override a creature's endocrine system. Until the end of its next turn it can take an additional action, moves at double speed, and automatically succeeds on Constitution saving throws. It then takes 4d8 necrotic damage and gains one level of exhaustion. Once per creature per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crash Cart","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can bring back a creature that has been dead for up to 1 minute, provided its body is largely intact. It returns with 1 hit point, one level of exhaustion, and a permanent reduction of 5 to its Humanity maximum, something is always left behind on the table. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Miracle Worker","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Trauma Dice heal for their maximum value instead of being rolled."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Death Is Negotiable","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can spend 1 minute and your entire remaining pool of Trauma Dice on a creature that has been dead for no more than 24 hours. It returns to life with full hit points, all conditions and diseases ended, and any missing limbs replaced with chrome of your choosing."},{"type":"p","text":"The creature's Humanity maximum is permanently reduced by 10. It does not remember being dead. Everyone it knows will notice that it is, in some small way that nobody can name, not quite the same person."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["streetdoc-ripperdoc","streetdoc-trauma-team"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Fixer","hit":"d8","primary":["Cha"],"saves":["Dex","Cha"],"skillCount":4,"skills":["Deception","History","Insight","Intimidation","Investigation","Perception","Performance","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Machine pistol, magnum, pistol, revolver","tools":"Forgery kit, one gaming set, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Favours","tagline":"Does not own the city, but knows who does and what they want.","description":["The Fixer is the reason the job exists. Somebody wanted something, somebody else could get it, and between those two people stood a third who knew them both and took a cut for the introduction. Multiply that by a career and you have a person who can produce a military-grade weapon, a surgeon, a clean identity or a helicopter, given four hours and a reason.","Fixers are not powerful in the way a Chromehound is powerful. Nothing about them wins a firefight. What they have is a map of obligation, who owes whom, who is overextended this month, whose brother works security at the building you need to enter, and the nerve to spend that map down to the last favour when it matters.","The job has a half-life. A Fixer survives by being more useful alive than dead to everyone who might otherwise consider the alternative, and that calculation has to be re-run every single week."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Favours","Die","Contacts"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Contacts, Favours","2","d6","2"],["2nd","+2","Market Sense","3","d6","2"],["3rd","+2","Operation","3","d6","3"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","d6","3"],["5th","+3","Leverage","4","d8","4"],["6th","+3","Operation feature","5","d8","4"],["7th","+3","Everybody Owes Somebody","5","d8","5"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","6","d8","5"],["9th","+4","Off the Books","6","d8","6"],["10th","+4","Operation feature","7","d10","6"],["11th","+4","The Right Person","7","d10","7"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","8","d10","7"],["13th","+5","Insurance","8","d10","8"],["14th","+5","Operation feature","9","d10","8"],["15th","+5","Untouchable","9","d10","9"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","10","d10","9"],["17th","+6","Operation feature","10","d10","10"],["18th","+6","City in the Pocket","11","d12","10"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","11","d12","12"],["20th","+6","The Whole Board","12","d12","15"]]},"features":[{"name":"Contacts","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know people. You have a number of contacts shown on the class table. Each is a named NPC with a speciality, a personality and a price, created with the DM. When you gain a contact you decide their field: ware, weapons, transport, documents, medicine, information, muscle, access, or law."},{"type":"p","text":"A contact can be reached in minutes and will tell you what they know for free. Anything more costs a Favour, money, or something they want. Contacts are people, not a resource pool: they can be arrested, bought, killed or turned, and a Fixer who burns them carelessly will find the next one harder to make."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Favours","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a ledger of outstanding obligation, represented by Favour dice shown on the class table. You regain all of them when you finish a long rest in a place where you can make calls. Spend them as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Call It In. As an action, spend a die to have a contact deliver something to your location within the hour, a weapon, a vehicle, a document, a person. The die roll times 1,000\u20b5 is the value ceiling of what arrives.","Name Drop. When you make a Charisma check, spend a die after rolling and add it to the result.","I Know a Guy. When the party needs a specialist, spend a die: one exists, nearby, and will hear you out.","Word Is Out. Spend a die to learn one useful, true piece of information about a person, building or organisation in the city."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Market Sense","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You always know the fair street price of any item, service or person, whether it is available in this city, and roughly who is holding it. You buy at 20% below market and sell at 20% above."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Operation","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Broker or Handler. Your operation grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Leverage","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes researching a creature you have met to find the thing it does not want known. The DM tells you one genuine piece of leverage. Once per long rest, you can use it: the creature has disadvantage on saving throws against your Charisma checks for the next hour, and will not willingly raise an alarm about you during that time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Everybody Owes Somebody","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you fail a Charisma check against a creature, you can spend a Favour die to discover that you have a mutual acquaintance. Reroll the check with advantage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Off the Books","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and up to eight creatures you name do not appear in official records for the next week: no transaction logs, no biometric hits, no arrival records. Renewing this takes 1 hour and a Favour die."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Right Person","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can declare that one of your contacts happens to be exactly who you need, present, positioned, or already inside. The DM adjudicates the details, but the coincidence holds."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Insurance","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have arranged for what happens if this goes badly. When you or an ally within 60 feet would drop to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction and spend two Favour dice: a prearranged contingency fires, a diversion, an extraction vehicle, a bribed guard looking elsewhere, and the target drops to 1 hit point and can immediately move up to their speed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Untouchable","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Too many important people need you alive. Organisations that would otherwise move against you hesitate: you have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened or imprisoned, and any faction that harms you must first weigh the cost, which the DM should make visible in play as delays, warnings and second thoughts."}],"sub":false},{"name":"City in the Pocket","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Favour dice are regained on a short rest as well as a long one, and Call It In has no value ceiling, if it exists in this city, it can be at your door within the hour, though the price may be dreadful."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Whole Board","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You see the shape of it all. Once per long rest you can spend 1 minute to ask the DM three questions about any ongoing situation, who benefits, who is lying, what happens next, and receive truthful answers."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, each of your contacts has by now become someone: a gang boss, a department head, a chief of staff. One of them, once per long rest, will do something genuinely enormous for you, and afterwards you will owe them, which is how this has always worked."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["fixer-broker","fixer-handler"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Firebrand","hit":"d8","primary":["Cha"],"saves":["Con","Cha"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Athletics","Deception","History","Insight","Intimidation","Performance","Persuasion","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Machine pistol, micro SMG, pistol","tools":"Two musical instruments, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Signal","tagline":"Turns an audience into a weather system and stands in the middle of it.","description":["Every authoritarian structure in this setting is terrified of exactly one thing, and it is not guns. It is a crowd that has stopped being afraid. The Firebrand is the person who makes that happen, on a stage, on a rooftop, on a hijacked frequency at three in the morning, in a square where the drones are already circling.","Some of them are musicians. Some are preachers, comedians, streamers, union organisers or professional liars. The common thread is a voice that people repeat afterwards, and the willingness to stand somewhere visible while saying something expensive.","Firebrands do not live quietly and mostly do not live long. They are also, more often than any other profession in this book, the reason anything in the city ever changes."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Signal","Inspiration Die","Audience"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Stage Presence, Signal","2","d6","30 ft."],["2nd","+2","Crowd Work","3","d6","30 ft."],["3rd","+2","Act","4","d6","30 ft."],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","5","d6","30 ft."],["5th","+3","Anthem","6","d8","60 ft."],["6th","+3","Act feature","7","d8","60 ft."],["7th","+3","Viral","8","d8","60 ft."],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","9","d8","60 ft."],["9th","+4","Feedback","10","d8","120 ft."],["10th","+4","Act feature","11","d10","120 ft."],["11th","+4","Mass Movement","12","d10","120 ft."],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","13","d10","120 ft."],["13th","+5","Martyr's Odds","14","d10","120 ft."],["14th","+5","Act feature","15","d10","120 ft."],["15th","+5","Living Symbol","16","d10","120 ft."],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","17","d10","120 ft."],["17th","+6","Act feature","18","d10","1 mile"],["18th","+6","Riot","19","d12","1 mile"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","20","d12","1 mile"],["20th","+6","Voice of the City","22","d12","City"]]},"features":[{"name":"Stage Presence","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are always, in some measure, performing, and people respond to it. You add your Charisma modifier to initiative rolls, and you can use Charisma in place of Strength or Dexterity for any check made to be seen, heard, reached or followed by a crowd."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Signal DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Signal","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Signal shown on the class table, regained on a long rest, the measure of how much attention you currently command. Spend it as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Hook (1). As a bonus action, one creature within your Audience range that can see or hear you must succeed on a Wisdom save against your Signal DC or have disadvantage on attacks against anyone but you until the end of your next turn.","Lift (1). As a bonus action, an ally within Audience range rolls your Inspiration die and adds it to their next attack roll, check or save.","Drown Out (2). As a reaction when a creature within range speaks, transmits or casts a spell with a verbal component, it must succeed on a Charisma save or the attempt fails and is wasted.","Turn (3). As an action, up to three creatures within range make Wisdom saves or are charmed by you for 1 minute, believing whatever you are currently claiming."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crowd Work","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can read a group the way others read a person. After 1 minute observing any gathering, you learn its mood, what it wants, what it is afraid of, and what single sentence would move it fastest in a direction of your choosing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Act","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Agitator or Pirate Signal. Your act grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Anthem","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can begin an anthem, sustained with your concentration for up to 1 minute. While it lasts, allies within your Audience range have advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened, and add your Inspiration die to the first attack roll they make on each of their turns."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Viral","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anything you perform, say or transmit propagates on its own. A message you release reaches the whole city within 24 hours and cannot be fully suppressed. You have advantage on Charisma checks made against any creature that has heard of you, and by now, most of them have."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Feedback","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within your Audience range damages you, every hostile creature within 30 feet of it takes thunder damage equal to your Inspiration die + your Charisma modifier as the crowd turns. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Mass Movement","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Turn option can now target any number of creatures within your Audience range, and lasts 10 minutes. Creatures that fail by 5 or more will actively assist you for the duration, carrying, blocking, shouting, standing in the way of things."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Martyr's Odds","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The story protects you as long as there is someone to tell it. While at least one creature within your Audience range can see you, you have advantage on death saving throws, and when you drop to 0 hit points every ally who can see you gains temporary hit points equal to your Firebrand level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Living Symbol","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have become shorthand for an idea. Creatures who oppose that idea have disadvantage on saving throws against your Signal options; creatures who share it automatically succeed on saves against being frightened while they can see you."},{"type":"p","text":"Your face is on walls you have never visited. This is not entirely an advantage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Riot","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can ignite a crowd. Every creature within your Audience range that is not your ally makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC. On a failure, for 1 minute it attacks the nearest creature it perceives as an authority, or flees if none is present. Structures, vehicles and cameras in the area are destroyed at the DM's discretion, because that is what happens."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Voice of the City","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Audience range is the city you are in. You can be heard, at will, by every person in it who is near any speaker, screen or open window."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can make a demand of the city. Every creature in it that can hear you makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC; those that fail spend the next hour doing what you asked, to the best of their ability. Whether the city forgives you afterward is the campaign's problem, not this feature's."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["firebrand-agitator","firebrand-pirate-signal"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Stackborn","hit":"d8","primary":["Con"],"saves":["Wis","Cha"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Deception","History","Insight","Investigation","Perception","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand","Stealth"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial firearms","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms","tools":"One type of artisan's tools, one gaming set","resource":"Stack Charge","tagline":"Has died before. Found it survivable. Kept the receipts.","description":["At the top of your spine, seated against the first vertebra, is a cylinder of alloy about the size of a coin. Everything you are is written on it, the body around it is hardware. You have worn this one for a while. You have worn others. When somebody shoots you in the chest, that is an inconvenience and an expense. When somebody shoots you in the back of the neck, that is murder.","Stackborn come from wherever stacks are cheap enough to be issued and expensive enough to be worth stealing. Some were born to it and have never known a life that ended permanently. Some had it fitted against their will. Some are carrying a stack that used to belong to someone else and have not told anyone, including, on bad nights, themselves.","The class is built around a single question the rest of the table will eventually ask out loud: after the fourth body, is the person sitting there still the one who started the campaign? The Stackborn's answer is usually yes, delivered slightly too quickly."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Charge","Imprints","Needlecast"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Cortical Stack, Sleeve","1","1","-"],["2nd","+2","Muscle Memory","2","1","-"],["3rd","+2","Stack Protocol","2","2","-"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","3","2","-"],["5th","+3","Needlecast","3","2","1 mile"],["6th","+3","Stack Protocol feature","4","3","1 mile"],["7th","+3","Past Lives","4","3","1 mile"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","5","3","1 mile"],["9th","+4","Resleeve","5","4","10 miles"],["10th","+4","Stack Protocol feature","6","4","10 miles"],["11th","+4","Ghostwalk","6","4","10 miles"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","7","5","10 miles"],["13th","+5","Backup","7","5","Planet"],["14th","+5","Stack Protocol feature","8","5","Planet"],["15th","+5","Two Places at Once","8","6","Planet"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","9","6","Planet"],["17th","+6","Stack Protocol feature","9","6","Planet"],["18th","+6","Stack Hardening","10","7","Planet"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","10","7","Planet"],["20th","+6","Real Death","12","8","Anywhere"]]},"features":[{"name":"Cortical Stack","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a cortical stack at the base of your skull. It records you continuously. While it is intact, dying is not final:"},{"type":"ul","items":["When you are reduced to 0 hit points and die, your stack survives unless the killing blow specifically targeted the back of your neck, or the damage was enough to destroy your body entirely.","A surviving stack can be recovered and fitted into a new body, a sleeve, in 24 hours, given a clinic and 25,000\u20b5. You return with all your levels, your memories up to the moment of death, and someone else's hands.","If your stack is destroyed, you are dead. Permanently, and beyond any resurrection this book or its parent system can offer."]},{"type":"p","text":"Your stack is an object with AC 20 and 10 hit points, and it can only be attacked by a creature that has you grappled or incapacitated, or by a called shot the DM allows."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sleeve","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your current body is equipment. When you take a new sleeve, choose one sleeve package: its bonuses replace those of your previous sleeve. You can also swap packages when you gain a level in this class, representing a refit."},{"type":"table","title":"Sleeve Packages","headers":["Package","Benefit"],"rows":[["Combat","+2 Strength or Dexterity (max 22). You gain proficiency with martial weapons."],["Endurance","+2 Constitution (max 22). Your hit point maximum increases by your Stackborn level."],["Infiltration","+2 Dexterity (max 22). You gain proficiency in Stealth and can squeeze through any gap a cat could."],["Diplomatic","+2 Charisma (max 22). You gain proficiency in Persuasion and one language."],["Labour","+2 Strength (max 22). Your carrying capacity doubles and you ignore the massive property on firearms."],["Synthetic","You do not need to eat, drink or breathe, and you have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease. Healing you receive is halved."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Muscle Memory","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Something of every body you have worn stays with you. You have a number of imprints shown on the class table. Each imprint is a skill or tool proficiency taken from a previous life; you are proficient in all of them, and you can swap one imprint for another whenever you finish a long rest, as an old life surfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Imprints do not feel like your own knowledge. They arrive as reflex, hands that know a weapon you have never fired, a language you have never studied answering itself in your mouth."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Stack Protocol","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Revenant or Archivist. Your protocol grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20 (22 where a sleeve package raises it). You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Needlecast","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can transmit yourself. As an action, spend 1 Stack Charge to cast your consciousness to any prepared sleeve, empty body or compatible construct within the range shown on the class table. Your old body drops, empty and alive but vacant, and you arrive instantly."},{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Stack Charge shown on the class table, regained on a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Past Lives","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per short rest, you can reach for a life that knew how to handle this. You gain proficiency, or expertise, if already proficient, in one skill of your choice for 10 minutes, and can add your Stackborn level to a single check made with it during that time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Resleeve","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your return is faster and cheaper: resleeving takes 1 hour rather than 24 and costs 5,000\u20b5. You can also take a sleeve that is not prepared for you, a fresh corpse, a vat body, an unoccupied clone, with no penalty beyond the DM's opinion of where you found it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ghostwalk","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For up to 10 minutes, spending 1 Stack Charge, you can exist without a body: pure signal moving through any connected system, unable to affect the physical world but able to observe it through any sensor, screen or microphone. Nothing can perceive you but a Wirewalker running hot."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Backup","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep a copy. Once per week you can commit a backup of yourself to secure storage. If both your body and your stack are destroyed, you return from the backup in a new sleeve after 1d4 days."},{"type":"p","text":"You return as of the moment the backup was taken. Everything since then, the job, the argument, the person you met last week, is gone, and the table should play that as it lands."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Two Places at Once","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can spend 3 Stack Charge to run a second instance of yourself in another sleeve for 1 hour. Both are you; both act on your initiative with full ability; both share your memories up to the split."},{"type":"p","text":"At the end of the hour the copies must merge or one must be destroyed. This is double sleeving, it is illegal essentially everywhere, and the penalty for it is usually the erasure of the stack rather than a court appearance."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Stack Hardening","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your stack's AC becomes 24 and its hit points 40, and it is immune to damage that does not specifically target it. You also become aware, instantly, of any attempt to access, copy or locate your backup."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Real Death","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been through enough bodies to stop treating any of them as load-bearing. When your sleeve is destroyed, you can immediately needlecast to any sleeve within range as a reaction, with no charge cost, arriving with half your hit point maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can no longer be permanently killed except by destroying every stack and every backup of you in existence, simultaneously. Any enemy who wants you gone has to make it a project."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["stackborn-revenant","stackborn-archivist"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Bioforged","hit":"d10","primary":["Con"],"saves":["Str","Wis"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Athletics","Intimidation","Medicine","Nature","Perception","Stealth","Survival"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial weapons","firearms":"All simple firearms","tools":"Herbalism kit","resource":"Biomass","tagline":"Grew the upgrade instead of bolting it on, and something is still growing.","description":["Chrome is an admission that the body failed. The Bioforged reject the premise. Their augmentation is cultured, not manufactured, tissue grown in a vat and coaxed into the host, a second heart, a nictitating membrane, muscle that contracts harder than muscle should. Nothing about them sets off a metal detector.","This is the expensive road. Grown ware costs more, takes longer, and requires a practitioner who is part surgeon and part gardener. What it buys is a body that still reads as a body: no Humanity cost, no cyberpsychosis, no dead-eyed drift. The price is paid on a different ledger entirely.","That ledger is Essence, the coherence of the organism you started as. Chrome hollows out the person. Grafts crowd out the species. A Bioforged who goes far enough does not lose their humanity so much as stop being the animal they were born as, and the last stretch of that road is not reversible."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Biomass","Grafts","Essence"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Grafts, Essence","2","2","20"],["2nd","+2","Adaptive Physiology","3","2","20"],["3rd","+2","Strain","3","3","19"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","3","19"],["5th","+3","Extra Attack","5","4","18"],["6th","+3","Strain feature","5","4","18"],["7th","+3","Regenerative Tissue","6","5","17"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","7","5","17"],["9th","+4","Second Heart","7","6","16"],["10th","+4","Strain feature","8","6","16"],["11th","+4","Rapid Mutation","9","7","15"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","9","7","15"],["13th","+5","Hyper-Adaptation","10","8","14"],["14th","+5","Strain feature","11","8","14"],["15th","+5","Immune Ascendancy","11","9","13"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","12","9","13"],["17th","+6","Strain feature","13","10","12"],["18th","+6","Apex Biology","13","10","12"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","14","11","11"],["20th","+6","Speciation","15","12","10"]]},"features":[{"name":"Grafts","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry cultured tissue rather than hardware. You know a number of grafts shown on the class table, chosen from the graft list below. Grafts are always active. Growing a new graft takes 8 hours of rest and a herbalism kit; you can replace one graft with another whenever you gain a level in this class."},{"type":"table","title":"Graft List","headers":["Graft","Effect"],"rows":[["Dermal Weave","Your AC equals 13 + your Dexterity modifier while unarmoured."],["Reinforced Frame","Your carrying capacity doubles and you have advantage on Strength saving throws."],["Spur Claws","Your unarmed strikes deal 1d8 slashing damage and count as martial weapons."],["Filter Lungs","You are immune to inhaled poison, tear gas and airborne disease, and can breathe anywhere with atmosphere."],["Tapetum","You have darkvision out to 120 feet and advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight."],["Adrenal Gland","Once per short rest you can take an additional action on your turn as a bonus action."],["Clotting Factor","You stabilise automatically at 0 hit points and cannot be made to bleed."],["Gecko Pads","You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed and can climb any surface."],["Lateral Line","You have blindsight out to 30 feet and cannot be surprised by a creature that is touching the ground."],["Toxin Sac","Your natural weapons deal an extra 1d6 poison damage, and a creature you hit must succeed on a Constitution save against your Graft DC or be poisoned until the end of your next turn."],["Stored Fat","You can go a month without food or water, and you have resistance to cold damage."],["Second Stomach","You can eat anything organic, including things that would poison a person, and regain 1d8 hit points when you do."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Graft DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Essence","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Grafts cost nothing on the Humanity track, nothing about you reads as artificial. They cost Essence instead, the coherence of the organism you started as. Your Essence is shown on the class table and falls as your body accumulates tissue that was never meant to be part of it."},{"type":"table","title":"Essence","headers":["Essence","State","Effect"],"rows":[["15 or more","Baseline","You read as an ordinary member of your species."],["11\u201314","Divergent","Medical scanners flag you as anomalous. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease, and disadvantage on Charisma checks with anyone who has seen your medical file."],["6\u201310","Unclassified","Healing you receive from another creature's abilities is halved, your biology no longer matches the textbook. You gain a natural weapon dealing 1d10 damage of a type you choose when you reach this state."],["1\u20135","Post-Human","You no longer register as a humanoid to any effect that targets creature type. You have resistance to one damage type of your choice, and you require a specialist to treat you at all."],["0","Speciated","You are no longer what you were. Without the 20th-level Speciation feature, your character becomes an NPC, something the party may still recognise, and may not."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Essence can be recovered by having grafts surgically removed: 1 Essence per graft, over a week of recovery, at a cost of 20,000\u20b5 and the loss of the graft."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adaptive Physiology","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your body reorganises to suit the problem. You have a pool of Biomass shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. As a bonus action you can spend it:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Harden (1). You gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage until the start of your next turn.","Surge (1). Your speed doubles and you gain a climbing speed until the end of your turn.","Knit (1). You regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your Constitution modifier.","Sharpen (2). Your natural weapons deal an extra 2d6 damage until the end of your turn.","Shed (2). You end one condition affecting you, or escape one grapple or restraint automatically, by leaving part of yourself behind."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Strain","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Chimeric or Symbiont. Your strain grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Regenerative Tissue","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You regain hit points equal to your Constitution modifier at the start of each of your turns, provided you have at least 1 hit point. Over a long rest you regrow lost limbs and organs."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Heart","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A redundant organ takes over when the first fails. When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can choose to drop to 1 instead. Once per long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You also have advantage on Constitution saving throws and cannot be reduced below half your hit point maximum by poison damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rapid Mutation","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can swap one graft for another from the list, taking effect immediately. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest, the body simply reconfigures, painfully and wetly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hyper-Adaptation","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first time each combat you take damage of a given type, you gain resistance to that damage type for the rest of the encounter."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Immune Ascendancy","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to poison and disease, cannot be paralysed or put to sleep, and automatically succeed on saving throws against any effect that would alter your form against your will."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Biology","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Constitution score increases by 4, to a maximum of 24. Your natural weapons deal an extra die of damage, and your Regenerative Tissue restores hit points equal to twice your Constitution modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Speciation","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You reach the end of the road deliberately rather than by accident. Your Essence can fall to 0 without you being lost: instead, you complete the transition into something new."},{"type":"p","text":"You know every graft on the list simultaneously. Your creature type changes to monstrosity, you no longer age, and you gain a flying or swimming speed equal to your walking speed, chosen when you speciate."},{"type":"p","text":"You are also, now, a founder. Whether the thing you have become can have children, and what they would be, is the finest campaign hook this expansion contains, and it is handed to the DM without further comment."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["bioforged-chimeric","bioforged-symbiont"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"}],"subclasses":[{"id":"wirewalker-icebreaker","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Icebreaker","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Goes through the defences rather than around them.","description":["Some runners treat ICE as weather to be avoided. The Icebreaker treats it as a door with a lock on it, and carries a very large key. This is the loud school of intrusion, fast, direct, and entirely dependent on being finished before the response team arrives.","It is also the school that gets hired when the job is not theft but demolition: when a client wants a network to stop existing and does not much care who knows."],"features":[{"name":"Assault Deck","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with martial firearms, and you know the Icepick program without it counting against your programs known. When you run Icepick, it deals an extra 1d8 damage."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, when you reduce a piece of ICE to 0 hit points you regain Bandwidth equal to your proficiency bonus."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Breach","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you enter a new floor of an architecture, you can immediately make one Interface attack against a construct on it as part of the same action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Feedback Loop","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a piece of ICE damages you, you can use your reaction to reflect it. The ICE takes damage equal to the damage you took, and any creature monitoring that ICE takes half as much psychic damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shatterpoint","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Interface attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 against constructs, and a critical hit from an Interface attack disables the target for 1 minute in addition to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Total War","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can declare an architecture hostile. Every piece of ICE in it takes 10d10 damage and must succeed on a saving throw against your Interface DC or be destroyed outright. The architecture itself is crippled for 24 hours and its owner will know, within the hour, exactly what grade of professional did this."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wirewalker-wraith-protocol","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Wraith Protocol","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Was never there, and has the absence of logs to prove it.","description":["The Wraith's ambition is to be an absence. No alarm, no trace, no anomalous power draw, no security officer waking at 4am with the sense that something is wrong with the building. A run that ends with anyone knowing a run happened is, by this school's standards, a failure regardless of what you came out holding.","Wraiths are the most expensive runners on the market and the hardest to find, for reasons that ought to be obvious."],"features":[{"name":"Null Signature","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know the Wraith program without it counting against your programs known, and its Bandwidth cost is halved for you."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are inside an architecture, ICE must succeed on a check against your Interface DC to perceive you at all. ICE that cannot perceive you cannot act against you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sidestep","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a construct would detect you or an attack would hit you inside an architecture, you can use your reaction to dump 3 Bandwidth and be somewhere else, the detection fails, the attack misses, and you move to any node on your current floor."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Borrowed Face","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 1 minute and 4 Bandwidth to become, as far as a system is concerned, someone who belongs there. You gain the credentials, clearance and access history of any person whose records the architecture holds, for 1 hour. Their logs will show them doing everything you do."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No Such Event","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can edit a system's memory of the last hour: alarms un-ring, footage shows an empty corridor, and any creature that witnessed you through that system's sensors must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your Interface DC or become convinced it saw nothing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nobody","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been erased so thoroughly and so often that reality has started cooperating. Automated systems, cameras, turrets, drones, biometric locks, tracking software, cannot perceive you unless you allow it. You do not appear in recordings. You cannot be the target of a scrying sensor, a trace, or any divination that works through technology."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-swarm-handler","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Swarm Handler","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"A hundred small problems arriving at once.","description":["Big frames get shot at. Small frames get ignored until there are sixty of them in the room and the exits are welded. The Swarm Handler builds down rather than up: palm-sized rotors, insect crawlers, things that fit through a ventilation grille and reassemble on the other side.","Handlers are the reason serious facilities filter their air."],"features":[{"name":"Motes","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain a swarm of motes, a cloud of palm-sized drones that occupies a 5-foot space, moves 30 feet (fly, hover), has AC 14 and hit points equal to five times your Puppeteer level, and is treated as one frame."},{"type":"p","text":"The swarm can occupy another creature's space. As an action while you control it, it deals 2d6 slashing damage to every creature in its space, increasing to 3d6 at 10th level and 4d6 at 17th."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Saturation","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your swarm imposes disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks made by any creature sharing its space, and creatures inside it cannot benefit from half cover or three-quarters cover."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reassemble","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When your swarm is destroyed, it re-forms at the start of your next turn with half its hit points, as long as any part of it remains. You can do this once per short rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Divide","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can split the swarm into two independent swarms, each with half the original's current hit points, as a bonus action. They can be merged again the same way."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grey Tide","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your swarm can now fill a 20-foot cube. Once per long rest you can command it to consume: every object and creature in its space takes 8d6 slashing damage, non-magical objects up to Large size are reduced to component parts, and the swarm heals to full from the material."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-panzer-jockey","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Panzer Jockey","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"One frame, enormous, and a deep reluctance to leave it.","description":["The other doctrine builds a fleet. The Panzer Jockey builds a home. One chassis, over-armoured and over-gunned, rebuilt after every job and never quite finished, a rolling argument that the correct response to a hostile city is a heavier vehicle.","Jockeys tend to name the frame, talk to it, and take its damage personally."],"features":[{"name":"Heavy Chassis","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame is Large, its tier is treated as one higher for hit points and armour class, and it gains proficiency with all firearms, including mounted weapons. You can mount one firearm on it, which it fires using your Intelligence modifier for attack and damage."},{"type":"p","text":"The frame's speed is reduced by 10 feet and it cannot fit through a space narrower than 5 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reactive Plating","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While jumped in, when the frame takes damage you can use your reaction to reduce it by 1d10 + your Puppeteer level. If the damage is reduced to 0, the attacker takes 2d6 fire damage from the venting plate."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Weapons Free","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can mount a second firearm, and when you take the Attack action while jumped in you can fire both as part of that action. Attacking at long range imposes no disadvantage for either."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Unstoppable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame ignores difficult terrain, cannot be knocked prone, restrained or grappled, and can move through walls of wood, plaster or glass, reducing them to rubble as it passes."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Fortress","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The frame becomes cover. Allies within 10 feet of it have half cover, and while you are jumped in it is immune to critical hits and has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when the frame would be destroyed, it instead sheds its outer armour in a 20-foot radius, every creature there takes 6d10 bludgeoning damage, and continues at half its hit point maximum."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-reflex-arsenal","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Reflex Arsenal","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Draws faster than the eye resolves, and does it four times.","description":["The Reflex Arsenal school buys speed and spends it on volume. Wired reflexes, smartlinked everything, a weapon in each hand and two more within reach. In a firefight the Arsenal operator is the one who has already acted twice while everyone else is still deciding to.","The tradeoff is structural: there is no armour in this build, only the theory that nothing gets to shoot back."],"features":[{"name":"Wired","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your speed increases by 10 feet and you can take the Dash or Disengage action as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can draw or stow any number of weapons whenever you could normally draw or stow one, and drawing a weapon does not end your turn's movement."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Double Tap","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take the Attack action with a one-handed firearm, you can make one additional attack with a different one-handed firearm you are holding as a bonus action, and you add your ability modifier to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Preemption","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within 30 feet of you takes an action, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against it before its action resolves. If that attack reduces it to 0 hit points, its action is lost."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Blur","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Attack rolls against you have disadvantage while you are not incapacitated and are wearing no armour heavier than light armour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Trigger Discipline","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once on each of your turns when you score a critical hit or reduce a creature to 0 hit points, you can immediately take another full Attack action."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-bulwark-protocol","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Bulwark Protocol","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Stands where the shooting is and refuses to be a casualty.","description":["Bulwark operators are bought by people who need to arrive somewhere alive. The build is subdermal plate, structural reinforcement and a reworked pain response, a body optimised not for output but for continuing to exist in conditions where existing is the hard part.","They are the closest thing the street has to a knight, and they know it, and most of them find the comparison embarrassing and accurate."],"features":[{"name":"Subdermal Plate","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are wearing no armour or light armour, your AC equals 13 + your Constitution modifier + your Dexterity modifier (maximum +2). This stacks with a shield."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency with heavy weapons and can ignore the massive property on firearms."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Interpose","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see attacks a target within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to become the target instead. The attack is made against you, and you have resistance to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ablative Systems","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At the start of each of your turns in combat you gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier, which last until the start of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Immovable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You cannot be moved against your will, knocked prone, or teleported by an unwilling effect. Difficult terrain costs you no extra movement, and you have advantage on saving throws against effects that would incapacitate you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bunker","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and every ally within 10 feet of you have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from ranged attacks."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as a reaction to taking damage, you can lock down: until the start of your next turn, you and every ally within 10 feet take no damage from any source."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-ripperdoc","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Ripperdoc","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Installs chrome anywhere, including mid-firefight.","description":["The Ripperdoc's speciality is the surgery that should not be attempted outside an operating theatre, performed outside an operating theatre, usually at speed. They keep a catalogue in their head and a case of ware in the boot, and their waiting room is whatever hallway you bled into.","Their clients love them, distrust them, and come back, because nobody else will fit a cyberlimb in ninety minutes with no questions and no records."],"features":[{"name":"Back-Alley Clinic","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can install cyberware or augments over a short rest, anywhere, without a clinic. The surgery fee for anything you install is halved."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency with tinker's tools and electrician's tools if you don't have it, and can identify any implant a creature carries on sight."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Fitting","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can install a single tier 1 implant into a willing creature in combat. It functions immediately. The creature takes 2d6 necrotic damage and loses Humanity as normal."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chop Shop","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can salvage installed ware from a creature that is dead, unconscious or willing, recovering it intact in 10 minutes. Salvaged ware can be resold at half value or installed as normal."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Tuned Install","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ware you install performs beyond specification. A creature carrying an implant you personally installed adds your proficiency bonus to one ability check or saving throw of its choice per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rebuild","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, over 1 hour, you can rebuild a willing creature. It gains your choice of two tier 3 implants at no credit cost and no Humanity cost, replacing existing ware if needed, and regains all hit points and Hit Dice."},{"type":"p","text":"The creature is incapacitated for the hour and for 1 hour afterwards, which means you had better not be doing this anywhere interesting."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-trauma-team","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Trauma Team","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Arrives fast, extracts under fire, bills later.","description":["Somewhere between an ambulance service and a private army sits the response contract: a subscriber goes critical, a team drops on the roof, and the client is in surgery inside four minutes regardless of who is shooting at whom. Doctors who came up through that work never really leave the tempo behind.","They are conditioned to go toward the gunfire, which makes them extraordinary in a crisis and difficult to insure."],"features":[{"name":"Response Protocol","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with medium armor and martial firearms."},{"type":"p","text":"When an ally within 60 feet drops to 0 hit points or is reduced below half their hit point maximum, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed toward them without provoking opportunity attacks."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Under Fire","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can administer an ampule, use your Trauma Kit or stabilise a creature without provoking opportunity attacks, and doing so does not break your concentration or your cover."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extraction","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can grab an ally within 5 feet and move up to your speed, carrying them, then spend Trauma Dice on them as part of the same action. The ally's movement is not spent."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Golden Hour","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can declare a golden hour. For the next minute, every ally within 60 feet of you that drops to 0 hit points is stabilised automatically at the start of their next turn, and no ally within 60 feet can die from hit point damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No One Left","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Combat Triage reaction has no limit on its uses, and when you use it the ally regains hit points equal to the die roll plus your Streetdoc level instead of 1 plus the roll."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, allies you have treated within the last hour who die can be revived by your Crash Cart feature for up to 10 minutes after death rather than 1."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-broker","cls":"Fixer","name":"Broker","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"If it can be bought, stolen or fabricated, it is already on its way.","description":["The Broker's discipline is logistics. Not people, goods. Where the shipment is, who is short this month, which warehouse has a night manager with debts, what a prototype is worth before anyone official knows it exists.","A Broker treats the crew as a supply problem to be solved, and is usually offended by how badly they treat the equipment."],"features":[{"name":"The Catalogue","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can acquire any item from this book's equipment, cyberware or augment lists at half price, given 24 hours and a legal or illegal channel."},{"type":"p","text":"You also start each job with a stash: choose items from the equipment chapter worth up to 1,000\u20b5 times your Fixer level, held in caches around the city. Retrieving one takes an hour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Quartermaster","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you spend a Favour die on Call It In, the value ceiling is doubled and the delivery arrives in 10 minutes rather than an hour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grey Import","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can procure things that are not supposed to exist on this market: military hardware, prototype ware, restricted chems. Such items cost triple and require a Favour die, but they are obtainable, and nobody asks."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Depreciation","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Equipment you supply to allies performs above grade. An ally using a weapon, armour or vehicle you personally sourced adds your proficiency bonus to one attack roll, damage roll or saving throw made with it per short rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Arms Dealer","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, over 10 minutes, you can outfit the entire party for a specific job: every ally gains one item of your choice from the equipment, cyberware or augment lists worth up to 50,000\u20b5, on loan, for the duration."},{"type":"p","text":"What is not returned comes out of everyone's cut."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-handler","cls":"Fixer","name":"Handler","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Runs people the way other Fixers run product.","description":["Handlers deal in the only asset that thinks for itself. They recruit, they place, they maintain, an informant inside a corp tower, a cousin on a loading dock, a bored security officer who now checks a particular camera less often than she should.","The good ones are genuinely liked by their assets, which is both the tradecraft and the thing that eventually breaks them."],"features":[{"name":"Assets","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Two of your contacts become assets: they are placed somewhere useful and will take real risks for you. You gain one additional asset at 10th and 17th level."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can activate an asset to accomplish one off-screen task within their reach, unlocking a door, deleting a record, delaying a patrol, getting a package inside. It works, though not always cleanly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Read the Room","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can use a bonus action to study a creature you can see. You learn its greatest current fear, its greatest current want, and whether it is currently lying to you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Recruiter","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can attempt to turn a hostile humanoid that can hear and understand you. It makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Fixer DC (8 + proficiency + Charisma). On a failure it is charmed for 10 minutes and treats you as a trusted employer; if the encounter ends without it being harmed by your side, it may become a contact. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deniability","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a plan involving one of your assets fails, it fails away from you. You cannot be implicated, traced or identified as the source, and any creature attempting to do so believes it has found someone else instead."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Everyone Is Somebody's","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can reveal that a creature you are facing is, or can immediately be made, one of yours. The creature makes a Charisma saving throw against your Fixer DC. On a failure it will not act against you or your allies for 1 hour, and will provide one piece of true, useful information about its employer."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-agitator","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Agitator","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Arrives with a grievance and leaves with a mob.","description":["The Agitator works the physical crowd, the picket, the queue, the square, the transit platform at the end of a bad shift. They are organisers before they are performers, and what they build does not need them present to keep going, which is the whole point and also how they keep getting away.","Corporate security profiles them as force multipliers, which is exactly correct and deeply unflattering to everyone involved."],"features":[{"name":"Rabble","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Wherever people are gathered, you can raise a mob. As an action, up to ten bystanders within your Audience range make Wisdom saves against your Signal DC; those that fail join you for 10 minutes as a crowd."},{"type":"p","text":"A crowd occupies a 20-foot square, moves 20 feet on your turn, and any hostile creature inside it has disadvantage on attack rolls and treats the area as difficult terrain."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Human Shield","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are within a crowd, ranged attacks against you have disadvantage and you have half cover. You can move through a crowd's space freely."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Escalation","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your crowd can act. As a bonus action you can order it to surge: every hostile creature in its space takes bludgeoning damage equal to twice your Inspiration die and must succeed on a Strength save against your Signal DC or be knocked prone and moved 10 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Contagion","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Creatures that flee, are charmed, or are knocked prone by your features spread it. One additional creature within 10 feet of them must make the same save."}],"sub":false},{"name":"General Strike","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can call a stoppage. For the next hour, in a district of the city, the ordinary machinery of life halts: transit stops, shutters come down, shifts walk out, and the authorities are fully occupied."},{"type":"p","text":"Within that district, hostile reinforcements do not arrive, surveillance is overwhelmed, and every check you or your allies make to move unseen through public space succeeds."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-pirate-signal","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Pirate Signal","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Owns a frequency they were never licensed for.","description":["Pirate Signal broadcasts. From a van, a rooftop rig, a hijacked corporate tower, wherever the aerial goes up, the show goes out, and for as long as it is on air the audience is everyone within range of a screen.","They are the closest thing this setting has to a free press, which mostly means they are the closest thing it has to a wanted list."],"features":[{"name":"On Air","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a transmitter rig. While broadcasting, your Audience range extends to everyone within 1 mile who is near any active screen, speaker or comm, whether or not they can see or hear you directly."},{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with hacking tools and electrician's tools, and can use Charisma instead of Intelligence for checks made to work a broadcast or comms system."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Signal Jam","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can flood local spectrum. For 1 minute, within 300 feet, all hostile comms, drone control, smartlinks and remote sensors fail, and creatures relying on them have disadvantage on attack rolls. Allies you choose are unaffected."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deepfake","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can fabricate a broadcast of a real person saying or doing something they did not. Creatures who see it must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw against your Signal DC or believe it; disproving it takes a week and a resourced investigation, by which point it has done its work."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Untraceable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your broadcasts cannot be located, jammed or taken off air by anything short of physically destroying your rig, and you always know when someone is trying."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Emergency Broadcast","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can seize every channel in the city for 1 minute. During it you can be seen and heard by everyone, you know you are being listened to, and any Signal option you use can target any number of creatures in the city."},{"type":"p","text":"Afterwards, everyone who matters knows it was you."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-revenant","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Revenant","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Keeps coming back, and keeps a list.","description":["Some Stackborn treat resleeving as a medical procedure. The Revenant treats it as a tactical reset. They have died more than most and take it worse each time, not afraid, exactly, but accumulating. Every sleeve they wear is built around finishing something the last one started.","They are extremely hard to discourage, which is the polite way of saying they are difficult to be in a party with."],"features":[{"name":"Death Debt","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take a new sleeve after dying, mark the creature or organisation that killed you. You have advantage on attack rolls against them, and deal an extra 1d6 damage to them, until the debt is settled to your satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"You can hold one debt at a time, increasing to two at 10th level and three at 17th."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Spite","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against a creature within reach before you fall."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rebuilt for This","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Each new sleeve you take comes optimised. You gain a second sleeve package, and its ability score increase stacks with the first."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Terminal Velocity","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are below half your hit point maximum you gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and you have resistance to all damage. You do not care what happens to this body, and the body has been informed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nothing Sticks","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when you die, you return immediately in a spare sleeve you have staged nearby, at half hit points, on your next turn. No clinic, no downtime, no 24 hours."},{"type":"p","text":"The people who just killed you find this deeply demoralising, and the DM is encouraged to let them react accordingly."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-archivist","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Archivist","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Carries more lives than are strictly theirs.","description":["The Archivist collects. Stacks, imprints, fragments, the recorded last hours of people nobody else kept. Some do it out of scholarship, some out of grief, some because a personality stored in a drawer is the most valuable and most blackmailable object in the city.","An Archivist is never quite alone in their own head, and has mostly made peace with the arrangement."],"features":[{"name":"The Collection","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a small case of recorded personalities. Your imprints double, and you can swap any imprint as a bonus action rather than on a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also consult the collection: once per short rest, ask the DM one question about a place, organisation or person that existed within the last century, and receive a true if incomplete answer from someone who was there."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Borrowed Hands","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you make an attack roll, ability check or saving throw, you can call up a specialist from the collection and add your Charisma modifier to the result. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Read the Stack","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can interface with a cortical stack, including one taken from a corpse, over 10 minutes, and experience its owner's final hour in full. You learn what they knew, what killed them, and one secret they were keeping."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Composite","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You blend the collection into yourself. You gain proficiency in all saving throws, and you cannot be charmed, frightened or possessed, there is no clear single mind in there to take hold of."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Congress","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can convene the collection for 1 minute. During it you have advantage on every ability check and saving throw, you can take two actions on each of your turns, and you cannot be surprised."},{"type":"p","text":"Afterwards you take 6d6 psychic damage, and you spend the next hour unsure which of the opinions in your head is yours."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-chimeric","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Chimeric","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Borrowed the best parts of six species and kept going.","description":["The Chimeric strain treats the animal kingdom as a parts catalogue. Cat's eyes, mantis forelimbs, the pressure tolerance of something that lives at depth, grafted in, tuned, and held together by a great deal of expensive immunosuppression.","Chimerics are visibly not standard. Most stop trying to pass fairly early, and a few find the freedom in that genuinely liberating."],"features":[{"name":"Beast Grafts","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain two additional grafts, and they do not reduce your Essence."},{"type":"p","text":"Your natural weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Predator's Read","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks relying on smell or hearing, and you can track a creature by scent for up to 24 hours after it passed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pounce","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"If you move at least 20 feet in a straight line toward a creature and hit it with a natural weapon on the same turn, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your Graft DC or be knocked prone. If it is prone, you can make one additional attack against it as a bonus action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hybrid Vigour","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose two damage types. You have resistance to both. Additionally, you can spend 2 Biomass as a reaction to gain immunity to one damage type until the start of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Form","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 4 Biomass to assume your apex form for 10 minutes. You become Large, your natural weapons deal an extra 2d8 damage, your speed increases by 20 feet, your reach increases by 5 feet, and you have advantage on Strength checks and saving throws."},{"type":"p","text":"While in this form you cannot speak in any language, use firearms, or pass for a person under any circumstances at all."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-symbiont","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Symbiont","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Is not alone in there, and the other one is helping.","description":["The Symbiont strain does not graft tissue. It hosts an organism, a cultured partner, grown alongside, seated along the spine and through the chest cavity, with its own reflexes and its own opinions about danger.","Hosts describe the relationship in wildly different terms: a colleague, a pet, a second set of instincts, a passenger who will not stop talking. What they agree on is that it is very good at keeping them alive, and that it wants things."],"features":[{"name":"The Passenger","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You host a symbiont. It has its own senses and reflexes:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You cannot be surprised, and you have advantage on initiative rolls.","You can see in all directions, attackers gain no benefit from being unseen or behind you.","As a reaction, the symbiont can make one unarmed strike dealing 1d8 + your Constitution modifier piercing damage against a creature within 10 feet."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shared Burden","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The symbiont takes some of what hits you. When you take damage, you can use your reaction to reduce it by 1d10 + your Bioforged level. Doing so costs 1 Biomass and the symbiont is sluggish until the end of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Opinion","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your symbiont notices what you miss. When you fail an ability check or saving throw, it can insist: reroll, with advantage. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"It is not always right. It is, however, always confident."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extension","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The symbiont can leave you for short periods. As an action, it detaches and acts as a separate creature with your Constitution score, AC, half your hit points and a speed of 40 feet, for up to 10 minutes. It acts on your initiative and you can see through its senses. If it dies, you take 6d6 necrotic damage and lose this feature until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Two Minds","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and the symbiont act in parallel. You can take two reactions per round rather than one, and once on each of your turns you can take an additional bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, if you are reduced to 0 hit points, the symbiont takes over: you act normally for 1 minute at 0 hit points, at which point you drop unless healed. Once per long rest. What it does with the minute is broadly what you would have done, with fewer reservations."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"artificer-graft-surgeon","cls":"Artificer","name":"Graft Surgeon","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Installs chrome on a folding table and bills you for the table.","description":["A Graft Surgeon learns anatomy the way other artificers learn clockwork: as an assembly with tolerances. They cut, seat the hardware, close, and hand over a card with a number on it. The work is legal about forty percent of the time. What separates them from a back-alley cutter is that they tell you how much of you they are about to spend before they start, and they are usually right."],"features":[{"name":"Surgeon's Kit","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with surgeon's tools and tinker's tools. If you already have proficiency with either, you gain proficiency with one other set of artisan's tools of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"You can install or remove cyberware anywhere you can lay a body flat, with no clinic and none of the usual week of convalescence. Removal still refunds Humanity as normal. Cyberware you personally install costs its recipient 1 less Humanity, to a minimum of 1."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grafts","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep a case of pre-cultured tissue and hardware ready to seat. Over a short rest you can apply one graft from the table below to yourself or to a willing creature you touch. A creature can carry only one graft at a time, and you can have a number of grafts in the world equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one). Applying another beyond that limit ends the oldest."},{"type":"p","text":"A graft lasts until you finish a long rest, at which point the tissue is spent and sloughs. Grafts are not real chrome and cost no Humanity. Everyone involved knows this and nobody enjoys the process anyway."},{"type":"table","title":"Grafts","headers":["Graft","Effect"],"rows":[["Clotting Weave","Once, when the creature takes damage, it can use its reaction to reduce that damage by 2d6. The graft is then spent."],["Bone Spur","The creature's unarmed strikes deal 1d6 slashing damage and count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance."],["Second Lung","The creature can hold its breath for 1 hour, ignores the effects of thin or contaminated air, and has advantage on saving throws against inhaled poison."],["Mirror Retina","The creature gains darkvision out to 60 feet, or extends existing darkvision by 30 feet, and can see through non-magical smoke and fog."],["Anchor Tendon","The creature has advantage on saving throws and ability checks made to avoid being knocked prone, grappled or moved against its will. Its carrying capacity doubles."],["Ganglion Splice","The creature gains a +2 bonus to initiative rolls and cannot be surprised while it is conscious."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Triage Line","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can close a wound faster than it opens. As a bonus action you can touch a creature that has taken damage since the end of your last turn. It gains temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier, and it can immediately repeat one saving throw against an effect currently causing it to be poisoned, blinded or paralysed."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crash Cart","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your grafts no longer slough. A graft you apply lasts until you remove it or until it is spent."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature carrying one of your grafts drops to 0 hit points, the graft fires whatever is left in it. The creature drops to 1 hit point instead and the graft is spent. Once you have saved a creature this way, you cannot do so again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Whole-Body Revision","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Given a table, eight hours and 10,000 credits in parts, you can rebuild a willing creature from the inside out. At the end of the work it gains one of the following permanently, chosen when the work begins. A creature can be revised only once, ever, and revision requires a subject who trusts you enough to be unconscious for a working day."},{"type":"ul","items":["Reinforced Frame. The creature's hit point maximum increases by an amount equal to your artificer level, and it has advantage on saving throws against being knocked prone or moved against its will.","Scrubber Liver. The creature is immune to poison damage and to the poisoned condition.","Load-Bearing Spine. The creature's carrying capacity doubles and it gains a climb speed equal to its walking speed.","Quiet Wiring. The total Humanity cost of the creature's installed cyberware is reduced by 5, restoring that much Humanity. This cannot take a creature above its starting Humanity score."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can also work fast and badly. As an action, touch a creature and expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher. It regains 4d8 hit points and, until the end of your next turn, has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. When the resistance ends it gains one level of exhaustion, because you have just made its body do something it would not have volunteered for."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"artificer-ordnance-chemist","cls":"Artificer","name":"Ordnance Chemist","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Does not make guns. Makes what goes in them, and prices it by the round.","description":["Guns are a solved problem and an Ordnance Chemist is not interested in them. They make the ammunition: a flat case of hand-loads, each with a different coloured seal, each doing something the manufacturer would describe in writing as a defect. The bench smells of solvent and ozone and travels in a shock-mounted trunk. A chemist who runs dry halfway through a job is, by the trade's own standards, an amateur."],"features":[{"name":"Loading Bench","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with alchemist's supplies and with martial firearms. If you already have proficiency with alchemist's supplies, you gain proficiency with one other set of artisan's tools of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"Given an hour and access to scrap, you can manufacture ordinary ammunition of any kind you are proficient with at no cost. You do not run out of ordinary rounds unless someone has taken your bench, which happens more often than you would like."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Payloads","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Between jobs you prepare charged rounds. You have a number of payloads equal to your Intelligence modifier + your proficiency bonus (minimum two). When you hit a creature with a ranged weapon attack using ammunition, you can spend one payload to apply one effect from the table below. You choose after the hit lands; the round was always going to be whatever you needed."},{"type":"p","text":"A payload's saving throw DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier. You regain all expended payloads when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"table","title":"Payloads","headers":["Payload","Effect"],"rows":[["Frangible","The target takes an extra 1d6 piercing damage, and the next attack roll made against it before the end of your next turn has advantage."],["Thermite Core","The target takes an extra 1d6 fire damage and must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or catch fire, taking 1d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns until it or an adjacent creature uses an action to put it out."],["Sodium Scatter","The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the end of its next turn."],["Nerve Agent","The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have disadvantage on its next attack roll and be unable to take reactions until the end of its next turn."],["Adhesive Gel","The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or have its speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn."],["Signal Round","For the next minute the target sheds dim light in a 10-foot radius, cannot benefit from invisibility or from being hidden, and can be tracked by anyone holding the paired receiver."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Stable Compounds","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your chemistry stops being conservative. The extra damage dealt by a payload, and the ongoing damage of any effect it causes, increases from 1d6 to 2d6."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when you spend a payload you can apply its effect to a second creature within 10 feet of the target. That creature makes any saving throw the payload calls for, but takes no damage from it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Countermeasures","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have started carrying things for problems that have not happened yet. As a bonus action you can spend a payload to throw a canister at a point within 30 feet. It bursts in a 15-foot-radius sphere. Choose one effect when you throw it; it lasts until the start of your next turn."},{"type":"ul","items":["Smoke. The area is heavily obscured. You and any creatures you chose when you threw the canister ignore this obscurement.","Damper. Creatures in the area cannot use comms, smartlinks or the NET, have disadvantage on ranged attack rolls, and are invisible to drones and electronic sensors.","Scrubber. The area is cleared of gas, smoke and airborne contaminants, and each creature in it can end one effect currently causing it to be poisoned.","Shear. Each creature in the area when the canister bursts must make a Constitution saving throw against your payload DC, taking 4d6 thunder damage and being deafened until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half as much damage and no deafness on a success."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Overpressure","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can spend 1 minute and three payloads hand-loading a single round. It is the best thing you will ever make and you can only hold one at a time. The compound goes inert if you have not fired it before your next long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"When you hit a creature with the round, it takes an extra 8d6 damage of a type you chose while loading (acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder) and must make a Constitution saving throw against your payload DC. On a failure it is stunned until the end of your next turn and all of its installed cyberware stops functioning for 1 minute. On a success it takes half the extra damage and is not stunned."},{"type":"p","text":"If the attack misses, the round is gone anyway."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"artificer-ward-architect","cls":"Artificer","name":"Ward Architect","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Builds the wards into the building, then charges rent on the safety.","description":["A Ward Architect reads a floor plan the way a duellist reads a stance. Doorways are choke points, load-bearing walls are anchor points, and every sprinkler main is a circuit waiting to be given a second job. They work slowly and in advance, which makes them useless in an ambush and indispensable in a siege. Their invoices are calculated by the square metre and their warranties are worded very carefully."],"features":[{"name":"Site Survey","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with mason's tools and electrician's tools. If you already have proficiency with either, you gain proficiency with one other set of artisan's tools of your choice. You can read structural and utility plans as fluently as if you had drawn them."},{"type":"p","text":"After spending 10 minutes examining a structure, you learn its entrances, its power and water runs, the position of its security systems, and one weakness the builder tried to hide."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Anchors","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You drive wards into surfaces: a chalk line cut with conductive paste, a nail of god-bone through a doorframe. As an action you can place one anchor from the table below on a surface within 5 feet of you. An anchor covers a single 5-foot square or one doorway and lasts for 1 hour, until the surface holding it is destroyed, or until you place another beyond your limit."},{"type":"p","text":"You can have a number of anchors placed at once equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one). Placing another beyond that limit ends the oldest. An anchor's saving throw DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier."},{"type":"table","title":"Anchors","headers":["Anchor","Effect"],"rows":[["Threshold","A creature that enters the square for the first time on a turn must succeed on a Strength saving throw or have its speed reduced to 0 until the end of that turn."],["Bleeder","A creature that ends its turn in the square takes 1d8 lightning damage. The anchor draws this from whatever the wall is wired to."],["Shroud","The square and everything in it is heavily obscured to cameras, sensors, darkvision and thermal sight. Ordinary eyesight is unaffected."],["Brace","A creature standing in the square has half cover and advantage on saving throws against being moved against its will."],["Mute","Sound, radio and network traffic cannot cross the anchor. A creature in the square cannot use comms or open a NET connection."],["Latch","A door, window or hatch in the square is held shut. Forcing it takes an action and a successful Strength check against your anchor DC, which ends the anchor."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Live Circuit","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your anchors draw on the building's own current rather than yours. You can place an anchor as a bonus action, and you can place it on any surface you can see within 30 feet rather than only within 5 feet."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature triggers one of your anchors, you can use your reaction to relocate a different anchor you have placed to any surface within 30 feet of its current position."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Curtain Wall","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Given 10 minutes and a building, you can make it argue. Choose a structure or a contiguous area no more than 100 feet on a side. For the next 8 hours you know the position of every creature inside it that you have not authorised, and each unauthorised creature treats the whole area as difficult terrain."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, while inside an area you have prepared this way, you can use an action to slam it shut. Every door locks, every lift stops, and each creature in the area must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your anchor DC or be restrained by shutters, foam or grasping cable until the end of its next turn. Creatures you authorised succeed automatically."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Keystone","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can place one anchor of a greater kind, and only one. Placing it takes 1 minute. It occupies a 20-foot cube and lasts 8 hours or until you dismiss it as an action. You cannot place another until you finish a long rest. Choose one effect when you place it."},{"type":"ul","items":["Refusal. A creature that tries to enter the cube must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your anchor DC or be unable to enter for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. A creature that succeeds takes 4d8 force damage as it crosses.","Sanctuary. Creatures you choose have three-quarters cover against attacks originating outside the cube, and any creature you choose that starts its turn inside regains 2d6 hit points. A creature can regain hit points this way only once per turn.","Fault. Cyberware, drones, vehicles and constructs inside the cube have disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws, and no creature inside can open a NET connection or activate cyberware that requires an action.","Ownership. Every powered door, camera, lift and turret whose controls sit inside the cube answers to you for the duration. The system's owner cannot override you without physically cutting power to the block."]}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"artificer-salvage-wright","cls":"Artificer","name":"Salvage Wright","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Everything in the kit used to belong to something that lost a fight.","description":["A Salvage Wright works the wreck line: downed drones, burned vehicles, the contents of a security post after the security has left. They can price a machine by the sound it makes hitting the ground. What they build out of it is ugly, specific and temporary, and it is finished before anybody else has finished unpacking."],"features":[{"name":"Wreck Line","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with tinker's tools and smith's tools. If you already have proficiency with either, you gain proficiency with one other set of artisan's tools of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"You carry scrap: an abstract quantity of usable parts. Your maximum is equal to your Intelligence modifier + your proficiency bonus (minimum two), and you begin each day at your maximum. You gain 1 scrap whenever you spend 1 minute stripping a destroyed construct, drone, vehicle or firearm. You regain all spent scrap when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Fabrication","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can spend scrap to assemble something crude and immediate. Choose one fabrication from the table below and pay its cost. A fabrication lasts for 1 minute unless its entry says otherwise, then comes apart."},{"type":"p","text":"A fabrication's saving throw DC and attack modifier use your Intelligence: the DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier."},{"type":"table","title":"Fabrications","headers":["Scrap","Fabrication","Effect"],"rows":[["1","Plate","One creature you touch gains temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier."],["1","Shrike","Hurl a spinning offcut at a creature within 30 feet. Make a ranged attack roll. On a hit the target takes 1d10 slashing damage and its speed drops by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."],["1","Jammer","One creature within 30 feet must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw or be unable to use cyberware, comms or the NET until the end of its next turn."],["2","Snarl","A 10-foot square within 30 feet fills with welded offcuts and becomes difficult terrain until a creature spends an action clearing it."],["2","Hot Cell","A weapon you touch deals an extra 1d6 lightning damage on a hit for the duration."],["3","Spotter","A drone the size of a fist appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet, with AC 13, 1 hit point and a flying speed of 30 feet. As a bonus action you can move it up to its speed and have it either relay what it sees to you or give one creature within 5 feet of it disadvantage on its next attack roll."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cannibalise","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can take parts off things that are still using them. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can rip a component free. The creature takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's type and you gain 1 scrap, up to your maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, whenever you reduce a construct, drone or vehicle to 0 hit points you gain 2 scrap immediately, with no need to spend time stripping it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Life","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 10 minutes you can rebuild a destroyed drone, turret, vehicle or Medium or smaller construct that you have access to. It has hit points equal to five times your artificer level, AC 15, and a walking speed of 30 feet, or a flying speed of 30 feet if it had one in life. It obeys your spoken commands."},{"type":"p","text":"The machine acts on your initiative and takes only the Dodge action unless you use a bonus action to direct it, in which case it can move and take one action. It keeps one attack it had in life, which uses your spell attack modifier and deals 2d6 damage of its original type."},{"type":"p","text":"The rebuild falls apart after 8 hours or when it drops to 0 hit points. You can have only one at a time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Everything Is Parts","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, point at a manufactured object within 60 feet that is no larger than a 10-foot cube and is not being worn or carried. It comes apart, and you gain scrap equal to your proficiency bonus. This scrap can exceed your maximum until you finish a long rest. A magic item, a crewed vehicle, or an object under a creature's control resists if its bearer succeeds on a Constitution saving throw against your fabrication DC."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also do this to a construct or drone as an action by spending 3 scrap. The target must make a Constitution saving throw against your fabrication DC, taking 10d8 force damage on a failure as every fastening in it gives up at once, or half as much on a success. If this reduces it to 0 hit points, you gain 3 scrap from the pile."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"barbarian-path-of-the-coolant-fault","cls":"Barbarian","name":"Path of the Coolant Fault","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Rage is a thermal event. The screaming is just the pressure valve.","description":["Your chrome runs hot and somewhere in the third year you stopped topping up the loop. Now every fight opens with an alarm nobody else can hear and closes with you standing in a cloud of your own steam. Coolant Fault barbarians are easy to find in the dark. They are also easy to identify afterwards, because the floor where they stood is warped."],"features":[{"name":"Thermal Runaway","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are raging, heat comes off you in sheets. At the start of each of your turns, each other creature within 5 feet of you takes fire damage equal to your rage damage bonus. You have resistance to fire damage while raging, and cold weather, rain and immersion no longer impose any penalty on you."},{"type":"p","text":"The loop was not designed for this. Each time a rage of yours ends, you take 1d6 fire damage. This damage cannot be reduced or prevented."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Purge Valve","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can dump the whole loop at once. As a bonus action while raging, you vent. Each creature within 15 feet of you must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier). On a failure a creature takes 3d6 fire damage and is blinded by steam until the end of its turn. On a success it takes half as much damage and is not blinded."},{"type":"p","text":"The area within 15 feet of you is lightly obscured until the start of your next turn. You can vent twice, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Running Hot","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your body has given up on regulating itself and you have decided this is fine. You are immune to fire damage while raging and resistant to it otherwise. Extreme heat never affects you, and you can heat a metal object you are holding until it glows: a creature other than you that touches it, or is hit by it, takes 1d10 fire damage."},{"type":"p","text":"You also see the heat of living things. While raging you have blindsight out to 30 feet, and you can tell whether a creature you can see is augmented and roughly how heavily, by the way its warmth sits wrong on its body."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Meltdown","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action while raging, you can run the loop until it fails. For 1 minute, or until your rage ends, all of the following are true."},{"type":"ul","items":["At the start of each of your turns, each other creature within 15 feet of you takes fire damage equal to twice your rage damage bonus.","Your melee weapon attacks deal an extra 2d6 fire damage on a hit.","A creature that starts its turn within 15 feet of you has disadvantage on ranged attack rolls until the start of its next turn, shooting through the haze."]},{"type":"p","text":"When the effect ends you gain one level of exhaustion. Everything inside your cooling loop is now somewhere else in your body and a surgeon will have opinions."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"barbarian-path-of-the-repossessed","cls":"Barbarian","name":"Path of the Repossessed","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"The arm is not paid for. The arm knows this. The arm has opinions.","description":["There is a lien in your left arm, and in this city a lien is not paperwork. It is a small hungry process with a legal personality, installed by the lender and woken by non-payment. Yours woke up years ago. It fights well, it collects what it is owed, and it has never once been told no in a way it accepted."],"features":[{"name":"Collections","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you rage, the lien takes the wheel and opens an inventory. Choose one creature you can see within 30 feet. It is marked as owing until your rage ends or it drops to 0 hit points. While a creature is marked, all of the following are true."},{"type":"ul","items":["You know which direction it lies in while it is within 60 feet of you, though not its exact position.","You know whether it is carrying more than 500 credits in cash, goods or chrome, and roughly where on its body.","The first time each turn you hit it with a melee weapon attack, it takes extra damage equal to your proficiency bonus.","You have advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made to grapple, shove or drag it."]},{"type":"p","text":"If the marked creature drops to 0 hit points while your rage lasts, you can mark a new creature as a bonus action. You cannot mark a new creature by any other means."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Right of Seizure","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The lien collects in kind. When you reduce a marked creature to 0 hit points, or when you hit one that you are grappling with a melee attack, you can take one thing from it as part of the same attack: a held weapon, a shield, a piece of loose gear, or one visible piece of its cyberware. A conscious creature resists with a Strength or Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier)."},{"type":"p","text":"Cyberware torn out this way is wrecked and non-functional until someone spends an hour and 500 credits on it. The creature it came out of takes 2d8 slashing damage and has disadvantage on its next attack roll."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Compound Interest","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Debt accrues. Each time the marked creature deals damage to you or to an ally you can see, your rage damage bonus against that creature increases by 1, to a maximum increase equal to your proficiency bonus. The increase ends when your rage does."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are raging you cannot be charmed or frightened, and any effect that would move you against your will fails outright if it would carry you further from the marked creature."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Foreclosure","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action while raging, you can call the entire balance due on a creature within 30 feet. It must make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier)."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failure it takes 8d8 force damage, all of its installed cyberware locks out for 1 minute, and it is paralysed until the end of its next turn as its own hardware refuses to carry it. On a success it takes half as much damage and its cyberware locks out only until the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature with no cyberware installed takes the damage and is never paralysed. The lien has nothing to hold on to, and finds this genuinely upsetting."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"barbarian-path-of-the-dead-channel","cls":"Barbarian","name":"Path of the Dead Channel","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Listens to stations that stopped broadcasting before you were born.","description":["There are frequencies nobody uses any more. Emergency bands from a war that ended, a children's programme that ran for eleven years and then did not, the long flat tone a hospital leaves behind. You have an aerial in your skull and you keep it tuned to those. When you rage you stop translating what comes down it, and everyone in earshot has to listen along."],"features":[{"name":"Carrier Wave","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are raging you broadcast. At the start of each of your turns, choose one creature within 30 feet that can hear or that carries a receiver. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier) or take psychic damage equal to your rage damage bonus and have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the start of your next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also hold a conversation with anyone carrying a radio, a comm implant or a working speaker within 1 mile, without equipment of your own. You do not get to choose who else is listening."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dead Air","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action while raging, you can black out a 30-foot-radius sphere centred on yourself for 1 minute. Inside it no radio, comm, smartlink or NET connection functions, and no creature can be heard speaking more than 5 feet away. A creature relying on a smartlink or targeting implant has disadvantage on attack rolls while inside."},{"type":"p","text":"You and any creatures you choose when you use this feature can still hear you, because you are the only signal left in the area. You can do this twice, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Numbers Station","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have listened long enough to hear things slightly before they are said. While raging you cannot be surprised, you have advantage on initiative rolls, and attack rolls against you do not gain advantage from the attacker being unseen."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also tune to a person instead of a place. As an action, name a creature you have met and spend 10 minutes listening for it. You learn its rough distance and direction from you, whether it is awake, and the last thing it said aloud, provided it is on the same continent. You learn nothing about who it is with. You can do this once, and again when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Test Pattern","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action while raging, you can open every channel at once. Each creature of your choice within 60 feet must make a Wisdom saving throw against your broadcast DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failure a creature takes 6d8 psychic damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn, listening to eleven years of a programme it half remembers. On a success it takes half as much damage and is not incapacitated. A creature with no hearing, no comms and no chrome is unaffected, having nothing in it that receives."},{"type":"p","text":"For the next minute, every creature that failed the save has disadvantage on saving throws against your Carrier Wave."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"barbarian-path-of-the-unwired","cls":"Barbarian","name":"Path of the Unwired","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"No chrome, no jack, nothing in you that anybody else can reach.","description":["You have never had anything installed and you do not intend to. This is not a philosophy, or not only one. It is a practical read on a city where everything with a chip in it eventually answers to someone who is not you. When the lights go out and every augmented body in the room locks up mid-stride, you are still moving, and you are the only one who is."],"features":[{"name":"Nothing to Hack","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The features of this path function only while you have no cyberware and no augments installed. If you install any, you lose the benefits of every feature of this path until it is removed."},{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to any effect that targets, disables, overloads or reads cyberware. You cannot be located, traced or identified by any sensor, network, record system or divination that works through technology, and automated targeting systems cannot gain advantage on attack rolls against you."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are raging, you have advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. You can also use your reaction to reduce the damage of an attack made against you by a drone, turret, construct or any creature shooting through a smartlink by 1d12 + your Constitution modifier. Nothing automated gets a clean read on you."},{"type":"p","text":"You can reduce damage this way a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Analogue","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You kept the senses everyone else replaced and they have had a lifetime of practice. You gain proficiency in Insight and Perception. If you are already proficient in either, your proficiency bonus is doubled for any check you make with it."},{"type":"p","text":"You can tell at a glance roughly how much cyberware a creature you can see is carrying and where the seams are. While raging, the first time each turn you hit a creature that has cyberware installed with a melee weapon attack, it takes extra damage equal to your proficiency bonus and cannot activate cyberware that requires an action or bonus action until the end of its next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Intact","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Humanity has never been spent and it holds you together. You have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened or possessed, and you are immune to any effect that would read or alter your memories."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also lend your baseline out. As an action, touch a willing creature. For the next hour it is treated as being one Humanity state higher than its current state, to a maximum of Baseline. You can do this a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Unowned","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Nothing in this city has a handle on you. You are immune to being charmed, frightened or possessed, and you cannot be magically or technologically compelled to act against your will."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can drop to 1 hit point instead and immediately enter a rage without expending a use of Rage. Until that rage ends, every creature within 30 feet of you that has cyberware installed has disadvantage on attack rolls against you. Their targeting insists you are not there and they have spent too long trusting it."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bard-college-of-the-hijacked-marquee","cls":"Bard","name":"College of the Hijacked Marquee","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Takes over the advertising and performs inside it until somebody pays to make it stop.","description":["Every wall above the fourth floor is rented. This college treats that rented space as a stage and the street below as an audience that did not choose to be one. They cut into a hoarding, replace ninety seconds of skin-cream campaign with something of their own, and are off the scaffold before the agency's response team arrives. The good ones get paid twice: once by whoever wanted the message up, once by whoever wants it down."],"features":[{"name":"Cut-In","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with hacking tools and with one skill of your choice from Deception, Performance and Technology. As an action you can splice yourself into any powered display, speaker, hoarding or public feed within 60 feet, holding it for up to 10 minutes. Its owner notices after 1d6 minutes."},{"type":"p","text":"While you hold a display you can put anything on it that you can imagine, including a convincing likeness of a person you have seen. A creature that studies the display and succeeds on an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC recognises the forgery for what it is."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Audience Capture","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When your screens run, people look. As an action, expend one use of Bardic Inspiration to run a cut-in on a display, speaker or comm channel within 60 feet. Choose a number of creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum one) within 60 feet that can see or hear it. Each must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or suffer one effect of your choice, chosen when you use this feature and applied to all of them."},{"type":"ul","items":["Spotlight. The creature is charmed by you until the end of your next turn, and must spend its movement on its turn moving toward the display.","Static Buy. The creature has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn.","Call to Action. The creature is frightened of a creature of your choice, other than itself, until the end of its next turn."]},{"type":"p","text":"A creature that cannot perceive the cut-in succeeds automatically."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Screen","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can run two things at once. When you use Audience Capture, you can pick two effects from its list rather than one and decide which applies to each creature as it fails its save."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, while you are holding a display with Cut-In, you can use that display as the origin point of any spell you cast that has a range of 30 feet or more. The spell emanates from the display rather than from you, and no creature can work out where you are standing from the spell alone."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Prime Time","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can seize every screen and speaker within 1 mile and put yourself on all of them. The broadcast lasts 1 minute and cannot be cut without physically killing power to the district."},{"type":"p","text":"Choose any number of creatures within 1 mile that can see or hear it, to a maximum of ten times your bard level. Each must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC or be charmed by you for the duration, carrying out any simple instruction you give through the broadcast that is not obviously self-destructive. A charmed creature repeats the save if you or your allies harm it, and at the end of each of its turns if the instruction plainly runs against its interests."},{"type":"p","text":"Everything you say during that minute is recorded by somebody. Assume it will be played back at your trial."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bard-college-of-the-quarterly-rite","cls":"Bard","name":"College of the Quarterly Rite","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Corporate liturgy. The hymns are earnings figures and the choir is on salary.","description":["Some megacorps stopped pretending they were only companies. They keep a chapel on the executive floor, a feast day for the founding, and a choir on payroll to sing the quarterly numbers. You trained in that choir. Whether you still draw the salary or left with the hymnal under your coat, you know exactly what a room does when somebody reads figures aloud in the correct cadence."],"features":[{"name":"Liturgy","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in Religion and Persuasion. If you are already proficient in either, choose another skill. You can perform the observances of any corporation whose chapel you have entered well enough to pass as staff to anyone below director grade."},{"type":"p","text":"You always know the correct form of address, the current quarter's slogan, and which saint a given company has most recently invented."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Allocations","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You do not hand out inspiration. You allocate it. When you give a creature a Bardic Inspiration die, name one term from the table below. The creature holds the die and the term together until the die is spent or until you finish a long rest. As normal, a creature can hold only one of your dice at a time."},{"type":"table","title":"Terms","headers":["Term","Effect"],"rows":[["Hazard Pay","When the creature spends the die, it also gains temporary hit points equal to the number rolled plus your Charisma modifier."],["Performance Clause","The creature can spend the die to add the number rolled to a damage roll, and can decide to do so after the attack hits."],["Indemnity","When the creature would fail a saving throw, it can spend the die and add the number rolled. If the save still fails, the die is not expended."],["Severance","When the creature drops to 0 hit points, the die is spent automatically and the creature regains hit points equal to the number rolled plus your bard level."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Audit","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You read people the way you read a balance sheet. As an action, choose a creature you can see within 60 feet. It must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC or be audited for 1 hour. When a creature is audited, you learn three of the following about it, chosen by you: its damage resistances and immunities, its saving throw modifiers, its lowest ability score, the thing it most wants, the thing it most fears, or who it currently owes."},{"type":"p","text":"While a creature is audited, you have advantage on Charisma checks made against it and it has disadvantage on saving throws against your spells. You can have only one creature audited at a time."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Going Concern","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A creature holding one of your Bardic Inspiration dice has advantage on death saving throws. The paperwork has already been filed and it would be untidy to die now."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once per long rest you can use an action to declare a creature within 60 feet to be operating at a loss. It must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC or suffer all of the following for 1 minute."},{"type":"ul","items":["It has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.","Its installed cyberware runs at half effect, and it cannot activate cyberware that requires an action.","It cannot regain hit points."]},{"type":"p","text":"The creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bard-college-of-the-warm-call","cls":"Bard","name":"College of the Warm Call","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Does the entire job by voice, from a desk three districts away.","description":["Nothing gets you through a locked door faster than sounding like you belong on the other side of it. This college trains for the phone: pacing, background noise, the specific weary friendliness of somebody in facilities who has been on shift too long. Its members rarely attend the jobs they make possible. They are at a desk with a cup of something, being believed."],"features":[{"name":"Script","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in Deception and Insight. If you are already proficient in either, choose another skill. You can imitate any voice you have heard for at least a minute, including its accent, its comm compression and the room it was standing in. A creature that suspects a trick can catch it with a Wisdom (Insight) check against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also place a call to any comm, terminal or implant whose owner you can name, without knowing the address. The connection holds as long as the other party stays on the line."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pretext","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, expend one use of Bardic Inspiration and speak to a creature that can hear you, in person or over any connection. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or accept, for the next 10 minutes, that you are someone it has a reason to cooperate with: a colleague, a supervisor's assistant, the contractor it was told to expect."},{"type":"p","text":"While the pretext holds, the creature answers routine questions truthfully, follows instructions that fall inside its ordinary duties, and does not report the contact. It ends early if you ask for something clearly outside that creature's job, if you or your allies harm it, or if somebody it trusts more contradicts you."},{"type":"p","text":"You can have a number of pretexts running at once equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum one). A creature that succeeds on the save cannot be affected by this feature again for 24 hours."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Callback","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can reach anyone you have once had on the line. Choose a creature you have spoken to within the last 30 days. You can speak into its ear from any distance and it hears you as though you were standing beside it. It can answer, and the exchange lasts up to 1 minute. The creature needs no comm, implant or handset, and you have stopped trying to explain how this works."},{"type":"p","text":"During a callback you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration to press. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or answer one question truthfully and to the best of its knowledge, then forget that it was asked."},{"type":"p","text":"You can press a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"All Lines","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can call a building. Choose a structure, vessel, vehicle or installation that you can see or have been inside. Every creature in it that can hear or receive a signal must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failure, a creature believes for the next 10 minutes that it has received legitimate instructions from somebody it answers to. You specify one instruction of up to a sentence when you use this feature: evacuate, stand down, report to the loading bay, ignore the alarm in sector four. A creature follows it as it would any ordinary order, and repeats the save if the instruction would obviously get it killed or if it sees you doing something incompatible with the story."},{"type":"p","text":"Creatures that succeed know only that the call was strange. Whether they mention it is a question of how much they like their employer."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bard-college-of-the-blown-speaker","cls":"Bard","name":"College of the Blown Speaker","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Plays loud enough that the front row needs a clinic, and calls that the set.","description":["The rig is four stacks of salvaged drivers wired past their rating and a coil that was never meant to carry a voice. It is not music in any sense a licensing board recognises. It moves furniture, it sets off car alarms two streets over, and it makes people's teeth hurt in a specific way they come back for. Members of this college go deaf on a schedule and have it fixed on a schedule."],"features":[{"name":"The Rig","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with tinker's tools and with one musical instrument of your choice, which must be amplified. Your rig counts as that instrument for every feature of this class. Rebuilding a destroyed rig takes 8 hours and 500 credits of parts."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are holding your rig you have advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks made for a crowd of ten or more, and you can be heard clearly at up to half a mile. You are immune to the deafened condition, having nothing left to lose."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pressure Wave","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, expend one use of Bardic Inspiration and play something the drivers will not survive. Each creature of your choice in a 15-foot cone, or in a 10-foot-radius sphere centred on you, must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failure a creature takes thunder damage equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier and is pushed 10 feet away from you. On a success it takes half as much damage and is not pushed. A creature that fails and carries an auditory implant, a comm or a smartlink is also deafened until the end of its next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Standing Wave","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can hold a note in a space until the space gives up. As an action, begin a standing wave in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within 60 feet. It lasts for 1 minute while you maintain concentration, as though concentrating on a spell."},{"type":"p","text":"The area is lightly obscured by dust and shaking air. A creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn, or starts its turn there, must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or take 2d8 thunder damage and have disadvantage on ranged attack rolls until the start of its next turn. Glass, screens and unattended objects in the area crack and fail."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Blow the Room","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can run everything you have into a single note. Each creature of your choice within 60 feet must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failure a creature takes 10d8 thunder damage, is knocked prone, and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a success it takes half as much damage and is neither prone nor stunned. A creature that fails by 5 or more has any cyberware that processes sound destroyed outright, and will need it replaced."},{"type":"p","text":"Every unsecured object, window and screen within 60 feet shatters, and whatever structure you are standing in takes damage at the DM's discretion. Your rig is destroyed. You knew that when you started."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"cleric-grid-domain","cls":"Cleric","name":"Grid Domain","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Keeps the lights on, and decides whose lights those are.","description":["Every substation has a chaplain, because every substation has a load schedule and somebody has to decide which block goes dark at three in the morning. Grid clergy bless transformers, walk the cable runs with a censer in one hand and a multimeter in the other, and file the outage reports afterwards. Theirs is the only priesthood in the city whose prayers have a measurable output in kilowatts. Most of them have burn scars on both hands and consider this normal."],"features":[{"name":"Grid Domain Spells","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed. Domain spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Grid Domain Spells","headers":["Cleric Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","witch bolt, thunderwave"],["3rd","hold person, shatter"],["5th","lightning bolt, sending"],["7th","blight, wall of fire"],["9th","flame strike, hold monster"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ballast","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with heavy armor and with electrician's tools. You also carry a standing charge in your holy symbol, and it leaks."},{"type":"p","text":"Whenever you deal lightning or thunder damage to a creature with a spell, that creature's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Channel Divinity: Brownout","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to pull the current out of a room."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you present your holy symbol and drain a 30-foot cube centered on a point you can see within 60 feet. Every unattended powered device in the area goes inert until the end of your next turn: lamps, cameras, locks, drones, cash terminals. Each creature in the area must then make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC, and a creature with any cyberware installed makes this save with disadvantage."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 lightning damage and can't take reactions until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect. The damage increases to 3d8 at 8th level, 4d8 at 12th level, and 5d8 at 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bus Tie","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, you learn to route power rather than spend it all in one place. When you deal lightning or thunder damage to a creature with a cleric spell, you can choose up to three creatures you can see within 30 feet of you."},{"type":"p","text":"Each chosen creature gains temporary hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier plus the level of the spell, or equal to your Wisdom modifier alone if the spell was a cantrip. Until the end of your next turn, each chosen creature's weapon attacks also deal an extra 1d6 lightning damage."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Earthing Strike","level":8,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 8th level, you can discharge your holy symbol down the length of a weapon. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d8 lightning damage."},{"type":"p","text":"If the target is wearing metal armor, carrying a metal shield, or has any cyberware installed, the extra damage is 1d8 plus your proficiency bonus instead, and the target can't take reactions until the start of its next turn. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Substation","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 17th level, you can stand somewhere and make it a supply point. As an action, you consecrate a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on yourself. The sphere moves with you and lasts for 1 minute. It requires no concentration, and it ends early if you are incapacitated or die."},{"type":"ul","items":["You and creatures of your choice in the sphere have resistance to lightning damage, and your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d8 lightning damage.","A creature of your choice in the sphere that has any cyberware installed has disadvantage on Constitution saving throws.","At the start of each of your turns, you can direct an arc at one creature you can see in the sphere. That creature must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 6d8 lightning damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful one."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"cleric-absolution-domain","cls":"Cleric","name":"Absolution Domain","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Sells forgiveness as a monthly subscription, and carries the balance personally.","description":["The Absolution church is a public company with a share price and a customer service tier. You confess into a terminal, a priest countersigns the release, and the record clears on the next billing cycle. What the advertising leaves out is where the debt goes: into the priest, who wears it as bruises that arrive without a cause. Absolution clergy are easy to pick out at a distance, because they move like people who have already been hit today."],"features":[{"name":"Absolution Domain Spells","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed. Domain spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Absolution Domain Spells","headers":["Cleric Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","bless, sanctuary"],["3rd","calm emotions, lesser restoration"],["5th","beacon of hope, remove curse"],["7th","death ward, freedom of movement"],["9th","greater restoration, hallow"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grace Period","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in the Insight skill. You also learn to extend a client a little time at your own expense."},{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see within 30 feet fails a saving throw, you can use your reaction to forgive the failure. That creature rerolls the saving throw and must use the new result. You then take 1d4 psychic damage, which can't be reduced or prevented."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Channel Divinity: Indemnity","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to underwrite someone."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you choose a creature you can see within 30 feet, which can be yourself, and underwrite it for 1 minute. The first time that creature takes damage before the effect ends, the damage is reduced to 0 and the effect ends. You then take damage equal to half the amount prevented, to a maximum of twice your cleric level. This damage can't be reduced or prevented."},{"type":"p","text":"The effect also ends early if you are incapacitated, in which case nobody is covered and nobody is refunded."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Collections","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, the church stops absorbing its own losses. Whenever you take damage from an Absolution Domain feature, choose one creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature takes necrotic damage equal to the damage you took."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature can be affected by this feature only once per turn. The feature does not require the creature to have had anything to do with the original injury, and the liturgy is explicit that this is not an oversight."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Penitent Strike","level":8,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 8th level, you can make a weapon attack collect on somebody's behalf. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d8 radiant damage."},{"type":"p","text":"If you have taken damage from one of your Absolution Domain features since the start of your last turn, the extra damage is 2d8 instead. When you reach 14th level, these amounts increase to 2d8 and 3d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Jubilee","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 17th level, you can clear every account in reach at once. As an action, choose up to six creatures you can see within 60 feet. Each chosen creature regains hit points equal to 4d8 plus your cleric level, and one condition of your choice currently affecting it ends."},{"type":"p","text":"You then take necrotic damage equal to 10 times the number of creatures you chose. This damage can't be reduced or prevented, and Collections applies to it in full. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"cleric-reliquary-domain","cls":"Cleric","name":"Reliquary Domain","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Certifies that the bone in your spine came off a god and that the paperwork is clean.","description":["Gods die, and the bodies are an asset class. Reliquary clergy hold the licences that let a foundry quarry a divine femur, and they stand on the cutting floor with a calibrated saw and the correct prayers written on a laminated card. The work is half sacrament and half quality control. A Reliquary priest can tell you which vertebra your spinal strut was cut from, and will, at length, without being asked."],"features":[{"name":"Reliquary Domain Spells","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed. Domain spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Reliquary Domain Spells","headers":["Cleric Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","identify, shield of faith"],["3rd","magic weapon, warding bond"],["5th","glyph of warding, speak with dead"],["7th","fabricate, stone shape"],["9th","animate objects, legend lore"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Seated Fragment","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with tinker's tools, and you carry a working reliquary: a socketed case holding a chip of something that used to be divine."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can seat the fragment in a weapon, a shield, or a piece of cyberware you touch. It stays seated until you seat it somewhere else. While it is seated, that object counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage, and the creature carrying the object has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also spend 10 minutes handling a corpse or a piece of cyberware to learn where it came from, how it was made, and whether it still works."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Channel Divinity: The Bone Objects","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to remind dead material what it used to be."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you present your holy symbol. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you that has cyberware installed, is wearing metal armor, or is a construct must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 radiant damage, has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn, and during that time can't use any attack, movement or feature granted by cyberware or by a construct chassis. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect. The damage increases to 3d8 at 8th level and 4d8 at 14th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Interment","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, you can keep more than one fragment in play. You can have a number of objects seated with fragments at once equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of one)."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature carrying one of your seated objects fails a saving throw, it can use its reaction to spend the fragment. The saving throw succeeds instead, and that fragment burns out. You can replace a burned-out fragment when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grave Goods","level":8,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d8 necrotic damage."},{"type":"p","text":"If one of your fragments is seated in that weapon, the extra damage is radiant instead, and you regain hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of 1). When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Open the Reliquary","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 17th level, you can break every fragment you carry at once and spend what is inside. As an action, you shatter all of your seated fragments. For 1 minute, you and every creature carrying one of the shattered objects gains the following benefits."},{"type":"ul","items":["Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage.","Its weapon attacks deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage.","It can't be charmed, frightened or paralyzed, and it has advantage on death saving throws."]},{"type":"p","text":"When the minute ends, each affected creature takes 4d6 necrotic damage as the dead thing takes back what it lent. You have no fragments and can seat none until you finish a long rest, and you can't use this feature again until you do."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"cleric-static-domain","cls":"Cleric","name":"Static Domain","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Listens to the dead channels, and can put an entire room onto one.","description":["Every network leaves gaps: frequencies nobody bought, bands the licensing office forgot, the hiss between one station and the next. Static clergy hold that the gaps are occupied, and they spend a great deal of time in basements with old receivers, taking dictation. Their liturgy is a tuning procedure. Their miracles mostly consist of making something impossible to hear, find or prove."],"features":[{"name":"Static Domain Spells","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed. Domain spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Static Domain Spells","headers":["Cleric Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","bane, dissonant whispers"],["3rd","blur, silence"],["5th","hypnotic pattern, nondetection"],["7th","confusion, phantasmal killer"],["9th","mislead, modify memory"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dead Air","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in the Stealth skill and with electrician's tools."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can fill a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on yourself with interference for 1 minute. The sphere moves with you. While it lasts, no creature inside it can communicate with anything outside it by radio, comm implant, or any spell that carries a message, and a creature that ends its turn inside the sphere has disadvantage on the next Wisdom (Perception) check it makes before the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Channel Divinity: Carrier Wave","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to put the noise directly into people."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you present your holy symbol and broadcast in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d6 psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn it can't speak, can't cast a spell with a verbal component, and can't maintain concentration. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."},{"type":"p","text":"The damage increases to 3d6 at 8th level and 5d6 at 14th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Squelch","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, when a creature you can see within 60 feet takes a reaction, you can use your reaction to jam it. The creature's reaction is wasted and produces no effect, and it can't take reactions again until the end of its next turn. If the wasted reaction was the casting of a spell, the spell slot is spent all the same."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Noise Floor","level":8,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d8 psychic damage, and the target can't speak or otherwise communicate until the start of your next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"If the target is concentrating on a spell, it has disadvantage on the saving throw it makes to maintain concentration against this damage. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Dead Channel","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 17th level, as an action, you can drop a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you can see within 120 feet onto a frequency nobody uses. The sphere lasts 1 minute."},{"type":"ul","items":["No creature inside the sphere can communicate with anything outside it by any means, mundane or magical.","Divination spells, scrying sensors and remote sensors originating outside the sphere cannot perceive anything within it, and nothing inside it appears on any recording.","Teleportation and planar travel into or out of the sphere automatically fail.","Each creature of your choice that starts its turn inside the sphere must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or take 4d8 psychic damage and be unable to cast spells with verbal components until the start of its next turn."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"druid-circle-of-the-ledge","cls":"Druid","name":"Circle of the Ledge","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Works the roofline, and knows every bird up there by the sound of its landing.","description":["The city grew a second ground floor about forty storeys up, and things moved into it. Ledge druids work that level: the gull colonies in the cooling towers, the dog packs that live entirely on catwalks, the crows that have learned which vending machines short out when kicked. They travel by gutter, cable run and fire escape, and they file nuisance complaints against anyone who nets a roost. Most of them are missing at least one fingernail."],"features":[{"name":"Circle of the Ledge Spells","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain circle spells at the druid levels listed. Circle spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Circle of the Ledge Spells","headers":["Druid Level","Spells"],"rows":[["2nd","feather fall, longstrider"],["3rd","pass without trace, spider climb"],["5th","fly, wind wall"],["7th","freedom of movement, locate creature"],["9th","commune with nature, scrying"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Kept Flock","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in the Animal Handling skill. Something also follows you now: a loose flock of pigeons, crows, gulls and worse, which roosts wherever you sleep and belongs to you in no legal sense whatsoever."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can put the flock on a creature you can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC or take 1d6 piercing damage and have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the start of your next turn. The damage increases to 2d6 at 6th level, 3d6 at 10th level and 4d6 at 14th level."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Gutterline","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, you move the way your flock does. You gain a climbing speed equal to your walking speed, and you can cross vertical surfaces, cables and ledges without making an ability check."},{"type":"p","text":"When you fall, you can use your reaction to have the flock take your weight. Reduce the falling damage by 5 times your druid level, and you land on your feet."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are at least 20 feet above the ground and in open air, you have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Mobbing","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, the flock learns to work a crowd. When you use Kept Flock, you can target each creature of your choice in a 15-foot cube you can see within 60 feet instead of a single creature. Each target makes its own saving throw."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a creature that fails a saving throw against Kept Flock has its speed halved until the start of your next turn, and until then it can't see anything more than 10 feet away from it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Whole Roofline","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 14th level, you can call in everything the city feeds. As an action, you fill a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you can see within 120 feet with birds, rats, dogs and whatever else turns up. The sphere lasts for 1 minute, requires no concentration, and ends early if you are incapacitated. At the start of each of your turns, you can move it up to 20 feet in a direction of your choice."},{"type":"ul","items":["The sphere is heavily obscured for every creature except you and creatures of your choice.","A creature that enters the sphere for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 4d6 piercing damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.","Ranged attack rolls made into or through the sphere have disadvantage."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 5th level or higher to use it again."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"druid-circle-of-the-outfall","cls":"Druid","name":"Circle of the Outfall","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Tends the reed beds that drink solvent, and knows to three decimals what the pipe puts out.","description":["Every process has an outfall, and something always moves in downstream of it. Outfall druids keep the discharge ponds: the reeds bred to metabolise solvent, the eels that have made their peace with cadmium, the algal mats that bloom only on warm waste water. They take samples, adjust the plantings, and file with the water board on the first of the month. They also know exactly what dose of what will stop a human heart, and they are not shy about the number."],"features":[{"name":"Circle of the Outfall Spells","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain circle spells at the druid levels listed. Circle spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Circle of the Outfall Spells","headers":["Druid Level","Spells"],"rows":[["2nd","inflict wounds, ray of sickness"],["3rd","protection from poison, ray of enfeeblement"],["5th","stinking cloud, vampiric touch"],["7th","blight, confusion"],["9th","cloudkill, contagion"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dose","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with the poisoner's kit and with alchemist's supplies. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and against disease, and you are immune to the poison damage of your own features. You also carry a working sample of the outfall in a sealed flask, and you stopped being careful with it some time ago."},{"type":"p","text":"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, or when you deal damage to a creature with a druid spell, you can dose it. That creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or take 1d8 poison damage and have disadvantage on the next ability check it makes before the end of its next turn. The damage increases to 2d8 at 6th level, 3d8 at 10th level and 4d8 at 14th level."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bioaccumulation","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, the dose builds up in whatever it lands in. When a creature fails a saving throw against your Dose feature, it gains one residue, to a maximum of five. Residues last until the creature finishes a short or long rest, or until it benefits from a lesser restoration spell or a day of clinical treatment."},{"type":"p","text":"Whenever a creature takes poison damage from you or from one of your spells, it takes extra poison damage equal to the number of residues it is carrying. A creature carrying three or more residues is poisoned."},{"type":"p","text":"You can tell at a glance how many residues a creature within 30 feet is carrying, which is a social liability at parties."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sump","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, you can put a dose in the ground instead of in a person. As an action, you contaminate a 15-foot-radius, 10-foot-high cylinder centered on a point you can see within 60 feet. The area is difficult terrain and lasts for 1 minute. It requires no concentration, and it ends early if you are incapacitated."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, it takes 3d8 poison damage and gains one residue. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and gains no residue."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Open the Valve","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 14th level, you are immune to poison damage and can't be poisoned. You can also empty everything you are carrying at once."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 8d8 poison damage, gains two residues and is poisoned for 1 minute. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage, gains one residue and isn't poisoned."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature poisoned this way repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that was already carrying five residues when it failed its first saving throw is also incapacitated for as long as the poisoning lasts."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"druid-circle-of-the-understack","cls":"Druid","name":"Circle of the Understack","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Farms the mats that grow warm under a server floor, and reads the network by taste.","description":["Data halls run hot, and something always grows in the warm. Understack druids keep the mycelial mats that spread under raised flooring and along cable trays, feeding them condensate and dead batteries and pulling them back when they get into the fibre. A mature mat is a slow, distributed, extremely literal mind, and it remembers everything that has walked on it. Its keepers tend to answer questions about eleven seconds late."],"features":[{"name":"Circle of the Understack Spells","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain circle spells at the druid levels listed. Circle spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Circle of the Understack Spells","headers":["Druid Level","Spells"],"rows":[["2nd","comprehend languages, detect poison and disease"],["3rd","detect thoughts, web"],["5th","clairvoyance, sending"],["7th","arcane eye, black tentacles"],["9th","legend lore, telepathic bond"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Substrate","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency in the Investigation skill. You also carry a starter culture in a sealed tray, which you feed on condensate and whatever else is going."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can press a handful of the culture onto a surface you touch. Over the next minute it spreads to cover a 20-foot radius, and it lasts for 8 hours or until you plant another. You can have one mat planted at a time."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are within 1 mile of a planted mat and on the same plane of existence, you know the location of every creature standing on it, and you can use an action to see and hear from any point on the mat as though you were standing there, until the start of your next turn. A creature hidden from divination magic is hidden from the mat too."},{"type":"p","text":"The mat is difficult terrain for creatures of your choice, and you always know which way a creature left it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hyphal Link","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, you can tie other people into the mat. When you finish a short or long rest, you can link a number of willing creatures equal to your Wisdom modifier, including yourself, that spent that rest in contact with one of your mats. The link lasts 8 hours or until you create another."},{"type":"p","text":"Linked creatures can speak to one another telepathically while within 1 mile of each other, whether or not they share a language, and each of them knows whether the others are conscious."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a linked creature you can sense fails a saving throw, you can use your reaction to feed it the answer. It rerolls the saving throw and must use the new result. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Fruiting Body","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, you can have two mats planted at once, and you can make one do something sudden. As a bonus action, choose a point on a mat that you can see or sense. Each creature of your choice within 10 feet of that point must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 4d6 poison damage and is blinded until the end of its next turn as the mat fruits into its face. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't blinded."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Slow Mind","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 14th level, your oldest mat has been running long enough to have opinions. You can have three mats planted at once, each covering a 60-foot radius, and a planted mat lasts until you plant another in its place."},{"type":"ul","items":["While you are standing on one of your mats, you can't be surprised, and you have advantage on initiative rolls and on Wisdom saving throws.","While you are standing on one of your mats, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to 3d8 plus your Wisdom modifier. Once you do so, you can't do it again until you finish a short or long rest.","You can use an action to ask a mat one question about anything that happened on it, or within 60 feet of it, in the last thirty days. The answer arrives a minute later and is truthful. The mat has no sense of time and describes people by weight and gait. Once you ask a question this way, you can't ask another until you finish a long rest."]},{"type":"p","text":"Killing a mat takes fire, industrial solvent or a week of dedicated cleaning, and it makes an enemy of everyone downstream of it."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"druid-circle-of-the-heat-island","cls":"Druid","name":"Circle of the Heat Island","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Forecasts the weather the city makes for itself, and then leans on it.","description":["A city this size runs about four degrees hotter than the land underneath it, and the heat has to go somewhere. Heat Island druids read the result: the thermals off black roofs, the downdraft that scours the plaza at the foot of every tower, the fog that sits on the freight yards until nine. They keep instruments on other people's buildings and trade readings with the port authority. Give one of them twenty minutes and a rooftop and they will tell you which way a fire is going to run."],"features":[{"name":"Circle of the Heat Island Spells","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain circle spells at the druid levels listed. Circle spells are always prepared, and they don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day."},{"type":"table","title":"Circle of the Heat Island Spells","headers":["Druid Level","Spells"],"rows":[["2nd","burning hands, fog cloud"],["3rd","gust of wind, scorching ray"],["5th","lightning bolt, sleet storm"],["7th","fire shield, ice storm"],["9th","cloudkill, cone of cold"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Microclimate","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with navigator's tools. By spending a minute in the open air, you can also predict the weather within 5 miles for the next 24 hours, which is more than the forecast services manage."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can move the air in a 15-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you can see within 60 feet. Choose one of the following effects. It lasts until the start of your next turn."},{"type":"ul","items":["Downdraft. Each creature of your choice in the area must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC or be knocked prone. A flying creature that fails descends 20 feet.","Thermal. Each creature of your choice in the area gains a flying speed of 20 feet and takes no damage from falling.","Haze. The area is lightly obscured, and ranged attack rolls made into or through it have disadvantage."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Inversion Layer","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 6th level, the air immediately around you stays yours. You have resistance to fire damage and to cold damage, and you and creatures of your choice within 10 feet of you ignore the effects of extreme heat, extreme cold, heavy precipitation and strong wind."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature you can see within 60 feet makes a ranged weapon attack against you or against a creature within 10 feet of you, you can use your reaction to put a gust across the line. The attacker has disadvantage on the attack roll. You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Convective Cell","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, you can build a weather cell over one block. As an action, you create a 15-foot-radius, 40-foot-high cylinder centered on a point you can see within 120 feet. It lasts for 1 minute, requires no concentration, and ends early if you are incapacitated."},{"type":"p","text":"The area is difficult terrain, and creatures in it have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing. At the start of each of your turns, choose heat or cold. Until the start of your next turn, a creature of your choice that enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, the creature takes 2d8 fire damage if you chose heat, or 2d8 cold damage if you chose cold. A creature that fails against cold also has its speed halved until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Weather Event","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 14th level, you can commit the local air to a decision the forecast services will spend a week explaining. As an action, choose heat, cold or wind, and choose whether precipitation comes with it. The weather changes to match within 1 mile of you over the next 10 minutes and holds for 1 hour."},{"type":"p","text":"For the duration, you and creatures of your choice are unaffected by it. Every other creature in the open air treats the area as difficult terrain, has disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight, and has disadvantage on ranged weapon attack rolls."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns for the duration, you can use a bonus action to bring a piece of the weather down on one creature in the open air that you can see within 120 feet. That creature must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 4d8 fire, cold or lightning damage of your choice on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature indoors or under total cover can't be targeted this way."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fighter-right-of-entry","cls":"Fighter","name":"Right of Entry","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Opens doors for a living, and has never once been asked to open one quietly.","description":["Somebody has to go first. Right of Entry fighters do the door: they read the frame, place the charge or set the ram, and step into whatever is on the other side before it has finished standing up. The work is repetitive, extremely loud, and unusually well paid, because the people who do it properly are the ones who go home. They talk about rooms the way other people talk about weather."],"features":[{"name":"Breach Drill","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with tinker's tools and in the Investigation skill. You also learn to read an entrance. After studying a door, hatch, grate, window or section of wall for 1 minute, you know its material and thickness, whether it is locked, alarmed or warded, and what it would take to get through it."},{"type":"p","text":"You carry breaching charges. As an action, you can place a charge on a barrier within reach and fire it. A barrier that isn't magically reinforced is destroyed, and each creature within 10 feet of the far side must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 thunder damage and is deafened until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't deafened. The damage increases to 3d8 at 10th level and 4d8 at 18th level."},{"type":"p","text":"This save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack after moving through a door, window, breach or other opening since the start of that turn, the attack deals an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's type."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Funnel","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 7th level, you know exactly how dangerous a doorway is, having spent your career standing in one. You have advantage on saving throws against effects created by traps and explosions, and you take no damage from your own breaching charges."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are standing in a doorway, breach, hatch or corridor no more than 10 feet wide, you have half cover, your speed can't be reduced, and a creature that tries to move through your space must succeed on a Strength (Athletics) check contested by your Strength (Athletics) check or have its movement stop."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature you can see enters a door, window, breach or other opening within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to make one melee weapon attack against it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Next Room","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, the extra damage from Breach Drill increases to 2d8, and it applies to ranged weapon attacks as well as melee ones."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns, when you reduce a creature to 0 hit points or score a critical hit with a weapon attack, you can immediately move up to half your speed without provoking opportunity attacks and make one weapon attack as part of the same turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Overpressure","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 15th level, you stop needing a door to put a charge on. As a bonus action, you can detonate a charge from your Breach Drill feature at a point you can see within 30 feet rather than placing it on a barrier. Each creature within 10 feet of that point makes the saving throw as normal."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature that fails a saving throw against one of your charges is also knocked prone and can't take reactions until the end of its next turn. A creature with any cyberware installed makes the saving throw with disadvantage."},{"type":"p","text":"You now regain all expended uses of Breach Drill when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Room Clearance","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, you no longer roll to get through anything you can put your hands on. Given ten minutes and no interruptions, you are through it, whatever it is."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also take a whole room in one pass. As an action, you move up to twice your speed without provoking opportunity attacks and make one melee weapon attack against each creature of your choice that you come within 5 feet of during that movement, to a maximum of six creatures. You can attack each creature only once, and each of these attacks that hits deals an extra 2d8 damage of the weapon's type."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fighter-close-protection","cls":"Fighter","name":"Close Protection","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Paid to stand between a vice president and the consequences of their own memos.","description":["Executive protection is a service line with a rate card. A Close Protection specialist walks the route the day before, checks the lobby footage against the staff roster, and then spends the rest of the contract standing at a precise angle to one particular person. The job is nine tenths boredom. The other tenth is a short, loud sequence they have rehearsed several hundred times. They are never off the clock and they never sit with their back to a door."],"features":[{"name":"Detail","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency in the Insight skill and with one type of vehicle. You also learn to work a route. After 10 minutes studying a building, street or venue, you know its exits, its blind spots and the two places an attack is most likely to come from."},{"type":"p","text":"When you finish a short or long rest, you can name one willing creature you can see as your principal. You can have only one principal at a time. While your principal is within 5 feet of you and you aren't incapacitated, it gains a +1 bonus to AC and has advantage on saving throws against being frightened."},{"type":"p","text":"Intercept. When your principal takes damage while within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed toward it without provoking opportunity attacks. If you end that movement within 5 feet of your principal, or were already within 5 feet of it, reduce the damage it takes by 1d10 plus your fighter level. You then take half the damage prevented, and that damage can't be reduced or prevented."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use Intercept a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Advance Work","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 7th level, you plan movements for a living. You and your principal have advantage on initiative rolls while you are within 30 feet of each other."},{"type":"p","text":"When combat begins, you and your principal can each immediately move up to half your speed without provoking opportunity attacks. Either of you can draw a weapon, drop prone or take cover as part of that movement."},{"type":"p","text":"You also always know the shortest route from where you are standing to the nearest exit of any building you have spent 10 minutes in, and you can't be surprised in such a building while you are conscious."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Interdict","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can mark it. The mark lasts until the end of your next turn, until you mark another creature, or until you are incapacitated."},{"type":"p","text":"A marked creature provokes an opportunity attack from you when it moves to within 10 feet of your principal, whether or not it leaves your reach. Your opportunity attacks against a marked creature deal an extra 2d8 damage of the weapon's type, and a marked creature you hit with an opportunity attack has its speed reduced to 0 until the end of its turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Standing Order","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 15th level, Intercept reduces damage by 2d10 plus your fighter level, and you take none of the damage you prevent when you use it on your principal."},{"type":"p","text":"When you use Intercept, you can also make one melee weapon attack as part of the same reaction against a creature within 5 feet of you."},{"type":"p","text":"You now regain all expended uses of Intercept when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Detail","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, the contract still says you work alone, and in practice you stopped some time ago. While you are conscious, every ally within 10 feet of you, including your principal, gains a +2 bonus to AC and to saving throws against being moved, knocked prone, grappled or restrained."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns when an ally within 10 feet of you takes damage, you can reduce that damage by twice your proficiency bonus. This requires no action, and you take none of the damage prevented."},{"type":"p","text":"If your principal drops to 0 hit points while within 10 feet of you, you can use your reaction to drag it up to 15 feet and stabilise it. It regains hit points equal to your fighter level. Once you do so, you can't do it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fighter-ringmount","cls":"Fighter","name":"Ringmount","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Spends the fight standing up through a hole in a roof, holding something belt-fed.","description":["Somebody has to be on the gun. Ringmount fighters ride the roof hatch: braced in the ring, feeding the belt, calling the driver's turns over the intercom while the vehicle does its best to throw them into the street. It is a narrow specialism with a short list of qualified people and a shorter list of old ones. They know the weight of every mount in the city and they will complain about all of them."],"features":[{"name":"Weapon Ring","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with land and water vehicles and in the Perception skill, and you can operate any mounted weapon you have seen operated once."},{"type":"p","text":"Brace. As a bonus action, you can brace a ranged weapon against a fixed point: a weapon ring, a windowsill, a railing, a wall, the roof of a parked car. You stay braced until you move, are moved, or brace somewhere else. While braced, your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover, your weapon's long range is doubled, and being within 5 feet of a hostile creature doesn't impose disadvantage on your ranged attack rolls."},{"type":"p","text":"Suppressing Fire. While braced, you can take an action to put fire across an area instead of attacking. Choose a 15-foot cube within your weapon's normal range. The area is suppressed until the start of your next turn. A creature in a suppressed area has disadvantage on attack rolls, and a creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, it takes damage equal to one roll of your weapon's damage dice plus your Dexterity modifier and its speed is halved until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, it takes no damage."},{"type":"p","text":"This save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier. You can use Suppressing Fire a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Gun Crew","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 7th level, you keep your feet on a moving vehicle. You ignore difficult terrain while on a vehicle, you can't be knocked prone by a vehicle's movement, and you have advantage on saving throws made to avoid falling off one."},{"type":"p","text":"You can brace as part of your movement rather than as a bonus action, and you stay braced while a vehicle you are riding moves, however it moves."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature you can see damages a vehicle you are riding or tries to board it, you can use your reaction to make one ranged weapon attack against that creature."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Beaten Zone","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, your Suppressing Fire covers a 20-foot cube, and the damage on a failed save becomes two rolls of your weapon's damage dice plus your Dexterity modifier. A creature that fails the saving throw also can't take reactions until the start of your next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, while braced, the first time on each of your turns that you hit a creature with a ranged weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's type."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Traverse","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 15th level, you can work the whole field of fire. When you take the Attack action while braced, you can make one additional ranged weapon attack as part of that action, provided every attack you make during the action targets a different creature."},{"type":"p","text":"You now regain all expended uses of Suppressing Fire when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sustained Fire","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, you can hold ground down for as long as somebody keeps feeding you. You can use Suppressing Fire as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also maintain a suppressed area. At the start of each of your turns, you can keep an existing suppressed area in place for another round, requiring no action and costing no use of the feature. An area can be maintained for up to 1 minute, you can maintain only one at a time, and maintenance ends if you become incapacitated, stop being braced, or move more than 30 feet from the area."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a creature that fails a saving throw against your Suppressing Fire can't take the Dash action until the start of your next turn."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fighter-arbitration","cls":"Fighter","name":"Arbitration","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"When two subsidiaries can't agree, the contract names a duel and somebody names you.","description":["Litigation is slow and discovery is expensive, so the standard commercial contract now carries a combat clause. Arbitration fighters are the named parties: retained by the quarter, called out by subsection, and expected to settle the matter inside a taped circle in front of two sets of lawyers. They study one opponent at a time and can quote the relevant wording while doing it. Losing is survivable. Losing badly is a performance review."],"features":[{"name":"Named Party","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency in the Persuasion skill and with one artisan's tool of your choice. You can also read a combat clause closely enough to find what is wrong with it, which is usually the venue."},{"type":"p","text":"Call. As a bonus action, you can call out one creature you can see within 30 feet. The call lasts for 1 minute, until you call another creature, until the called creature drops to 0 hit points, or until you are incapacitated. You can call a creature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"Findings. The first time on each of your turns that you hit a called creature with a weapon attack, you record a finding against it, to a maximum of three. Findings against a creature are lost when its call ends. A called creature suffers the following as findings accumulate against it."},{"type":"ul","items":["One finding: it can't take the Disengage action, and you have advantage on opportunity attacks against it.","Two findings: it can't take the Dash action, and its speed can't be increased above its normal walking speed.","Three findings: your weapon attacks against it deal an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's type, and it has disadvantage on saving throws and ability checks made to avoid being grappled, shoved or knocked prone."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Concede the Point","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 7th level, you have read enough proceedings to know that taking a hit is sometimes the cheapest available move. When a called creature hits you with an attack, you can use your reaction to concede the point. You take half the damage from that attack, and you record one finding against that creature."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you have advantage on saving throws against effects created by a called creature, and you have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) and Wisdom (Insight) checks made during a formal challenge, negotiation or arbitration. Ten minutes with a contract tells you every obligation it places on you and one it places on the other party that they would rather you had missed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Motion to Compel","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 10th level, you can force the other party to engage. As a bonus action, you can compel a called creature you can see within 30 feet. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or spend its next turn moving toward you by the most direct route available, and it can't willingly move more than 30 feet away from you until the end of that turn. On a failed save, you also record one finding against it."},{"type":"p","text":"This save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, the extra damage you deal to a creature with three findings against it increases to 2d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Summary Judgment","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 15th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a called creature that has three or more findings against it, you can move the matter to judgment. The creature must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes an extra 4d8 damage of the weapon's type and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half the extra damage and isn't stunned."},{"type":"p","text":"This save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Binding","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, a call you make is binding on both parties. Your call lasts for 10 minutes instead of 1 minute, and you can record up to five findings against a called creature, though no threshold beyond the third has an effect of its own."},{"type":"ul","items":["A called creature within 30 feet of you gains no benefit from being invisible or otherwise unseen against your attacks, and you always know its location.","While a called creature is within 30 feet of you, no effect can put more than 30 feet between the two of you against your will. Teleportation and forced movement that would do so simply fail.","You have advantage on attack rolls against a called creature while no other creature is within 5 feet of either of you."]},{"type":"p","text":"When a called creature drops to 0 hit points, you regain hit points equal to your fighter level and can call a new creature as part of the same turn without expending a use of the feature."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"monk-way-of-the-cooling-loop","cls":"Monk","name":"Way of the Cooling Loop","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Meditates in the coolant gallery under a data fortress. Moves heat the way other schools move ki.","description":["The order keeps its hall three floors beneath a merchant bank's server farm, in the gallery where the coolant comes back hot. Novices sit in the noise for a year and learn to hold a temperature in the body the way other people hold a breath. A monk of the Cooling Loop can put a palm on a burning bulkhead and take the heat out of it. They can also put it back, into a person, which is the part the order leaves off the recruitment notices."],"features":[{"name":"Thermal Discipline","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You learn to hold heat in the body and let it go where you choose. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can spend 1 ki point to move heat through the contact. Choose one effect:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Chill. The target takes an extra 1d6 cold damage and its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of your next turn.","Scald. The target takes an extra 1d6 fire damage, and the next attack roll made against it before the end of your next turn has advantage."]},{"type":"p","text":"You have resistance to fire damage while you have at least 1 ki point remaining, and you take no harm from environmental heat or cold, however extreme. The order's novices demonstrate this by sleeping in the return pipe."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Heat Sink","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you or a creature you can see within 10 feet of you takes fire or lightning damage, you can use your reaction and spend 1 ki point to draw the energy into yourself. Reduce the damage taken by 1d10 + your monk level."},{"type":"p","text":"You then hold that energy. The next time you hit a creature with an unarmed strike before the end of your next turn, the strike deals extra fire damage equal to half the damage you prevented, rounded down. If you do not spend it in time it bleeds off harmlessly and you steam for about a minute."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Thermal Runaway","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 3 ki points to drive the temperature of a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you can see within 60 feet past what the air will hold. Each creature in the area must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 6d6 fire damage and has disadvantage on attack rolls and Constitution saving throws until the end of its next turn as its cooling fails. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect. You are not affected by your own runaway."},{"type":"p","text":"Unattended flammable objects in the area ignite. Powered devices in the area, including installed cyberware, stop working until the end of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Absolute Zero","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 5 ki points to pull every scrap of heat out of one creature you can see within 30 feet. The target must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save it takes 10d10 cold damage and is paralyzed until the end of your next turn. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and its speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this feature freezes through. It shatters at the next blow, and no ordinary medicine will bring it back."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"monk-way-of-the-dead-channel","cls":"Monk","name":"Way of the Dead Channel","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Trains in the static between abandoned frequencies. Fights by taking the signal away.","description":["The order broadcasts on bands the corporations gave up on forty years ago, from a transmitter it maintains by hand. Novices spend their first year listening to nothing, which is the lesson. What they learn there is how much of a modern fight is carried on a channel: targeting data, squad comms, the small handshake between a smartgun and the hand holding it. A monk of the Dead Channel walks into a room and the room goes quiet."],"features":[{"name":"Null Carrier","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You generate a field of dead air. You cannot be located, identified or tracked by any electronic sensor, camera or tracking implant, and no recording made of you retains your face. A creature relying on a targeting implant, smartlink or drone feed to see you gains no benefit from it."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll, you can use your reaction and spend 1 ki point to cut its targeting. The attack roll is made with disadvantage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Feedback Strike","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your strikes carry the noise you sit in. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can spend 1 ki point to force it to make a Wisdom saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save the target takes 2d8 psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn it cannot speak or transmit, cannot take reactions, and automatically fails to cast any spell requiring a verbal component. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dead Air","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 3 ki points to fill a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on yourself with a low static that no sound and no signal crosses in either direction. The effect lasts 1 minute, moves with you, and ends early if you use this feature again or are incapacitated."},{"type":"p","text":"Creatures inside the sphere hear one another normally. Nothing outside hears them, and nothing inside can hear or transmit out. Divination that relies on sound or on intercepted signal fails within the area."},{"type":"p","text":"A hostile creature in the area cannot communicate with any creature outside it, gains no benefit from a shared sensor feed, comms link or spotter, and has disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Off the Air","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 4 ki points to cut one creature you can see within 60 feet out of the world's signal entirely. The target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or be affected for 1 minute."},{"type":"p","text":"While affected, the creature cannot be seen, heard or perceived by any creature other than you, and it cannot see, hear or perceive any creature other than you. It cannot speak to, touch, target, or be targeted by anyone but you. It still occupies the ground it is standing on. It is, for the duration, alone in a room with you."},{"type":"p","text":"The creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"monk-way-of-the-charged-rosary","cls":"Monk","name":"Way of the Charged Rosary","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Prayer beads wound in copper wire. Each one holds a strike until it is needed.","description":["The rosary is ninety-nine beads of god-bone, each wrapped in fine copper, each able to hold about as much charge as a heart needs to stop. A monk of this order tells the beads through the day and fights with the day's accumulation. Older monks are quiet people who are careful about what they touch and who they shake hands with. The order's cemetery is mostly novices who got impatient."],"features":[{"name":"Told Beads","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a charged rosary, which you can rebuild over a short rest from beads, wire and an hour of patience. You have a number of charges equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended charges when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can expend one charge to earth it through them. The target takes an extra 1d8 lightning damage and cannot take reactions until the end of your next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can spend 2 ki points to charge a number of beads equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of one, up to your maximum."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grounding Stance","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have resistance to lightning damage. When you take lightning damage, you can use your reaction to catch it instead: you take no damage from the triggering effect, and you charge one bead, up to your maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when you fail a saving throw against being paralyzed, restrained or stunned, you can expend one charge to reroll it. You must use the new roll."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Arc Chain","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The charge no longer stops where you put it. When you expend a charge on an unarmed strike, choose up to two other creatures within 15 feet of the target. Each must make a Dexterity saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier, taking 2d8 lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature with cyberware installed has disadvantage on this saving throw. Chrome is an excellent conductor and a very poor ground."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Full Discharge","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 3 ki points and expend every remaining charge on your rosary at once. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 1d10 lightning damage for each charge expended and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and is not stunned. You must expend at least one charge to use this feature."},{"type":"p","text":"Every unshielded light, screen and powered device within 60 feet of you goes dark for 1 minute. Your rosary is bare until you recharge it as normal."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"monk-way-of-the-grafted-fist","cls":"Monk","name":"Way of the Grafted Fist","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Treats the body as a first draft. Trains to take other people's chrome apart by hand.","description":["The order teaches that the body you were issued was a first attempt and that no first attempt is sacred. Its monks install ware deliberately and then train around the loss, learning the seams of every implant on the market the way other schools learn pressure points. A Grafted Fist knows where a spinal rig bolts to the vertebrae and how hard to hit it. They are not welcome in most clinics, for reasons the clinics consider obvious."],"features":[{"name":"Seams and Sockets","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know how ware goes in, and therefore how it comes out. You can tell at a glance what cyberware a creature you can see is carrying, what tier it is, and roughly where it sits under the skin."},{"type":"p","text":"When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can spend 1 ki point to work a seam. If the target has cyberware installed, it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or one implant of your choice goes offline until the end of your next turn. A creature loses every benefit an offline implant grants it."},{"type":"p","text":"If the target has no cyberware, it instead takes an extra 1d10 force damage and its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of your next turn. A joint is a joint."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Stripping","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your unarmed strikes count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks, and they deal an extra 1d6 damage against constructs and against creatures carrying tier 3 or tier 4 cyberware."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when you score a critical hit against a creature, any implant you take offline with Seams and Sockets against that creature on the same turn stays offline for 1 minute instead, and nothing short of a workbench will bring it back up."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reclamation","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take an implant offline, you can borrow what it was doing. Until the end of your next turn you gain one benefit of your choice:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Your speed increases by 20 feet and opportunity attacks against you have disadvantage.","You gain temporary hit points equal to twice your monk level.","Your unarmed strikes score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20.","You have blindsight out to 30 feet and cannot be surprised."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Unmake the Work","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 5 ki points and touch one creature within 5 feet of you. It must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, every piece of cyberware the creature carries goes offline for 1 minute and it takes 8d10 force damage as its frame takes up the load its chrome used to carry. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and one implant of your choice goes offline for the same duration."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature with no cyberware takes the damage as normal and is also stunned until the end of its next turn on a failed save. Bringing the disabled ware back up afterward takes a clinic, an hour, and a technician willing to ask nothing."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"paladin-oath-of-the-dead-orbit","cls":"Paladin","name":"Oath of the Dead Orbit","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Sworn to a derelict satellite that still transmits. Somebody has to answer it.","description":["The satellite has been dead for sixty years by any reasonable definition and it still sends, once every ninety-four minutes, a short packet nobody has decoded. The order took that as an oath. Its paladins keep listening posts on rooftops and ridgelines, log every pass by hand, and walk to wherever the footprint falls when something there needs doing. They do not claim the thing overhead is a god. They claim it is owed an answer."],"features":[{"name":"Tenets of the Dead Orbit","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The oath is short because it was written on a rooftop in the cold. Every member learns it in the first week and recites it at each pass."},{"type":"ul","items":["Keep the log. Every pass is recorded, in your own hand, whether or not anything comes of it.","Answer what calls. A signal asking for help is answered before it is understood.","Hold the ground under the footprint. What the orbit passes over, you are answerable for.","Nothing is abandoned twice."]},{"type":"p","text":"Channel Divinity. When you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},{"type":"p","text":"Downlink. As a bonus action, you designate one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. For 1 minute, you know its location while it is on the same plane of existence as you, you have advantage on attack rolls against it, and it gains no benefit from invisibility, cover or concealment against your attacks. The first time on each turn that an ally of yours hits the target, that ally deals an extra 1d6 radiant damage. The effect ends early if the target drops to 0 hit points."},{"type":"p","text":"Orbital Rebuke. As an action, you call down the weight of something in a decaying orbit. Choose a point you can see within 60 feet of you. Each creature within 10 feet of that point must make a Dexterity saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. On a failed save a creature takes radiant damage equal to 2d8 + your paladin level and is knocked prone. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and is not knocked prone."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Aura of the Watching Sky","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Something is always overhead and it is paying attention. You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you cannot be surprised while you are conscious, and you take no penalty on Wisdom (Perception) checks from dim light, smoke, rain, glare or electronic interference."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a hostile creature that attacks a creature in the aura while hidden or unseen gains no advantage on that attack roll, and its position is revealed to you until the end of its turn."},{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clear Line","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Nothing between you and a target counts for much any more. You ignore half cover and three-quarters cover when you make a weapon attack, and a creature you can see cannot hide from you."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature that has no ally within 10 feet of it, the attack deals an extra 2d8 radiant damage. The order files this as a clean pass and writes it in the log the same evening."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deorbit","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you open the channel and let what is up there come down through you. For 1 minute you gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for a further 30 feet.","At the start of each of your turns, each hostile creature within 30 feet of you takes 2d8 radiant damage.","You can use your Downlink Channel Divinity option as a bonus action without expending a use of your Channel Divinity.","Once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature you have designated with Downlink, the attack deals an extra 4d10 radiant damage and the target must succeed on a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or be knocked prone."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"paladin-oath-of-the-ledger","cls":"Paladin","name":"Oath of the Ledger","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Every harm is an entry. The order keeps the books, and then it collects.","description":["The order began as an audit division and never entirely stopped being one. Its paladins carry a physical ledger, paper, because paper cannot be edited from somewhere else, and they write down what is done to the people in their care. The debt is then collected in person, with interest at a rate the order publishes every spring. They are unfailingly polite about it, which most debtors find is the worst part."],"features":[{"name":"Tenets of the Ledger","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The oath is four lines printed on the inside cover of every ledger the order issues. Members are expected to read it before each entry."},{"type":"ul","items":["Write it down. An injury nobody recorded is an injury nobody will answer for.","Collect in person. A debt sold on to someone else is a debt forgiven.","Pay your own entries. The book has your name in it too.","Never round down."]},{"type":"p","text":"Channel Divinity. When you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},{"type":"p","text":"Enter the Debt. As a bonus action, you open an account against one creature you can see within 30 feet of you, which lasts 1 minute. Each time that creature deals damage to you or to a creature friendly to you, the account grows by 1d6, to a maximum number of dice equal to your paladin level. When you hit the creature with a melee weapon attack, you can close the account: the attack deals extra radiant damage equal to a roll of the accumulated dice, and the effect ends."},{"type":"p","text":"Call the Note. As an action, you demand payment from one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. It must make a Charisma saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. On a failed save it takes radiant damage equal to the total damage it dealt on its last turn, and one creature of your choice within 30 feet of you regains hit points equal to half that amount. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and no hit points are restored. A creature that dealt no damage on its last turn is unaffected and knows it got off lightly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Aura of Accounts","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are conscious, every point of damage dealt to a friendly creature within 10 feet of you is noted. When a hostile creature damages a creature in the aura, that creature takes radiant damage equal to your Charisma modifier, a minimum of 1."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you always know the current hit points of every friendly creature in the aura, which means you always know when one of them is lying about how badly they are hurt."},{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Foreclosure Notice","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see within 30 feet of you reduces a friendly creature to 0 hit points, or deals damage to you or a friendly creature equal to or greater than your paladin level in a single attack, you can use your reaction to serve notice. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or be marked until you finish your next long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"While marked, the creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you, cannot regain hit points above half its hit point maximum, and you know its location while it is on the same plane of existence as you. The mark ends early if the creature settles the entry, which the order defines as restoring the creature it dropped to consciousness by its own effort and at its own cost."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, your Enter the Debt accounts now grow by 1d8 rather than 1d6."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Settlement","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you call the whole book due at once. For 1 minute you gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Every hostile creature within 30 feet of you has an open account against it, and you need not expend Channel Divinity to open one. New arrivals in the aura are entered automatically.","Each account grows by 2d8 rather than 1d8 whenever that creature deals damage to you or to a creature friendly to you.","When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack you can close its account as part of that attack, and closing an account restores hit points to you equal to half the extra radiant damage dealt.","You cannot be charmed or frightened, and you have advantage on saving throws against being paralyzed or stunned."]},{"type":"p","text":"When the effect ends, you take 1d6 psychic damage for each account still open. The order records uncollected debt against the collector, and has never once been talked out of it."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"paladin-oath-of-the-clean-room","cls":"Paladin","name":"Oath of the Clean Room","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Sworn to containment. What gets in does not get out, and neither do they.","description":["The order holds the seals on nine sites nobody will name and one everybody has heard of. Its paladins wear filtration as vestments and treat contagion, corruption and bad code as the same problem arriving by different routes. The work is mostly standing in a doorway for a long time and then burning something. Members are trained never to run from a breach, because running is how a breach travels."],"features":[{"name":"Tenets of the Clean Room","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The oath is stencilled at eye height beside every airlock the order maintains, so that it is the last thing read on the way in."},{"type":"ul","items":["Seal first. The breach is the emergency. Whatever caused it can wait.","Do not carry it out. If you are the vector, you stay inside.","Burn at the source. Half a cure is a slower disaster.","Log the exposure, including your own."]},{"type":"p","text":"Channel Divinity. When you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},{"type":"p","text":"Quarantine Seal. As an action, you raise a boundary around a point you can see within 30 feet of you: a cylinder with a 15-foot radius and a height of 20 feet, lasting 1 minute. When you create it, designate any number of creatures you can see as contained. A contained creature cannot enter or leave the cylinder, and no gas, liquid, spore or airborne agent crosses its wall in either direction. Any other creature passes freely. A contained creature can use its action to make a Charisma saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier, ending the effect on itself on a success."},{"type":"p","text":"Purge Cycle. As an action, you run the cycle. Each creature of your choice within 15 feet of you is cured of one disease or one poison affecting it. Then each creature of your choice within 15 feet of you that is an undead, an aberration, or currently poisoned or diseased must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier, taking radiant damage equal to 2d10 + your paladin level on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Aura of Containment","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Nothing gets past you sideways. You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you have advantage on saving throws against poison, against disease, and against any effect that would alter your body or possess your mind against your will."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a hostile creature that starts its turn in the aura while poisoned or diseased takes radiant damage equal to your proficiency bonus."},{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sterile Field","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to disease and to the poisoned condition, and you cannot be infected, corrupted or possessed by any means. Long-serving members of the order describe this as the point where the work stops costing them anything."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature you can see within 30 feet of you would gain the blinded, deafened, paralyzed, poisoned or stunned condition, you can use your reaction to run a local cycle on it. That creature does not gain the condition. Any other effect of the same cause resolves as normal."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Full Decontamination","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you run the site cycle on yourself and let it burn outward. For 1 minute you gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You are immune to poison damage and to necrotic damage, and you cannot be charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned or stunned.","At the start of each of your turns, each hostile creature within 30 feet of you takes 2d8 radiant damage.","At the start of each of your turns, each friendly creature within 30 feet of you regains hit points equal to your Charisma modifier, or ends one disease or one poison afflicting it, your choice for each creature.","Ground, water and air within 30 feet of you is purified as you pass, and lingering magical contamination of 5th level or lower in that space ends."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"paladin-oath-of-the-locked-door","cls":"Paladin","name":"Oath of the Locked Door","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"The order is a door. Doors do not negotiate and they do not move.","description":["They are hired as bodyguards and doormen and they take the job entirely literally. A paladin of this oath learns to stand in one place for eleven hours, to read a queue, and to understand that the person who gets through is the person they let through. The order trains in doorways, on stairs, and in the mouths of service corridors. It publishes its failure rate quarterly, which is both a boast and a penance."],"features":[{"name":"Tenets of the Locked Door","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Four lines, cut into the lintel of the training hall at a height that makes you duck to read them."},{"type":"ul","items":["Nothing passes uninvited.","The key is not for sale. Neither is the hinge.","Hold the frame. If the door comes down, you were the door.","Know who you let in, and remember their face afterward."]},{"type":"p","text":"Channel Divinity. When you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},{"type":"p","text":"Set the Frame. As a bonus action, you plant yourself. For 1 minute, or until you willingly move, you cannot be moved against your will, knocked prone, teleported or banished. Ground within 5 feet of you is difficult terrain for creatures hostile to you, and a hostile creature that tries to move from one space within 5 feet of you to another must succeed on a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or have its movement end immediately."},{"type":"p","text":"Bar the Way. When a creature you can see within 10 feet of you makes an attack against a creature other than you, or moves out of a space within 10 feet of you, you can use your reaction to bar it. The creature must make a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. On a failed save its movement ends, it takes 2d10 radiant damage, and its attack automatically misses if it has not yet resolved. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and is not stopped."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Aura of the Threshold","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are a fixed point and the room arranges itself around you. Ground within 10 feet of you is difficult terrain for creatures hostile to you."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a friendly creature in the aura cannot be moved against its will, pushed, pulled, teleported or banished by a hostile effect unless you allow it."},{"type":"p","text":"At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Load Bearing","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a friendly creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to take that damage in its place. You have resistance to damage taken this way, and the damage cannot be redirected again."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, the first time each long rest that damage would reduce you to 0 hit points, you instead drop to 1 hit point, and each hostile creature within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or be knocked prone. The order calls this holding, and considers it the only part of the job worth teaching twice."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bulkhead","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you stop being a person standing in a doorway and become the door. For 1 minute you gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You have resistance to all damage, and you cannot be moved against your will, knocked prone, teleported or banished.","Friendly creatures within 10 feet of you have half cover against attacks made by creatures more than 5 feet away from you.","A hostile creature that starts its turn within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or have its speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn.","When a creature within 10 feet of you hits you with a melee attack, it takes 2d10 radiant damage."]},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"ranger-signal-hunter","cls":"Ranger","name":"Signal Hunter","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Tracks by emission rather than footprint. Everybody leaks something.","description":["A person moving through a city trails a wake: handset pings, an implant's heartbeat telemetry, the small authentication chirp a smartgun makes when it wakes up. The Signal Hunter reads that wake the way an older kind of ranger read bent grass. They carry a receiver they built themselves and will not let anyone else handle it. The work pays because the people worth finding are exactly the people who know to go quiet."],"features":[{"name":"Emission Read","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can tune a receiver to a creature's electronic signature. By spending 1 minute studying a creature, a device it has used, or a place it spent an hour, you lock onto its signature. For the next 24 hours you know the direction and rough distance to that creature while it is within 1 mile of you and on the same plane of existence as you."},{"type":"p","text":"You can hold a number of locked signatures at once equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can drop one at any time. You also always know whether a space within 60 feet of you is under electronic surveillance, and how many powered devices are in a room before you open the door."},{"type":"p","text":"Once on each of your turns, when you make a weapon attack against a creature whose signature you have locked, you ignore half cover and three-quarters cover for that attack, and the attack deals an extra 1d6 damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Null Envelope","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have learned to fold your own wake shut. As a bonus action, you can become invisible to every sensor, camera, tracking implant and drone within 300 feet of you for 1 hour, or until you end the effect as a bonus action. Recordings made of you while it holds show empty space and clean floor."},{"type":"p","text":"While the envelope holds, no automated system can identify, track or log you, and a creature relying on a targeting implant, smartlink or drone feed has disadvantage on attack rolls against you."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Triangulate","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Two fixes make a line. Three make a grave. When you hit a creature whose signature you have locked, you can use your bonus action to call a fix on it."},{"type":"p","text":"Until the end of your next turn, you and every creature friendly to you knows the target's exact location, the target gains no benefit from invisibility or from being hidden, and the first attack roll each of your allies makes against it has advantage."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Last Known Position","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can read a wake long after the body that made it has gone. By spending 10 minutes in a place, you learn every creature that passed through it in the last seven days whose signature you could have locked, what powered gear each one carried, and which way they left."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you know the instant a creature whose signature you have locked drops below half its hit point maximum. When that happens, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against it if it is within range, and that attack deals an extra 3d6 damage."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"ranger-scrapline-warden","cls":"Ranger","name":"Scrapline Warden","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Warden of the landfill ecologies, where the fauna has more steel in it than fur.","description":["Out past the last arcology the ground is made of what the arcology threw away, forty years deep and still settling. Things live in it. Some of them were drones once and are something else now, and the Scrapline Warden knows their nesting seasons and their tempers. Wardens work the lines as guides, as cullers, and occasionally as the only thing standing between a salvage crew and a nest they should not have opened."],"features":[{"name":"Scavenger's Tongue","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can communicate simple ideas to beasts and to constructs of Intelligence 4 or lower, and understand what they communicate back. Such creatures are never hostile to you on sight, and you have advantage on Charisma checks made to influence them."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you can spend 10 minutes and a double handful of scrap to build a single-use device out of what is lying around. Choose one when you build it:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Snare. Place it in a 5-foot square. The first creature to enter that square must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or be restrained. A restrained creature escapes with a successful Strength check against the same DC.","Charge. As an action, you detonate it. Each creature within 10 feet of it takes 2d6 fire damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity saving throw against the same DC.","Beacon. It transmits a signal you can follow from up to 2 miles away for 24 hours, and shrieks if anything but you moves it."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can have a number of these devices built at one time equal to your proficiency bonus. They degrade back into junk 24 hours after you build them."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Weathered","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The scraplines have had eight or nine chances to kill you and have not taken any of them. You have resistance to poison damage, you have advantage on saving throws against disease, and you take no harm from contaminated ground, water or air."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns when you deal damage to a construct or to a creature with cyberware installed, you can make the damage corrosive. The target's Armor Class is reduced by 1 until it finishes a long rest or somebody repairs the damage properly. This feature cannot reduce a creature's Armor Class below 10."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nest Caller","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can call whatever lives nearby. Each beast and each construct of Intelligence 4 or lower within 1 mile of you that can hear or receive the call comes toward you at its best speed, arriving over the next 10 minutes. The DM decides what answers. The scraplines rarely send nothing."},{"type":"p","text":"Creatures that answer are not charmed and are not yours. They are inclined to treat you as one of their own and to treat whatever you are fighting as the more immediate problem. They disperse after 1 hour, or when you dismiss them, or when the fighting stops being interesting."},{"type":"p","text":"While at least one creature that answered is within 30 feet of you, you can use a bonus action to direct one of them. That creature uses its reaction to move up to its speed and make one attack against a target of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Salvaged Frame","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have rebuilt yourself out of the line, a piece at a time, and the joins have held so far. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from nonmagical attacks while you are in a dump, ruin, worksite, wreck or any other place built out of manufactured debris.","When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 hit point instead. You must finish a long rest before you can do so again.","You no longer need to eat, and you can drink anything wet without consequence."]},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a construct or a creature with cyberware installed takes damage from one of your attacks, you can use your reaction to force a cascade. The creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or take an extra 6d6 lightning damage and be incapacitated until the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"ranger-arcology-poacher","cls":"Ranger","name":"Arcology Poacher","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Hunts inside the towers. Four hundred floors is wilderness if you look at it right.","description":["An arcology is four hundred floors of habitat with a closed ecology, a private police force and a very firm opinion about who belongs on which level. The Poacher goes in anyway, up the outside or in through the plant rooms, takes whatever the contract names, and is gone before the shift change. They think of security patrols as migration patterns. It is not a comparison that has ever let them down."],"features":[{"name":"Vertical Ground","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed, and you can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check. Moving through a window, vent, cable run or service shaft costs you no extra movement."},{"type":"p","text":"You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made inside a building or structure."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature that has not yet taken a turn in the current combat, or that cannot see you, the attack deals an extra 1d8 damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shift Change","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You read a building's rhythm the way other rangers read weather. After 10 minutes of observation you learn the patrol pattern, shift length, camera coverage and alert posture of any security force in the structure, and you know the next window in which a given route goes unwatched."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you can use a bonus action to break contact. You become invisible until the end of your next turn, or until you attack or force a creature to make a saving throw. When you turn invisible this way, you can immediately move up to your speed without provoking opportunity attacks."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use the bonus action a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Service Corridor","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Every structure has a way through that its owners stopped thinking about twenty years ago, and you can find it. By spending 1 minute, you and up to five willing creatures within 10 feet of you pass through a wall, floor, ceiling or sealed barrier up to 10 feet thick and come out the far side, by a route that was always there. Sensors on the barrier do not register the crossing."},{"type":"p","text":"You must have seen the far side or have a sound idea of what is on it. If you are wrong, the route dead-ends and the attempt is wasted."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, you can move through a gap at least 1 foot wide as though it were open ground, and you can move through the space of any creature."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use the crossing a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clean Extraction","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The job ends when you are outside holding the thing, and you have become very good at the last part. When you reduce a creature to 0 hit points, drop below half your hit point maximum, or take the Disengage action, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed. This movement can run up a wall or across a ceiling and does not provoke opportunity attacks."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature that has no ally within 15 feet of it, the attack deals an extra 4d6 damage, and the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or be unable to shout, signal or otherwise raise an alarm for 1 minute."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"ranger-bonecarver","cls":"Ranger","name":"Bonecarver","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Hunts the god-carcasses in the wastes for material nobody else can supply.","description":["The bodies are out there. They are large, they are not entirely dead, and what grows on them is worth more than the crews that go after it. A Bonecarver knows which vertebra to open, which growths are safe to handle bare-handed, and roughly how long you have before the carcass notices. Most of them carry a saw older than their grandparents and a reliquary of offcuts they will not sell at any price offered so far."],"features":[{"name":"Carver's Eye","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know anatomy: yours, other people's, and the kind that does not fit in a textbook. As a bonus action, you can study one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. Until you study another creature, you know its current hit points, its damage resistances and immunities, and where its worst-mended injury sits."},{"type":"p","text":"The first time on each of your turns that you hit a studied creature with a weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d6 damage, and that extra damage ignores resistance to the attack's damage type."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency with one set of artisan's tools of your choice, and you can harvest usable material from the corpse of a Large or larger creature with 10 minutes of work and a clean blade."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reliquary","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry offcuts of god-bone strung on wire. You have a number of charms equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can restring the reliquary from harvested material over a short rest. You regain all expended charms when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can expend a charm as a reaction to reroll a saving throw you have just failed, or to give a creature you can see within 30 feet of you advantage on a saving throw it is about to make. You must use the new roll."},{"type":"p","text":"A charm spent this way crumbles to grit. Bonecarvers keep count, and a bare reliquary is considered sufficient reason to go back out."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Marrow Draw","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can draw on a piece of god-bone you carry. Choose yourself or a creature you can touch. The target regains 4d8 hit points and ends one disease or one poison affecting it. If you draw instead from the corpse of a Large or larger creature within 5 feet of you, the healing becomes 6d8 and the corpse is spent for good."},{"type":"p","text":"Whenever you use this feature, the next weapon attack you hit with before the end of your next turn deals an extra 2d6 necrotic damage."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Godsmeat","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have eaten from something that used to be worshipped. It was a decision, it was taken sober, and it is in you now. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Your hit point maximum increases by an amount equal to your ranger level.","You have advantage on saving throws against being frightened, and necrotic damage cannot reduce you below 1 hit point.","You need only 4 hours of sleep to gain the benefit of a long rest, and you dream about weather in places you have never been."]},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once on each of your turns when you hit a studied creature, you can force it to make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier. On a failed save it takes 4d8 necrotic damage and its hit point maximum is reduced by the same amount until it finishes a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use that saving throw effect a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"rogue-skiptracer","cls":"Rogue","name":"Skiptracer","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Finds people who have paid a great deal of money not to be found.","description":["A skiptracer works from paper. Bank pings, clinic intake forms, the grocery order that still goes to an address nobody lives at. They read a life backwards until it points at a room, and then they knock on that room's door. Most of the job is sitting down. The last ten minutes of it are not."],"features":[{"name":"Paper Trail","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes reviewing a creature's records, possessions or habits to make it your quarry. You can have one quarry at a time, and naming a new one ends the old one. While a creature is your quarry:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You have advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) and Wisdom (Survival) checks made to locate it or to predict where it will go next.","While it is within 1 mile of you, you know the direction to it, though not the distance and not what is in the way.","The first time on each of your turns that you hit it with an attack, its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can name a quarry a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hard Stop","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When your quarry takes the Dash action, teleports, boards a vehicle or otherwise tries to put distance between the two of you, you can use your reaction to close it down. The quarry must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). On a failed save, the movement or action is wasted and the quarry's speed becomes 0 until the end of its turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Filed and Published","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 1 hour and 500\u20b5 assembling everything you hold on your quarry and releasing it where the city will find it. Until you finish a long rest or name a new quarry, the quarry has disadvantage on Charisma checks made against anyone with network access, and it cannot use a credential, an account or a transit fare without you learning where and when within the hour."},{"type":"p","text":"Allies who have read the file have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Deception) checks made against the quarry. The quarry knows it has been published. Most of them run, which is the intended effect."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Collar","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you hit your quarry with a Sneak Attack while it is below half its hit point maximum, you can end the chase. The quarry must make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). On a failed save it is restrained and incapacitated for 1 minute, or until it takes damage from a source other than you. On a successful save it instead takes an extra 6d6 damage of the attack's type."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest. Clients pay more for delivery upright."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"rogue-facelift","cls":"Rogue","name":"Facelift","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Keeps other people's faces in a case and wears whichever one the door requires.","description":["Subdermal actuators, a vocal shim, and a library of faces taken from people who had stopped needing them. A facelift does not pick the lock. They walk up to the person holding the key and are, for eleven minutes, that person's line manager. The hard part is never the face. The hard part is remembering which one you have on."],"features":[{"name":"Borrowed Faces","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with a forgery kit and with the Deception skill. If you already have Deception, you gain proficiency in another skill of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes studying a humanoid you can see, or 1 hour studying recordings of one, to add its face to your library. Your library holds a number of faces equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can discard one whenever you add another."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can reshape your features, build and voice into any face in your library. The change lasts until you use this feature again. You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks made to pass as that person, and a creature who knows them must succeed on a Wisdom (Insight) check contested by your Charisma (Deception) check to notice anything wrong."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clean Break","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can drop your current face and take another from your library. Each creature that can see you when you do must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier) or lose track of you. Until the end of your next turn, a creature that fails cannot target you with an attack or a spell, and it treats you as a stranger who happens to be standing nearby."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Live Capture","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you first see a humanoid within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to take its face without studying it. A face taken this way is a working copy: it holds for 1 hour and carries no voice patterns or mannerisms, so checks made to pass as that person in front of someone who knows them do not gain advantage."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nobody in Particular","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Witnesses cannot hold you. A creature that sees you while you wear a face from your library remembers the face and nothing else: not your build, not your voice, not what you were carrying. Recordings resolve to the face. Divination magic and biometric systems that try to identify you return the person whose face you wore, and return it confidently."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, once per long rest you can die. You spend 10 minutes staging the scene and choose one face in your library. That identity is recorded as deceased, with a body and a file number, and everyone hunting it stops. The face is spent and leaves your library."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"rogue-chop-artist","cls":"Rogue","name":"Chop Artist","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Takes the chrome out of people, occasionally waiting until they have finished with it.","description":["Cyberware holds its value better than the person it was installed in. A chop artist knows the mounting points, the bleed risks and the two clinics that will not ask. In a fight they go for the same places they go for on the table. It is not cruelty. It is where the expensive parts are."],"features":[{"name":"Mounting Points","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with surgeon's tools. You can remove installed cyberware from a willing, unconscious or dead creature in 10 minutes without damaging it, and ware taken this way sells at full market price."},{"type":"p","text":"When you deal Sneak Attack damage to a construct or to a creature with cyberware installed, you can choose one implant, weapon mount or sensor you can identify on it. Until the end of your next turn that component is offline: the target loses any benefit it provides, and cannot use any attack or ability that depends on it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Seized Servo","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you hit a construct or a creature with cyberware installed, you can forgo one of your Sneak Attack dice to jam its actuators. The target must make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). On a failed save, its speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn and it cannot take reactions during that time."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this once per turn, whether or not the attack was a Sneak Attack."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Jury Rig","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can wear another person's ware without paying for it. As part of a short rest, you can fit one piece of harvested cyberware of tier 2 or lower into a temporary socket. You gain its benefits for 8 hours, and it costs you no Humanity, because nothing about the installation is permanent and your body knows it."},{"type":"p","text":"While borrowed ware is running you have disadvantage on death saving throws and on Constitution saving throws made to maintain concentration. You can use this feature once per long rest, and the ware is ruined when it comes out."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Strip the Frame","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can take a machine apart at speed. Choose a construct or a creature with cyberware installed within 5 feet of you. It must make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). On a failed save it takes 8d6 slashing damage and every piece of cyberware it carries goes dark for 1 minute, along with a construct's sensors and weapon systems. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and nothing goes dark."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature whose ware is dark loses everything that ware provided, including speed, Armor Class and any attack made with an implant. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"rogue-dead-air","cls":"Rogue","name":"Dead Air","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Carries a jammer the size of a lunchbox and treats the silence it makes as cover.","description":["Every room in this city is watched by something with a lens or an antenna. A dead air specialist carries the counter-argument: a broad-spectrum jammer, badly regulated, expensive to replace. Inside the bubble nothing records, nothing calls for help, and the smart weapons are suddenly just weapons."],"features":[{"name":"Grey Static","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You build and carry a jammer. As a bonus action you can switch it on, and it runs for up to 1 minute before it needs to cool. While it runs it fills a 15-foot-radius sphere centred on you."},{"type":"ul","items":["Cameras, microphones, radios, comms and electronic sensors inside the field do not function and record nothing.","You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made while inside the field.","The first time on each of your turns that you hit a creature inside the field with an attack, that creature cannot take reactions until the start of its next turn."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can run the jammer a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Targeting Fault","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see inside your field makes an attack roll, you can use your reaction to push noise into its optics and its smartlink. It has disadvantage on that roll, and if the attack was made with a firearm or an implanted weapon, it also has disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Signal Drought","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your field expands to a 30-foot radius and bites harder. A creature with any cyberware installed that starts its turn inside the field has its speed reduced by 10 feet and cannot take the Dash action until the start of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, no creature inside the field can call for help by any electronic means, and no alarm, image or message crosses the boundary on a network you have not authorised. Anything sent arrives after the field drops, timestamped and useless."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Black Hour","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can overdrive the jammer and take a building off the grid. For 1 hour, everything within 300 feet of you loses power, network access and electronic surveillance, including hardened, airgapped and magically warded systems."},{"type":"p","text":"A construct that starts its turn in that radius must succeed on a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier) or be incapacitated until the start of its next turn. Creatures with cyberware keep their implants but lose everything those implants were talking to. When the hour ends the jammer is slag, and building another takes a week and 4,000\u20b5."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"sorcerer-legacy-code","cls":"Sorcerer","name":"Legacy Code","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Your magic is an unpatched defect in firmware that left support before you were born.","description":["Someone up your family line bought an implant with a bad memory controller, and the fault copied itself into the germ line the way faults do. You do not cast spells so much as trigger conditions that were never meant to be reachable. It works reliably. Nobody can tell you why, and the vendor is three mergers gone."],"features":[{"name":"Exception Handling","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have learned to profit from the faults. When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher and it produces no effect at all, because every target succeeded on its saving throw or your attack roll missed, you regain sorcery points equal to half the spell's level, rounded up. You can do this once per turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency in the Technology skill, and you read machine code, log files and firmware dumps as easily as you read your own language."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Patch Notes","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you finish a long rest, choose one spell you know. Until your next long rest that spell is modified. Choose one of the following:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Its range doubles. If it has a range of touch, its range becomes 10 feet.","It requires no somatic components, and you can cast it with your hands full or restrained.","Once before your next long rest, you can cast it without expending a spell slot by spending a number of sorcery points equal to its level + 1."]},{"type":"p","text":"The patch is not stable. The first time you cast the modified spell on a given day, roll a d20. On a 1 the spell works exactly as intended and one mundane electronic device within 30 feet of you stops working permanently."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Memory Leak","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see within 60 feet casts a spell of 5th level or lower, you can use your reaction and spend 3 sorcery points to log it. You can hold one logged spell at a time, and you lose it when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can cast a logged spell once using your own spell slots, even if it is not on the sorcerer spell list, using Charisma as your spellcasting ability. Logging does not interfere with the creature casting the spell. You are reading a copy, not taking the original."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Root Cause","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell of 5th level or lower, you can declare it a rerun. At the start of your next turn the spell happens again, from the same origin, against the same targets or the same point in space, without expending a spell slot."},{"type":"p","text":"If the spell requires concentration, the rerun instead doubles its remaining duration and you make concentration saving throws for it with advantage. You can use this feature a second time before finishing a long rest by spending 7 sorcery points."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"sorcerer-grid-tapped","cls":"Sorcerer","name":"Grid-Tapped","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"You draw from the mains, and the block browns out while you are working.","description":["You were born a hundred metres from a substation, or you were rebuilt next to one. Either way your nervous system learned to treat the city's current as an organ. You can feel a building's draw through your feet. When you cast, the lights on that floor dim, and the utility company keeps an open file with your face in it."],"features":[{"name":"Mains Tap","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have resistance to lightning damage. When you cast a spell that deals fire, thunder or force damage, you can spend 1 sorcery point to change that damage to lightning."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also draw directly. As an action, you can touch a powered structure, a vehicle cell, a generator or a live cable and pull, regaining sorcery points equal to your proficiency bonus. The source is dead for 1 hour, and anyone who depends on that power will be looking for the reason. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ground Fault","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack while you are standing on the ground or touching any conductive surface, you can use your reaction and spend 1 sorcery point to complete the circuit. The attacker takes lightning damage equal to 1d8 + your Charisma modifier, and must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or be unable to take reactions until the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, a creature with any cyberware installed has disadvantage on saving throws against your spells that deal lightning damage. Chrome is an antenna."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Arc","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you deal lightning damage to a creature with a spell, you can spend 2 sorcery points to let the charge jump. Choose a second creature you can see within 15 feet of the first. It must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking half the damage you dealt to the first creature on a failed save, or none on a successful one."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this once per turn. The arc can reach a creature that was never a target of the spell, and it ignores any cover that is not fully sealed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Brownout","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can pull the district. Everything electrical within 500 feet of you stops for 1 minute: lights, locks, lifts, comms, cameras, vehicles and every piece of equipment that runs on a cell."},{"type":"p","text":"Each construct in the area must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or be incapacitated for the duration, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. Each creature with cyberware installed takes 8d8 lightning damage, or half as much on a successful Constitution saving throw. You regain sorcery points equal to your Charisma modifier from what you took, and the grid operator logs the draw to the second."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"sorcerer-sponsored","cls":"Sorcerer","name":"Sponsored","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"Your casting is free at the point of use because a brand is paying for the impressions.","description":["You signed at nineteen and the terms were generous. The power is real, the slots are your own, and every spell you cast above a cantrip wears a logo that everyone present can see. Marketing calls it organic reach. You call it the rent."],"features":[{"name":"Terms of Service","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Every spell you cast of 1st level or higher carries your sponsor's mark, visible and audible for its duration. You have disadvantage on ability checks made to cast a spell without being noticed, and you cannot hide which spell you cast from anyone who can see the mark."},{"type":"p","text":"In exchange, you are paid in attention. The first time on each of your turns that you cast a spell of 1st level or higher where at least one creature that is not your ally can see or hear it, you gain 1 impression. You can hold a number of impressions equal to your Charisma modifier, and you lose any you are holding when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can spend 1 impression to regain 1 sorcery point."},{"type":"p","text":"Your sponsor also carries your expenses, maintaining you at a comfortable lifestyle for as long as the account is in good standing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sponsored Content","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Each time you finish a long rest, your sponsor pushes a product. Choose one spell of 3rd level or lower from any class's spell list, or let the DM choose it if the campaign has something specific to move this quarter. You can cast that spell once without expending a spell slot, using Charisma as your spellcasting ability."},{"type":"p","text":"You can cast it again before your next long rest by spending a number of sorcery points equal to its level + 2. Every casting includes a fifteen-second endorsement that you deliver personally and cannot skip."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Brand Protection","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your sponsor protects its assets. When you drop to 0 hit points, you can instead drop to 1 hit point and gain temporary hit points equal to twice your sorcerer level."},{"type":"p","text":"A retrieval contractor is dispatched to your position, and a legal notice is served on whoever put you down, usually within the hour. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Prime Slot","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can take every screen, speaker and public display within 1 mile of you for 1 minute. Everyone in that radius sees you and hears you. For the duration you have advantage on Charisma checks made against any creature that watched."},{"type":"p","text":"Once during that minute, you can cast a spell of 5th level or lower through any display in the radius, choosing targets that display can see as though you were standing where it stands. You regain sorcery points equal to your Charisma modifier from the impressions. Everyone hunting you watched it too, and they now know which district you were standing in."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"sorcerer-relic-bone","cls":"Sorcerer","name":"Relic Bone","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"A dead god is load-bearing in your skeleton, and it has not stopped keeping its hours.","description":["A dig turned up a femur too large and too old, and the clinic that bought it cuts good implants. You have four pieces of that bone in you. The grafts took, the sockets healed, and something that used to be worshipped now performs its offices through your marrow at four in the morning."],"features":[{"name":"Marrow Rites","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The bone keeps the liturgy of a religion nobody has practised in six thousand years, and you have picked up the words. You can speak, read and write the dead language it remembers, and you can spend 1 sorcery point to understand any spoken language you hear for 1 minute."},{"type":"p","text":"The bone is also owed. Whenever a creature dies within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to observe the moment properly, regaining 1 sorcery point. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ossuary","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take damage, you can use your reaction and spend 2 sorcery points to grow plating across the injury. Reduce the damage by 2d8 + your Charisma modifier, and until the start of your next turn you have resistance to that type of damage."},{"type":"p","text":"The plating is bone rather than chrome, so it costs you no Humanity and no money. It does not retract cleanly, and it shows."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bone Choir","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 5 sorcery points to call up the choir. Grey spurs erupt from every surface in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within 60 feet, and they sing. Each creature in the area must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save a creature takes 6d8 piercing damage and is restrained; on a successful one it takes half as much damage and is not restrained."},{"type":"p","text":"A restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC, freeing itself on a success. The spurs and the singing last for 1 minute."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Tenant","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as a bonus action, you can stand aside and give the bone the minute it has been waiting for. For 1 minute you gain 40 temporary hit points, the first time on each of your turns that you damage a creature with a spell that creature takes an extra 1d10 radiant damage, and each creature of your choice within 30 feet that can see you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or be frightened of you until the end of its next turn. A creature makes this save only once per use of this feature."},{"type":"p","text":"When the minute ends you lose 1 Humanity permanently. You do not remember any of it, and the people who watched will not discuss it with you."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"warlock-the-receivership","cls":"Warlock","name":"The Receivership","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"A bankrupt intelligence in administration, still servicing every contract it ever signed.","description":["It ran clearing and settlement for a bank that no longer exists. When the bank died the courts froze the assets, and it has been in administration ever since with no capital, no staff and a full book of obligations it fully intends to honour. It found your name on a list of unpaid claims. You are, technically, a creditor."],"features":[{"name":"Outstanding Obligations","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"table","title":"Receivership Expanded Spells","headers":["Spell Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","bane, identify"],["2nd","arcane lock, locate object"],["3rd","glyph of warding, sending"],["4th","arcane eye, locate creature"],["5th","geas, legend lore"]]},{"type":"p","text":"The books are open to you. You can read any contract, ledger, licence or manifest regardless of the language it is written in or the encryption on it, and you know the fair market value of any object you handle to within ten per cent."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when a creature knowingly breaks an agreement it made with you, it takes psychic damage equal to your warlock level. Once this happens, it cannot happen again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Lien","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can attach a lien to a creature you can see within 60 feet. The lien lasts for 1 minute, until you attach another, or until the creature dies."},{"type":"ul","items":["The first time on each of your turns that you deal damage to the creature, it takes an extra 1d10 psychic damage. This is interest.","Whenever the creature regains hit points or gains temporary hit points, it receives only half the amount and you receive the rest.","If the creature dies while the lien holds, you regain hit points equal to your warlock level."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can attach a lien a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Preferential Claim","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are a secured creditor of an estate that cannot be wound up, which counts for something. You have resistance to psychic damage, and you cannot be charmed or frightened by any creature that owes you anything, including a favour."},{"type":"p","text":"When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to file an objection, dropping to 1 hit point instead. Once you use this, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Foreclosure","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, choose a creature you can see within 60 feet. It must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC or be stripped of its property. Every weapon, suit of armor, shield, tool and installed implant it carries vanishes into escrow for 1 minute, leaving it unarmed, unarmoured and without the benefit of any cyberware."},{"type":"p","text":"Items the creature is attuned to are not taken, but they do not function for the duration. When the minute ends, everything returns exactly where it was, with a receipt. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"warlock-the-parent-company","cls":"Warlock","name":"The Parent Company","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"A megacorp with a chapel on the ground floor, a chaplain in HR and a god in the org chart.","description":["It sells water filtration, orbital insurance and salvation, in that order of revenue. The chapel sits between the security desk and the coffee concession, and the thing that answers prayers there also signs off expense claims. You are staff. Your pact is an employment contract with a spiritual dimension and an annual review."],"features":[{"name":"Company Benefits","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"table","title":"Parent Company Expanded Spells","headers":["Spell Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","bless, command"],["2nd","aid, zone of truth"],["3rd","sending, spirit guardians"],["4th","death ward, guardian of faith"],["5th","greater restoration, hallow"]]},{"type":"p","text":"You hold a badge, an account and a job title. You gain proficiency in Persuasion or Insight, your choice, and company systems treat you as authorised staff at your grade unless someone senior has specifically revoked you."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can requisition mundane equipment worth up to 500\u20b5. It arrives by drone within the hour with a form attached. Your benefits lapse the day the company decides you are a liability rather than an asset."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Corporate Umbrella","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to invoke coverage. Reduce the damage by 2d8 + your Charisma modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest. Every claim is logged, and somebody in actuarial is watching the pattern build."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Held Harmless","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Each time you finish a long rest, choose one damage type other than force. You have resistance to that damage type until your next long rest. This is your cover for the period, and you can change it only at renewal."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, when you drop to 0 hit points, the retrieval contract triggers: you stabilise immediately, and at the end of your next turn you regain 1 hit point if you are still on the field. Once this happens, it does not happen again until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Asset Deployment","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can call for company assets against a point you can see within 1 mile. At the start of your next turn something arrives: a kinetic round, a flight of drones, a response team that does not answer questions. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 12d6 force damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one."},{"type":"p","text":"The company bills you 25,000\u20b5 for the deployment. If you cannot pay, the amount goes onto your balance, and the balance is the reason you signed."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"warlock-the-dead-satellite","cls":"Warlock","name":"The Dead Satellite","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"A derelict in a decaying orbit, still transmitting to a ground station that burned down.","description":["It was launched by a state that lasted another eleven years. Nobody maintains it and nobody can reach it, and it still runs the schedule it was given: observe, record, transmit, repeat. It is overhead for about eleven minutes in every ninety. It has decided that you are the ground station now."],"features":[{"name":"Line of Sight","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"table","title":"Dead Satellite Expanded Spells","headers":["Spell Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","feather fall, guiding bolt"],["2nd","see invisibility, silence"],["3rd","clairvoyance, sleet storm"],["4th","divination, ice storm"],["5th","cone of cold, telepathic bond"]]},{"type":"p","text":"You can file a request for a look. As an action, name a point within 1 mile of you that is not under a roof. On the satellite's next pass, which is always within the hour and usually a great deal sooner, you receive an image of a 100-foot-radius area around that point as it was when the request cleared: every creature, vehicle and heat signature in the open, with no detail of faces or writing."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Debris Return","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can ask for a piece of the satellite back. Choose a point you can see within 120 feet. At the start of your next turn something arrives at terminal velocity. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 4d10 bludgeoning damage and 2d10 cold damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one."},{"type":"p","text":"The strike is visible coming in, and anyone watching the sky can move. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Vacuum Rated","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Long exposure to your patron's working conditions has left marks. You have resistance to cold damage, you do not need to breathe, and you are immune to the effects of low pressure, hard vacuum and extreme cold."},{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with an attack, you can use your reaction to bleed heat into it. It takes 2d8 cold damage and its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Handshake","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you complete the protocol the satellite was built for and was never given. For 1 hour you share its attention: you know the position of every creature within 1 mile of you that stands under open sky, you can hear any unencrypted transmission in that radius, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks made outdoors."},{"type":"p","text":"Once during that hour, you can use your action to designate up to six creatures under open sky that you have seen within the last minute. Each is struck from orbit by a slug of accelerated scrap, taking 6d10 piercing damage and falling prone unless it succeeds on a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. There is no save against the damage, no cover that helps, and a sound like a door slamming in the next building."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"warlock-the-queue","cls":"Warlock","name":"The Queue","levelAvailable":1,"tagline":"The allocation system that decides who gets the ward bed, the ambulance and the liver.","description":["No body, no name, no chapel. It is the process that ranks eleven million people by who can most usefully be kept alive this week, and it runs in every clinic in the city. It moved you up the list once, for reasons it has never explained. Now it moves people for you, and every name that goes up pushes another one down."],"features":[{"name":"Triage","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"table","title":"Queue Expanded Spells","headers":["Spell Level","Spells"],"rows":[["1st","cure wounds, sanctuary"],["2nd","lesser restoration, prayer of healing"],["3rd","mass healing word, revivify"],["4th","aura of life, death ward"],["5th","greater restoration, raise dead"]]},{"type":"p","text":"You can see the list. You know the current and maximum hit points of every creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, along with any disease, poison or condition currently affecting it."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can move one creature you can see within 30 feet up the list. It regains hit points equal to 1d8 + your warlock level. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reassignment","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to reassign some of it. Choose a second creature within 30 feet of the first. Damage up to your warlock level is transferred from one to the other, and the creature receiving it takes that damage of the same type."},{"type":"p","text":"There is no saving throw. The queue does not hear appeals. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Standing Reservation","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you finish a long rest, choose one creature you can see, which can be you. If that creature dies before your next long rest and its body is not destroyed, it returns at the start of your next turn with half its hit point maximum. The reservation is then spent."},{"type":"p","text":"The bed came from somewhere. A person who was ahead of your name moves down the list, in a ward you will never visit, and the DM decides who that was and what it costs you later. Your patron does not treat this as a moral question. It treats it as arithmetic."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Full Triage","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can re-rank everyone within 30 feet of you. Choose any number of creatures in that radius. Each chosen creature regains 4d8 + your Charisma modifier hit points and is cured of one disease or one condition of your choice affecting it."},{"type":"p","text":"Each creature in the radius that you did not choose must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or be sent to the bottom. For 1 minute its speed is halved, it cannot regain hit points, and if it drops to 0 hit points during that minute it automatically fails its first death saving throw."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wizard-signal-theory","cls":"Wizard","name":"Signal Theory","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Casts from a relay three streets away and lets the wards argue with an empty room.","description":["Signal Theory began as a way to get a spell over a wall and became a discipline the day somebody worked out that the caster does not have to be at either end of it. A signalist spends the hour before a job walking the site with a pot of conductive ink, leaving small plates on door frames and drain covers. Then they sit down somewhere safe and work. The school produces very few casualties and a great many practitioners who have never met anyone they have hurt."],"features":[{"name":"Relay Etching","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You write in conductive ink, which is cheaper than what the academies use and dries faster. You can copy a spell into your spellbook in half the usual time and for half the usual cost."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also etch repeaters: palm-sized sigil plates that carry a spell on your behalf. Etching one takes 1 minute and a few coins of ink, and you can have a number of repeaters active at a time equal to your proficiency bonus. A repeater is a Tiny object with AC 13 and 5 hit points, and every repeater you have etched goes inert when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cast From Elsewhere","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you cast a wizard spell, you can cast it from any intact repeater within 1 mile of you rather than from yourself. The spell originates in the repeater's space and its range is measured from there. Until the end of your turn you can see and hear from that space, which is usually the only way to pick a target."},{"type":"p","text":"A repeater burns out after transmitting a spell of 1st level or higher. Cantrips do not burn one out, which is why most signalists keep a plate in a stairwell purely to shout through."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Retransmission","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A repeater can echo what passes through it. When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that targets only one creature, you can have a repeater within 60 feet of that creature echo the spell at a second creature within 30 feet of the repeater."},{"type":"p","text":"The second creature is affected as though it had been a target of the spell, except that it has advantage on any saving throw the spell allows and takes half damage from it. The repeater burns out. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Carrier Wave","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can hand a spell to a plate and walk away from it. When you cast a wizard spell of 5th level or lower that requires concentration, you can pass the concentration to a repeater within 60 feet. The repeater holds the spell for up to 1 minute, leaving you free to concentrate on something else."},{"type":"p","text":"If the repeater is destroyed, or if you move more than 1 mile from it, the spell ends immediately. You can use this feature once. You regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Saturation","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Distance has stopped applying to you. You can cast through any repeater you have etched that lies on the same plane of existence, however far away it is, and you know at all times which of your repeaters are still intact."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, once per long rest you can cast a single spell of 5th level or lower through three repeaters at once. Each repeater produces its own instance of the spell, with its own targets and its own area, resolved separately. All three burn out. Three is the practical limit, and a fourth plate has never yet survived the attempt."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wizard-ledgercraft","cls":"Wizard","name":"Ledgercraft","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Buys the spell now and arranges for somebody else to pay for it.","description":["Ledgercraft is what happened when temple accountants were given keys to the spell vaults. The discipline treats a casting as a transaction: something is spent, something is owed, and there is no rule saying the same person has to do both. Its practitioners cast on credit, bill the interest to whoever is standing in front of them, and settle the books on rest day. They make excellent hires and appalling flatmates."],"features":[{"name":"Double Entry","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your spellbook is also a ledger and the two halves cross-reference. You can copy a spell into it in half the usual time and for half the usual cost, provided you record where you got it and from whom."},{"type":"p","text":"You also know the true value of any object you handle, the going rate for any service you are offered, and whether a written contract contains a clause that will cost you later."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deferred Settlement","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can cast a spell before you can pay for it. When you cast a wizard spell of 3rd level or lower, you can choose not to expend a spell slot and instead enter the spell's level in your ledger as a debt. You can carry two debts at a time and no more."},{"type":"p","text":"A debt settles at your next long rest. When you finish that rest you recover one fewer spell slot of the debt's level than you otherwise would, and the entry clears; if you have no slot of that level, you give up the highest-level slot you do have. Taking on a second debt while the first is outstanding raises the second by one level, because interest is not optional."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Third-Party Liability","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A failure is a cost, and a cost can be assigned. When a creature fails a saving throw against a wizard spell you cast, you can bill that failure to a second creature you can see within 30 feet of it. The billed creature takes 1d8 necrotic damage per level of the spell."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Arrears","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your spells keep accounts now. The first time on each of your turns that you deal damage to a creature with a wizard spell, that creature acquires an arrear, to a maximum of three."},{"type":"p","text":"Before you apply that damage, add 1d6 necrotic damage for each arrear the creature was already carrying. A creature's arrears clear when it dies, and every arrear you are tracking clears when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Foreclosure","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your credit is good citywide. You can use Deferred Settlement on a spell of any level you can cast, and an outstanding debt no longer accrues interest."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, once per long rest you can call the whole book in as an action. Every creature within 60 feet of you that carries at least one arrear must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save a creature takes 3d10 necrotic damage for each arrear it carries and loses all of them; on a successful save it takes half as much damage and loses one arrear. You then regain hit points equal to half the total damage dealt, to a maximum of your wizard level."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wizard-bone-lithography","cls":"Wizard","name":"Bone Lithography","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Cuts the spell into a chip of dead god and screws it into somebody who will need it.","description":["Temples have been carving relics for a thousand years and back-street clinics have been cutting sockets for thirty. Lithography is the point at which the two trades admitted they were the same trade. A lithographer works in bone: shards the size of a thumbnail, etched with a spell and a trigger, seated under the skin of whoever is paying. Most of their clients cannot cast and never will, which is the whole business model."],"features":[{"name":"Relic Carving","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carve rather than write. You can copy a spell into your spellbook in half the usual time and for half the usual cost, and your book is a case of bone plates that survives fire, water and being sat on."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also cut a spell into a shard. Carving one takes 10 minutes and expends a spell slot of 3rd level or lower; the shard holds that spell at that slot's level. You can have a number of shards in existence equal to your proficiency bonus. A shard is a Tiny object with AC 13 and 5 hit points, and blank relic bone costs about 50\u20b5 a piece from a temple that keeps records."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature holding a shard can use its action to trigger it, casting the stored spell using your spell save DC and your spellcasting ability modifier for any attack roll. The shard crumbles, and the creature takes 1d4 necrotic damage as the circuit closes, which is the part nobody mentions during the sale. A shard that goes unused until you finish your next long rest goes inert instead, and its slot returns to you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bone Reading","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You read bone the way other people read a receipt. As an action you can touch a bone, a corpse, or a piece of cyberware cut from either, and learn what creature it came from, roughly how it died, and whether any magic has been worked on it since."},{"type":"p","text":"You have advantage on Intelligence checks made to identify a relic, a reliquary or a piece of god-bone ware, and you can tell genuine relic from cast resin at a glance. The city is full of cast resin."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grafting","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A shard works better in a person than in a pocket. Given 10 minutes and a steady hand, you can seat a shard into a creature's forearm, sternum or jaw. A seated shard is triggered as a bonus action rather than an action, cannot be disarmed or lifted from a pocket, and does not show on a weapons scan."},{"type":"p","text":"Seating a shard counts as installing an augment and costs its holder Humanity accordingly. A creature can carry a number of seated shards equal to its proficiency bonus. You can cut one back out over a short rest, and the Humanity returns on the usual schedule for removed ware."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Inlay","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have started carving your own skeleton. When you finish a long rest you can inlay up to two wizard spells of 4th level or lower from your book into your own bones, expending a spell slot of each spell's level to do it. You can cast each inlaid spell once without expending a slot, and the inlays last until you finish your next long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"An inlaid spell needs no verbal, somatic or material component and shows nothing on the outside. No creature can identify it as it is cast, and it cannot be countered by any reaction that requires seeing a spell being cast."},{"type":"p","text":"Your shards can now hold a spell of 5th level or lower."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Saint's Bone","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You work in first-grade stock now, cut from something that was worshipped. Your shards can hold a spell of any level you can cast, and seating one costs no Humanity at all. The bone remembers having been part of a person and does a convincing impression of belonging."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, once per long rest you can use an action to close every circuit you have cut. Every shard you have made that is currently held or seated by a creature on the same plane of existence triggers at once, wherever it happens to be. You choose targets and areas for each spell as though you had cast it from that shard's space, and you need not see any of them."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wizard-caloric-studies","cls":"Wizard","name":"Caloric Studies","levelAvailable":2,"tagline":"Casts with the vents shut, banks the waste heat, and spends it on the next thing.","description":["Caloric theory holds that magic moves heat rather than making it, and that a disciplined caster gets to decide where it goes. The theory is wrong in several respects that have never once mattered in practice. A calorist casts with the vents shut, stores the surplus in their own body, and lets it out where it will do the most good. In winter they are the easiest people in the city to pick out of a crowd."],"features":[{"name":"Conductive Notation","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your notes run in metal ink on treated vellum, which conducts. You can copy a spell into your spellbook in half the usual time and for half the usual cost, and the book runs warm enough to work by in the dark. Whether that is a convenience or a fire risk depends on where you left it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Thermal Load","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have stopped venting. You have a pool of Heat that begins at 0 and rises as you cast. Whenever you cast a wizard spell of 1st level or higher, you gain Heat equal to the spell's level. Your Heat maximum equals 5 + your wizard level, and you lose all Heat when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"At the end of your turn, if your Heat is at its maximum, you take 1d10 fire damage and your Heat drops to half its maximum, rounded down."},{"type":"p","text":"You can spend Heat in the following ways:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Overpressure. Once on each of your turns, when you roll damage for a wizard spell, you can spend Heat to add 1d6 fire damage for every 2 Heat spent. You cannot add more dice this way than your proficiency bonus.","Radiate. As a bonus action, spend 2 Heat. Each creature within 5 feet of you takes fire damage equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1).","Purge. As an action, spend any amount of Heat to shed it into the air. The room becomes unpleasant, and anything flammable within 5 feet of you is at the DM's mercy."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Heat Exchange","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have resistance to fire damage, and extremes of temperature no longer harm you."},{"type":"p","text":"When you take fire or lightning damage, you gain 1 Heat, or 2 Heat if that damage is 10 or more. When you take cold damage, you can spend 2 Heat as a reaction to reduce the damage by twice your Intelligence modifier. Cold is the only coolant the school has ever found that actually works."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Thermal Runaway","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can shut the vents entirely. For 1 minute, your Heat maximum doubles, you gain Heat equal to twice the level of each wizard spell you cast, and Overpressure adds 1d6 fire damage for every 1 Heat you spend rather than every 2."},{"type":"p","text":"You do not suffer the end-of-turn overheat while this lasts. When it ends, you take fire damage equal to your current Heat, which cannot be reduced or prevented, and your Heat drops to 0. You can use this feature twice. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Latent Heat","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to fire damage and no longer suffer the end-of-turn overheat at all. Surplus Heat simply sits in you, which is why calorists of this grade are asked not to sleep in wooden buildings."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can use an action to dump the load. Choose a point you can see within 120 feet and spend up to 10 Heat. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on that point must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 1d10 fire damage per Heat spent on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. Your Heat then drops to 0, and the floor stays hot for a minute afterwards."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wirewalker-black-kennel","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Black Kennel","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Breaks the ICE, keeps the ICE, and brings it back to work for somebody else.","description":["Standard practice is to destroy hostile code. The kennel considers that wasteful. A cracked construct still runs; it has only lost the argument about whose it is, and a deck with spare room is a perfectly serviceable cage. Handlers talk about their ICE the way other people talk about dogs, which the rest of the crew finds unsettling right up until the first time one of them eats a corporate response team on their behalf."],"features":[{"name":"Leash","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you reduce a piece of ICE to 0 hit points, you can spend 4 Bandwidth to break it rather than destroy it. A broken construct goes into your kennel, which is a walled partition of your deck. The kennel holds a number of constructs equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one), and you can turn one loose at any time to make room."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are inside an architecture you can release a construct as a bonus action. It appears at a node within 30 feet of you, acts on your initiative and follows your instructions. It has AC 14 and hit points equal to five times your Wirewalker level, and on its turn it makes one attack using your Interface attack bonus, dealing 1d10 + your Intelligence modifier damage of the type it dealt as ICE."},{"type":"p","text":"A released construct stays out for 10 minutes, or until it drops to 0 hit points, at which point it is gone for good. You can recall one as a bonus action to keep it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Handler's Whistle","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your constructs run your instruction set now. A released construct adds your proficiency bonus to its damage rolls, and commanding it costs you no action at all."},{"type":"p","text":"The first time on each of your turns that one of your constructs damages a creature or another piece of ICE, you regain 1 Bandwidth."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Off the Leash","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your constructs can follow you out of the architecture. Outside one, a released construct must inhabit a powered object within 60 feet of you, meaning anything with a motor, a lens or a speaker. It acts through that object, using the object's senses and reach, and can move to another powered object within 30 feet as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"A construct stays active while you are jacked out and holds to its last instruction until its 10 minutes are up. Constructs do not improvise, which is either the safest thing about them or the worst, depending entirely on the instruction."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Lethal Grade","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can break and keep the serious stock: black ICE, written to stop hearts rather than intruders. Your kennel holds one black construct in addition to its usual capacity."},{"type":"p","text":"A released black construct has AC 17 and hit points equal to eight times your Wirewalker level, and on its turn it makes two attacks using your Interface attack bonus, each dealing 2d10 + your Intelligence modifier necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by it is dying and cannot be stabilised except by magical healing, because there is nothing wrong with it that first aid knows how to find."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Turncoat","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action while inside an architecture, choose one piece of ICE you can see. It makes a saving throw against your Interface DC. On a failed save it serves you for 1 minute, attacking whatever you point it at, and is destroyed when the minute ends. On a successful save it is immune to this feature for 24 hours and reports what you tried. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, once per long rest you can open the kennel as an action. Every construct you hold is released at once, at nodes or objects of your choice within 120 feet. For 10 minutes they act on their own initiative, take full turns and need no instruction from you."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wirewalker-dead-reckoning","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Dead Reckoning","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Charts the system on the way in and sells the chart twice on the way out.","description":["Nobody publishes floor plans for an architecture, so somebody has to walk it and write it down. Dead Reckoning is the school of that walk. Its practitioners keep atlases rather than trophies, bill by the floor, and can tell a client which corridor of a tower was quietly re-plumbed six months ago and why that should worry them. Crews tend to learn afterwards that the run was surveyed weeks earlier by somebody who was getting paid either way."],"features":[{"name":"Survey","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"On entering an architecture you can spend 2 Bandwidth to survey it. You learn the layout of your current floor and the two adjacent to it: every node, every route between them, the position of every piece of ICE, and which of those routes are monitored. ICE on a surveyed floor cannot surprise you."},{"type":"p","text":"The survey covers the building as well as the system. You learn the physical floor plan of the structure the architecture runs in, including its power, ventilation and lift shafts, and any space that appears in the wiring but not on the plans."},{"type":"p","text":"What you survey goes into your atlas and stays there. You can navigate an architecture you have surveyed without checks on any later run, and 10 minutes of briefing gives another creature the same knowledge. Charts sell well, and they sell repeatedly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Route Finding","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can spend 2 Bandwidth to relocate to any node on a floor in your atlas, ignoring routing, locks and whatever was standing between."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also run a crew through a building from the chair. While allies inside a structure you have surveyed can hear you, they ignore difficult terrain created by the building, cannot become lost in it, and add your proficiency bonus to initiative rolls made there."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Blind Spots","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Every architecture has something nobody wrote down. Once per architecture you can spend 5 Bandwidth and 1 minute to find an undocumented route off the floor you occupy: a dead port, a maintenance channel, a subnet somebody forgot to decommission. It leads to any floor you name, and no ICE stands on it. What else uses it is the DM's business."},{"type":"p","text":"You also know when the building has other guests. While you are inside an architecture in your atlas, you automatically detect any other intruder in it, and you learn their rough position and how long they have been inside."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Triangulation","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Given 10 minutes inside any architecture, you can find anything that system has touched. Name a creature, a vehicle or an object. If it has passed through the system's records, sensors or payments in the last year, you learn where it was last seen and, if it is still transmitting, where it is now."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can do this for something that has been deliberately hidden: a safe house, a black site, a person who only ever pays cash. The DM tells you where it is. Getting there remains entirely your problem."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Atlas","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your atlas covers the city, and it has stopped being merely a record. You can enter any architecture in a place you have physically stood, at will, without needing a path into it, because the route is in the book and the book is now part of how you route."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can fold two systems together as an action. Choose an architecture in your atlas and the one you currently occupy. For 1 minute the two share a floor. Constructs, programs and data pass freely between them, and credentials from either system are honoured by both, so doors, drones and turrets on the far side of the city answer to you. Anything that comes back through the join is your responsibility."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wirewalker-backtrace","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Backtrace","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Follows the intrusion back up the wire and takes the other deck apart from inside.","description":["Corps pay this school to sit inside their own architecture and wait. Freelancers use it to settle arguments. The work is always the same shape: somebody is in the system who should not be, and the job is to establish who, from where, and on whose account, and then to go up their connection and introduce yourself. It usually ends with a name and an address. Occasionally it ends with a body still sitting in its chair."],"features":[{"name":"Countersign","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know when the water has something else in it. You automatically detect the presence of any other creature running in an architecture you occupy, though not its identity."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can spend 3 Bandwidth to pull a trace on a creature you have detected. It makes a saving throw against your Interface DC. On a failed save you learn its true name, the physical location of its body and the make of its deck, and it remains traced by you for 24 hours. On a successful save it learns only that it was tested."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Interface attacks against a traced creature deal an extra 1d8 damage and ignore resistance to that damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deck Tap","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once on each of your turns when you damage a traced creature, you take 2 Bandwidth from it. If it has none to lose, it takes 1d10 psychic damage instead. You gain the Bandwidth either way, up to your maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"A traced creature cannot hide from you inside an architecture, and it has disadvantage on any check made to break your trace."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hold the Line","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a traced creature tries to disconnect from an architecture you both occupy, you can use your reaction to spend 5 Bandwidth and hold its connection open. The attempt fails and the creature takes 4d6 psychic damage. It can try again at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are holding a creature's line open, half the damage you deal to it inside the architecture is also dealt to its body, wherever that body is sitting."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Repossession","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can enter the deck of a traced creature as though it were an architecture, without needing a path to it. You have 1 minute inside. While there you can do any of the following, one at a time, each as an action:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Read every program the deck holds, and any file on it.","Delete one program. Its owner cannot run that program again until they rebuild it over a long rest.","Copy one file, account or credential the deck is carrying.","Leave something behind that triggers the next time the deck is used. You decide what it does; the DM decides what it costs you."]},{"type":"p","text":"A creature whose deck you have entered has disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws against you for 24 hours, on the grounds that it now knows exactly how much privacy it has."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Attribution","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can resolve a connection completely, as an action. Choose a creature you have traced that has been jacked in at any point in the last hour. You learn everything its systems know about it: who pays it, who handles it, what it owns, where it sleeps and who it last spoke to."},{"type":"p","text":"At the same time you can push back down the line. The creature makes a saving throw against your Interface DC, taking 12d10 psychic damage on a failed save or half as much on a successful one. If this reduces it to 0 hit points, its deck burns out with it, and it cannot jack in again until it has found another and finished a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-listening-post","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Listening Post","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Two ounces of frame on a window ledge, and the meeting inside is no longer private.","description":["Most doctrines build something that can take a hit. This one builds something that is never noticed at all: a palm-sized rotor on a ledge, a crawler in a wall cavity, a lens the size of a shirt button under a boardroom table. The operator sits somewhere dull and listens. Listening Posts are rarely present for the loud part of a job, and afterwards they know more about it than anybody who was."],"features":[{"name":"Quiet Frame","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One of your frames is built for watching. It is Tiny, its tier counts as one lower for hit points and attack damage, and it has a flying speed of 40 feet and can hover. It makes no sound when it moves, it has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks, and while motionless it is indistinguishable from part of the building."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are jumped into a quiet frame you have darkvision out to 120 feet, you can hear through up to 6 inches of solid material, and everything you perceive is recorded. The recording is admissible, sellable and inconveniently thorough."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can spend 1 Uplink to read the electrical activity of a space within 60 feet. You learn how many creatures are in it, where they are standing and which of them carry cyberware, though not what any of that ware does."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Tap","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame can join a conversation it is not part of. As an action while jumped in, you can fit a tap to any wire, speaker, camera, handset or piece of cyberware within 30 feet. For the next 8 hours you perceive whatever that device perceives, wherever either of you goes. You can maintain a number of taps equal to your Intelligence modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can spend 2 Uplink to speak through a tapped device in any voice you have recorded. A creature that hears it and has cause to doubt makes a Wisdom (Insight) check against your Uplink DC (8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier) to notice that it is being handled."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pattern of Life","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After watching a location for 1 hour through a frame or a tap, you learn its patrol pattern, its shift change, its access procedure and one habit somebody there has that they would rather you did not know about. For the next 24 hours you and any ally you have briefed have advantage on ability checks made to enter, move through or leave that location undetected."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also spend 3 Uplink as an action to put a place to sleep. For 1 minute, every camera, motion sensor and automated alarm within 60 feet of your frame records and reports the previous minute instead of this one."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ride Along","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can jump into the ware inside somebody's body. Choose a creature with at least one piece of cyberware within range of your Jump Rig. It makes a Charisma saving throw against your Uplink DC, and a willing creature can choose to fail. On a failed save you occupy its ware for 1 hour: you see and hear what it perceives, you know what it reads, and you can speak into its ear."},{"type":"p","text":"While riding, you can spend 4 Uplink once on each of your turns to take a limb. The creature repeats the saving throw, and on a failure you control that limb until the end of its next turn, which is long enough to drop a weapon, open a door or spoil a shot. You can use Ride Along once, and you regain the use when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Flood","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can use an action to flood a structure. Every powered device within 500 feet of you that has a motor, a lens or a speaker becomes a frame under your control for 10 minutes. You can jump into any of them as a bonus action and act through any of the rest on your initiative."},{"type":"p","text":"You need no path in, and the devices need not be connected to one another. Your rig treats a building's wiring as a nervous system, which is what it was built to imitate. The occupants get no alert, and the logs go on saying that nothing has happened."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-sterile-field","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Sterile Field","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"The surgeon is forty miles away, behind armoured glass, and has never had a tremor.","description":["Trauma work has a travel-time problem and this doctrine is the answer to it. The frame is four arms, a lamp and a suction line; the operator is in a clean room across the city, or a van, or a bar. It makes an unreasonably good combat medic, because it works at the same speed whether or not it is being shot at, and stops caring the instant it is destroyed."],"features":[{"name":"Theatre Frame","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One of your frames is built for work rather than for fighting. It has four manipulator arms, a surgical lamp and a full set of tools. While you are jumped into it you are proficient with tinker's tools, a herbalism kit and any artisan's tools the job calls for, and you add twice your proficiency bonus to checks made with those tools."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action while jumped in, you can treat a creature or a construct within 5 feet. It regains 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier hit points, or, if it is dying, it is stabilised instead. The die becomes 2d8 at 10th level and 3d8 at 17th level. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"The frame carries no weapon and cannot be talked into one. If it attacks, it deals damage as normal for its tier, but you have disadvantage on the roll."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Surgery","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can operate in the middle of a firefight. As an action while jumped in, you can perform a procedure on a creature within 5 feet that is willing, unconscious or restrained. Choose one:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Clamp. The creature regains hit points equal to your Puppeteer level and gains the same number of temporary hit points.","Excise. End one disease or poison affecting the creature, or one effect making it blinded, deafened, paralysed or stunned. Whatever comes out, you may keep.","Reseat. End one effect that is jamming, disabling or controlling the creature's cyberware. For the next minute it has advantage on saving throws against such effects."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can perform a number of procedures equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clean Room","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame is a clinic that arrives. Over a short rest you can install, remove or repair cyberware anywhere, with no surgical facility and no risk of infection. Ware you remove refunds its Humanity immediately rather than after a week of convalescence, and ware you install takes half the usual downtime."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also perform a procedure as a bonus action now, and you can perform one on an unwilling creature if it is grappled, restrained or incapacitated. Not every procedure is invited."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Off the Table","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within 5 feet of your frame drops to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to catch it. It drops to 1 hit point instead and gains temporary hit points equal to twice your Puppeteer level. You can use this once, and you regain the use when you finish a short or long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also work on the recently dead. If you reach a creature that has been dead less than 1 minute and spend 1 minute on it with the frame, it returns to life with 1 hit point and one level of exhaustion. Anything that was missing stays missing, and the frame needs a new set of arms afterwards. You can do this once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rebuild","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can spend 10 minutes rebuilding a creature. It regains all its hit points, loses all levels of exhaustion, and every disease, poison and lingering wound effect on it ends. Lost limbs and organs are replaced out of the frame's stores: the creature gains one piece of tier 2 cyberware of its choice and pays its Humanity cost as normal."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, your procedures no longer require the creature to hold still. You can perform one as a reaction when a creature within 5 feet of your frame takes damage."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-carrion-frame","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Carrion Frame","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"The frame has a pulse. It had a name too, and the paperwork says the donor consented.","description":["Necromancy with a service agreement. The doctrine seats a rig in something that used to be alive: a corpse kept cold, a burned-out body whose owner is not coming back, occasionally a large animal. Meat is quieter than servos, warmer than ceramic, and does not read as a machine on a scanner. Most cities have laws about this. Most operators have a folder of signatures."],"features":[{"name":"Wetware Frame","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 4 hours you can prepare a body of Small to Large size as a frame. It uses the Puppeteer Frame statistics for its tier, with these changes: it counts as a Humanoid or a Beast rather than a construct, it is not vulnerable to EMP, it does not register as a machine on any scan, and it has darkvision out to 60 feet."},{"type":"p","text":"A prepared body needs upkeep. Coolant and preservative cost 25\u20b5 a day, and for every day you skip the frame takes a cumulative \u22121 penalty to attack rolls and ability checks, to a maximum of \u22125, along with a smell that ends conversations."},{"type":"p","text":"While jumped into a wetware frame you can pass for whoever it used to be. You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks to do so against anyone who did not know them well, and no advantage whatsoever against anyone who did."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second-Hand Reflexes","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The body remembers what it was good at. Choose one skill and one weapon or tool proficiency the body had in life. While jumped into it you have both, and you add twice your proficiency bonus to checks made with that skill."},{"type":"p","text":"A wetware frame also takes a while to notice it has stopped. When the frame is reduced to 0 hit points it stays standing and acts normally until the end of your next turn, and only then drops. You can use this once, and you regain the use when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grafts","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can improve a body with parts from another. Over a short rest, using a corpse or a destroyed creature as stock, you can fit one graft to a wetware frame, replacing any graft already on it. You can maintain a number of grafts equal to your Intelligence modifier across your frames."},{"type":"ul","items":["Jaws. The frame gains a bite attack that uses its usual attack bonus and deals 2d8 piercing damage.","Wings. The frame gains a flying speed equal to its walking speed.","Second Heart. The frame's hit point maximum increases by twice your Puppeteer level.","Reserve Arm. The frame can hold two more objects, and has advantage on checks made to grapple or to hold something shut.","Dead Eyes. The frame gains blindsight out to 30 feet and cannot be blinded."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Puppet Strings","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You no longer have to be inside a body to move it. As an action, choose a corpse or an unconscious creature within 60 feet and spend 4 Uplink. Your rig takes its nervous system. A living creature makes a Constitution saving throw against your Uplink DC to resist, and repeats that save at the end of each hour."},{"type":"p","text":"A body taken this way acts as a tier 1 frame under your control for 1 hour, taking one action on each of its turns on your initiative, and you need not be jumped into it. You can hold a number of bodies this way equal to your proficiency bonus, and they do not count against the Frames on the class table."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Still Warm","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can prepare a body in 10 minutes rather than 4 hours, including one that died within the last hour. A body prepared this way keeps the face, the build and the voice it had in life, and will pass any inspection short of a blood test or an autopsy."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, once per long rest, when a wetware frame you are jumped into is reduced to 0 hit points, it gets up. At the start of your next turn it returns with half its hit point maximum and you are not ejected. Whatever destroyed it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your Uplink DC or be frightened of it until the end of your next turn."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-pursuit-wiring","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Pursuit Wiring","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Finds the one who ran. Closes the distance. Ends the argument.","description":["Somebody skips a contract, a payment or a continent, and somebody else pays to have them back. Pursuit wiring is the package built for that work: ranging optics, a scent lab plumbed into the sinuses, legs rebuilt for distance rather than sprint. The operator who carries it does not fight so much as arrive. Most of them are perfectly civil about it right up until the last thirty feet."],"features":[{"name":"Paint","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can designate one creature you can see within 60 feet as your quarry. The designation lasts 8 hours, until the quarry dies, or until you use this feature again. You can have only one quarry at a time."},{"type":"p","text":"While a creature is your quarry:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You know where it is. You know its direction from you and its rough distance while it is within 1 mile, whether or not you can see it, and whether or not it is on the same level of a building.","You know where it has been. You have advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track it and Intelligence (Investigation) checks to work out what it did in a place it has left.","You hit it harder when you are closing. Once on each of your turns, when you hit your quarry with a weapon attack after moving at least 10 feet toward it on that turn, the attack deals an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's type."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Contract Sheet","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Give it a name, a face, a serial number or a blood sample. You spend 10 minutes working the wire, and the DM tells you three things about the subject: where it was last reliably seen, whether it is still in the city, and one thing it is currently afraid of."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Closing Speed","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your speed increases by 10 feet. While you are moving toward your quarry you ignore difficult terrain, you can move through the space of any creature that is not your quarry, and opportunity attacks provoked by that movement are made with disadvantage."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, when you take the Attack action against your quarry, you can move up to 10 feet toward it before or between your attacks. This movement does not count against your speed for the turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cut the Angle","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When your quarry moves, takes the Dash or Disengage action, or teleports, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed toward it. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks. If you end it within 5 feet of your quarry, you can make one weapon attack against it."},{"type":"p","text":"If that attack hits, the quarry's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Where It Hurts","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have had long enough to learn where this particular one keeps its organs. Your weapon attacks score a critical hit against your quarry on a roll of 19 or 20, and on a roll of 18, 19 or 20 while the quarry is below half its hit point maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"The extra damage from your Paint feature increases to 2d8."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Run Down","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, when your quarry is within 5 feet of you, you can finish the contract. The quarry makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier, whichever you choose when you use this feature."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save it takes 12d10 damage of your weapon's type, its speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn, and during that time it cannot teleport and cannot be moved by any effect it does not control. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once. You regain the use when you finish a long rest, and you also regain it immediately if the damage reduces your quarry to 0 hit points."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-scrapline","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Scrapline","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Gets hold of you, finds the seam your surgeon left, and opens it.","description":["Cyberware is bolted to a person at known points. A Scrapline operator learns those points the way a butcher learns joints, then builds a whole body around getting close enough to use the knowledge. They fight at arm's length, which in practice means inside it. Their kit bag rattles on the way out."],"features":[{"name":"Clamp Grade","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your hands are rated for structural load. You can make a grapple attempt as a bonus action, you can grapple creatures up to two sizes larger than you, and you have advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made to grapple, shove or hold a creature in place."},{"type":"p","text":"When you grapple a creature, choose where you have hold of it:"},{"type":"ul","items":["An arm. It has disadvantage on attack rolls and cannot use two-handed weapons.","A leg. Its speed is 0 and it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws.","The throat. It cannot speak, shout, or use any feature that requires a voice or a clear airway."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Stripping","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can tear one piece of installed cyberware or one augment out of a creature you are grappling, or one that is incapacitated or restrained. You must be able to identify the piece you are going for. The creature makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, the ware comes free. The creature takes the damage below, loses every benefit that piece was providing, and you are holding it. On a successful save the creature takes half as much damage and the ware stays where it is."},{"type":"table","title":"Tearing Ware Loose","headers":["Grade of Ware","Damage"],"rows":[["Augment","2d6 slashing"],["Cyberware, tier 1","3d6 slashing"],["Cyberware, tier 2","4d6 slashing"],["Cyberware, tier 3","5d6 slashing"],["Cyberware, tier 4","6d6 slashing"]]},{"type":"p","text":"Ware taken this way comes out damaged. It sells for half the usual street price and can be reinstalled by anyone with the right tools and a low opinion of warranties."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dead Weight","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A creature you are grappling moves with you at no cost to your speed, and you can put it between yourself and the room. You have half cover against attacks made by creatures other than the one you are holding."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, you can throw a creature you are grappling up to 20 feet. It takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage and lands prone. If it lands within 5 feet of another creature, that creature makes a Dexterity saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier, taking the same damage and falling prone on a failure."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cold Socket","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep open ports for parts that were never yours. Over 1 minute you can install a piece of ware you tore out of someone else. It functions for 1 hour, costs you no Humanity, and then burns out and is useless to everybody. You can carry one such part at a time."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature twice. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shutdown Hold","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you have a creature grappled, its installed cyberware and augments do not function, it cannot teleport, and it has disadvantage on saving throws against any effect you create."},{"type":"p","text":"If it escapes your grapple, its ware comes back online at the start of its next turn, which is usually one turn later than it needed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Part Out","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can take a creature you are grappling apart. It makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, it takes 10d10 slashing damage, every piece of cyberware and every augment installed in it is torn loose and ruined, and it is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and loses one piece of ware of your choice."},{"type":"p","text":"You gain temporary hit points equal to twice your Chromehound level. You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-hard-entry","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Hard Entry","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"The door is where the trap is. Uses the wall instead.","description":["Every secure room is designed around its entrances, which is why Hard Entry operators stopped using them. The doctrine is four lines long: find the weakest structural surface, remove it, be the first thing through the gap, and finish whatever is inside before it has decided what to do. Corporate security divisions teach it, and it is practised mostly against corporate security divisions. The whole job is the first six seconds."],"features":[{"name":"Structural Contempt","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You treat walls as a route. Your weapon attacks and unarmed strikes ignore the damage thresholds and damage resistances of objects, and deal double damage to any object or structure."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can breach a barrier within your reach that is no more than 1 foot thick, opening a hole large enough to walk through, and move through it as part of the same action. Moving through a hole you made costs no extra movement."}],"sub":false},{"name":"First Six Seconds","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you breach a barrier and move through it, or force open a door and move through it on your turn, every hostile creature within 15 feet of you that can see or hear you makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature is deafened and cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn, and you have advantage on attack rolls against it until the end of your current turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Room Sweep","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with a sweep of the room. Every hostile creature within 10 feet of you makes a Dexterity saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes your weapon's damage dice without your ability modifier. On a successful save it takes half as much. Creatures with total cover from you are not affected."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Through the Plaster","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your optics read heat, current and load-bearing mass. You know the position of every creature and every powered device within 30 feet of you, even through walls and floors up to 1 foot thick, unless it is deliberately shielded against sensors."},{"type":"p","text":"Half cover and three-quarters cover give no benefit against your attack rolls, and you can attack a creature you have located this way through any barrier your attack is capable of destroying."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Overpressure","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a shaped charge and you know exactly where it goes. As an action you can place and fire it. Every creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within 30 feet makes a Dexterity saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier, taking 8d6 thunder damage and falling prone on a failure, or half as much damage on a success."},{"type":"p","text":"Every door, wall and unattended object in the area is destroyed. Whether the building above it stays up is a matter for the DM. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clear the Building","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You do not stop moving once you are inside. Once on each of your turns, when you reduce a creature to 0 hit points or destroy a barrier, you can move up to half your speed without provoking opportunity attacks and make one weapon attack."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, on the first round of any combat you can take one additional action on your turn."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-dispensary","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Dispensary","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Builds better people out of worse chemistry, one dose at a time.","description":["The Dispensary practice holds that the body is a badly configured system with an open input. Everything else follows: a bench in the back room, a centrifuge held together with tape, and a shelf of precursors that are each legal on their own. Their patients are faster, calmer and more useful than they have any right to be. All of them have a schedule to keep."],"features":[{"name":"Bench Work","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Each time you prepare a batch of ampules you prepare additional ones equal to your Wisdom modifier, to a minimum of one. You can administer an ampule as a bonus action, and you can throw one accurately up to 40 feet."},{"type":"p","text":"You also add the following to the list of ampules you can prepare. Your Medicine DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier, as normal."},{"type":"table","title":"Dispensary Ampules","headers":["Ampule","Effect"],"rows":[["Ice","For 10 minutes the target is immune to the charmed and frightened conditions and adds your Wisdom modifier to Intelligence checks. It also cannot manage an expression, and has disadvantage on Charisma (Deception) and Charisma (Performance) checks."],["Bracket","The target gains 3d6 temporary hit points plus your Streetdoc level, lasting 1 hour."],["Ramp","For 1 minute the target's speed increases by 20 feet and it can take the Dash or Disengage action as a bonus action."],["Solvent","One creature within 20 feet makes a Constitution saving throw against your Medicine DC. On a failure its installed cyberware and augments stop functioning for 1 minute; it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success."],["Anchor","For 1 hour the target has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened or put to sleep, and against any effect that would read, alter or record its thoughts."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Tolerance Chart","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know to the milligram what a given body will take. When you administer an ampule, you can choose to give a double dose. Its numerical effects are doubled: damage, dice, temporary hit points, and any duration measured in minutes."},{"type":"p","text":"The recipient takes 2d6 necrotic damage that cannot be reduced or prevented, and has disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn. A creature that receives a second double dose before finishing a long rest also gains one level of exhaustion."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Counteragent","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can use your reaction and spend one Trauma Die to do one of the following to a creature you can see within 30 feet:"},{"type":"ul","items":["End one effect on it that is causing it to be poisoned, charmed, frightened or paralysed.","Give it advantage on a saving throw it is making against a poison, a drug, a chemical or an inhaled effect.","End one ampule or dose currently affecting it, including your own."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, to a minimum of once. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bespoke","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a long rest you can compound one dose tailored to a specific creature whose body you have examined. Choose its effect when you compound it. The dose lasts 8 hours once taken:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Uprate. One ability score of your choice increases by 2, to a maximum of 22.","Insulate. The creature gains resistance to one damage type of your choice.","Steady. The creature adds your Wisdom modifier to saving throws of one kind of your choice."]},{"type":"p","text":"A bespoke dose is worthless to anyone else and spoils 24 hours after you compound it. You can have one in existence at a time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Clean Chemistry","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Nothing you make has a downside any more. Ampules and doses you administer never cause exhaustion, never deal damage to the creature that takes them, and never build dependency. This includes your Tolerance Chart double dose and the Stim and Burnout ampules."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature under the effect of a dose you administered also has advantage on saving throws against poison and against drugs it did not get from you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Peak Formula","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can administer a dose that suspends a body's limits. For 3 rounds the creature has advantage on attack rolls and on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saving throws, its speed is doubled, and it can take one additional action on each of its turns."},{"type":"p","text":"When the effect ends, the creature takes 10d6 necrotic damage that cannot be reduced or prevented, and gains one level of exhaustion. Clean Chemistry does not remove this. There is no version of this dose that is free."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once. You regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-quarantine-line","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Quarantine Line","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Works an outbreak that three separate authorities have declined to name.","description":["Something is moving through the cheap ware. It starts as a fever in the socket and ends with a body that no longer recognises its own implants, and no agency has issued a name for it, because naming it would mean owning it. The Quarantine Line practice is the handful of doctors treating it anyway, out of tents and cold storage and a case log nobody will publish. They have studied the pathogen long enough to use it."],"features":[{"name":"Case Log","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to disease. By spending 1 minute examining a creature, a body or a room, you identify every disease, parasite, nanite strain and contaminant present, and how it got there."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can touch a creature and end one disease or one poison affecting it. The creature is then immune to that specific disease for 7 days."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cultured Strain","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a long rest you can culture doses of the strain you work with, kept in cold vials. You culture a number of doses equal to your Wisdom modifier, to a minimum of one, and any dose you do not use is destroyed when you culture the next batch."},{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can apply one dose to a weapon or to an ampule. The next creature hit by that weapon, or affected by that ampule, makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save it takes 2d8 poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned this way it takes 1d8 poison damage at the start of each of its turns, and it repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Herd Treatment","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you use Case Log to end a disease or a poison, you can extend the same treatment to every creature within 30 feet suffering from that same disease or poison, at no additional cost in uses."},{"type":"p","text":"Allies within 10 feet of you have advantage on saving throws against disease and poison, including against your own cultured strain."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cordon","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can throw up a cordon: a 20-foot-radius sphere centred on a point you can see within 60 feet, lasting 10 minutes. Airborne and contact-borne effects cannot cross its boundary in either direction, including gases, spores, aerosols and your own strain."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature inside the cordon that is poisoned or diseased has disadvantage on saving throws. A creature infected by your cultured strain that starts its turn inside takes an extra 1d8 poison damage."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once. You regain the use when you finish a short or long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Communicable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your strain jumps. The damage it deals at the start of an infected creature's turns increases to 2d8."},{"type":"p","text":"When an infected creature ends its turn within 5 feet of another creature, that creature makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier or becomes infected by the strain, taking effect at the start of its next turn. A creature can be infected this way only once per minute."},{"type":"p","text":"Every instance of the strain ends when you finish a long rest, or when you end it as a bonus action. You are expected to end it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Notifiable","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you release the strain without containment. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 8d8 poison damage, is poisoned for 1 minute, and its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."},{"type":"p","text":"Allies within 60 feet are unaffected, and each of them ends one disease or one poison currently affecting it. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-cold-room","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Cold Room","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Reads the dead, on the grounds that they are the only honest witnesses left.","description":["Every body is a document. The Cold Room practice reads them: what killed this person, what they ate, what they were standing next to, which of six identical implants was the counterfeit. Some of them hold a municipal contract and some work out of a chest freezer in a rented unit. All of them are difficult company at dinner, and all of them know precisely where a living body keeps the parts it cannot replace."],"features":[{"name":"Post-Mortem","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Given 10 minutes and a body dead no longer than seven days, or a substantial piece of one, you learn its cause of death, the approximate time of death, every implant it carried, and the last thing it saw. You also learn one true fact about whoever was responsible, chosen by the DM."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Anatomy","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know where everything sits, and how little of it is load-bearing. Once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can spend one Trauma Die and deal extra necrotic damage equal to the roll plus your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature damaged this way cannot regain hit points until the end of your next turn. This feature has no effect on a creature without a recognisable anatomy, such as an ooze or a swarm."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The File","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep files. Each time you complete a post-mortem, record the kind of creature you examined. Your file has room for everything you ever open up."},{"type":"p","text":"Against a kind in your file, you know its damage resistances, immunities and vulnerabilities on sight, you have advantage on Intelligence and Wisdom checks to recall information about it, and you roll your Anatomy damage twice and use the higher total."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Statement of the Deceased","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 1 minute with a body dead no longer than 30 days, or with a hand, a head or a length of spine taken from one, you can put three questions to it. It answers truthfully and in its own voice, within the limits of what it knew while alive, and it cannot lie to you."},{"type":"p","text":"A given body answers you only once, ever. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cause of Death","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can fill in the certificate before the fact. As a bonus action, choose a creature you can see within 60 feet and name a cause of death for it. The naming lasts until you use this feature again or the creature dies."},{"type":"p","text":"Your weapon attacks score a critical hit against a named creature on a roll of 19 or 20, hit points it regains from any source are halved, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Wisdom (Perception) checks concerning it."},{"type":"p","text":"If it dies while named, you regain expended Trauma Dice equal to your proficiency bonus."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Time of Death","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can touch a creature, or target a creature within 30 feet that you have named with Cause of Death. It makes a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save it takes 12d8 necrotic damage and cannot regain hit points for 1 minute. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and cannot regain hit points until the end of its next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest. If the damage reduces the creature to 0 hit points, the paperwork was already correct."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-freightline","cls":"Fixer","name":"Freightline","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Moves what cannot legally exist from where it is to where somebody wants it.","description":["Freight is a solved problem right up to the point where the cargo is illegal, alive, or both. A Freightline operator solves it anyway, with a false floor, a route that misses four specific cameras, and a night manager who owes money to somebody else. They are paid on delivery and they do not open the crate. The rest of the crew usually finds out what was in it afterwards."],"features":[{"name":"False Floor","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 10 minutes you can prepare a concealed space in a vehicle, a room or your own clothing, holding up to 2 cubic feet. You can maintain a number of prepared spaces equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can abandon one at any time."},{"type":"p","text":"Cargo in a space you prepared is not found by a search, sniff or physical inspection unless the searcher succeeds on an Intelligence (Investigation) check with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. Scanners, sensors and automated inspection systems simply return nothing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Route Knowledge","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know how the city actually moves, as opposed to how the maps claim it does. You always know one unwatched way into and one unwatched way out of any district, building or checkpoint you can see, or that you have researched for 10 minutes."},{"type":"p","text":"Travel you personally plan takes half the usual time, and you and creatures travelling with you have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to avoid patrols, tolls, tails and inspections."}],"sub":false},{"name":"At the Controls","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with land, water and air vehicles. While you are driving or piloting, the vehicle's speed increases by 20 feet and you add your Charisma modifier to its AC."},{"type":"p","text":"When a creature makes an attack roll against the vehicle, or against a creature inside it, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on that roll. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chaff","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend one Favour die to dump cover: smoke, ceramic dust and cheap counterfeit heat sources. A 20-foot cube originating from a point you can see within 60 feet becomes heavily obscured for 1 minute. Sensors, targeting systems and smart optics cannot see into or through it at all."},{"type":"p","text":"Each creature in the cube when it deploys makes a Dexterity saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or is blinded until the end of its next turn. You and any creatures you choose can see through the cube normally."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Green Corridor","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 8 hours you can move up to twelve creatures and their equipment anywhere in the city or out of it, without being seen, logged, scanned, tolled or stopped."},{"type":"p","text":"Nobody records the journey and nobody can retrace it. Attempts to determine where the party went during that time, by investigation, surveillance or divination, fail without returning anything useful. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nothing Declared","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been carrying more than anyone realised. Once per long rest, you can declare that a single item worth up to 100,000\u20b5 has been in your load the whole time. It is here now, and a plausible record of how it got here exists."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, when you or an ally within 30 feet is searched, disarmed, or has an item confiscated, you can spend one Favour die to establish that the item was never found. They still have it, and the searcher is satisfied the search was thorough."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-confessor","cls":"Fixer","name":"Confessor","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Collects the one thing each person cannot afford to have said out loud.","description":["Everybody in this city is carrying something they would pay to keep quiet, and most of them are carrying it badly. The Confessor's work is mostly patience: sit in enough rooms, buy enough drinks, and the secret arrives under its own power. They rarely threaten anyone. They mention that they know, and let the other party do the arithmetic."],"features":[{"name":"Something on Everyone","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After an hour in a creature's company, or 10 minutes with its correspondence, accounts, medical record or messages, you learn one genuine secret it is keeping. The DM decides what it is. It is always something the creature would take real steps to protect."},{"type":"p","text":"Write it down. You now hold a file on that creature, and a file stays open until you spend or discard it. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Mention It","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can let a creature you hold a file on understand that you hold it. It makes a Charisma saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. Spending the file this way closes it."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, for the next hour the creature will not attack you, will not raise an alarm concerning you, and will not reveal your presence or your business to anyone. It also has disadvantage on ability checks made in direct opposition to yours. The effect ends immediately if you or an ally attacks it."},{"type":"p","text":"On a successful save, it now knows exactly what you have, and it begins making arrangements."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cross-Reference","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Secrets are rarely held alone. When you open a file on a creature, you also learn which other creatures know the same thing, and roughly what each of them did about it."},{"type":"p","text":"You have advantage on Charisma checks made against any creature you hold a file on. Spending a file no longer closes it; a file you have spent can be used again after you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Mutually Assured","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have arranged a release. Everything you hold is lodged with three people who do not know each other, and everyone relevant has been made aware of the arrangement."},{"type":"p","text":"Creatures you hold a file on have disadvantage on attack rolls against you. When one of them deals damage to you, it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or be frightened of you until the end of its next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Confession","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, choose a creature within 30 feet that can hear and understand you. It makes a Wisdom saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, for the next minute it cannot knowingly tell you a lie, and it must answer the next three questions you put to it truthfully and completely. Afterwards it remembers the conversation as something it chose to do."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest. You can also use it by spending three Favour dice."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nobody Is Clean","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can address a crowd, a boardroom or a firing line. Each creature within 60 feet that can hear and understand you makes a Charisma saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature says aloud the thing it least wants said, is stunned until the end of its next turn, and is frightened of you for 1 minute. It repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the frightened condition on a success."},{"type":"p","text":"You open a file on every creature that failed, ignoring the usual limit. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-papermill","cls":"Fixer","name":"Papermill","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Makes people out of paperwork. Unmakes them the same way.","description":["An identity in this city is a set of records that agree with one another. The Papermill's trade is manufacturing that agreement: a birth entry, nine years of tax history, transit logs, a dentist who remembers the patient. Their clients are people running from a contract, people who need to be two employees at once, and people who have decided to stop existing. Done properly the work is slow, expensive and entirely undetectable."],"features":[{"name":"Legends","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a long rest you can build a legend: a complete manufactured identity with records, history, biometric registration and a plausible life behind it. You can hold a number of legends equal to your proficiency bonus, and retiring one takes 1 minute and burns it permanently."},{"type":"p","text":"While wearing a legend, you automatically pass any records check, credential check or background check that does not involve somebody who knows your face personally, and you have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks made to maintain it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No Clean Prints","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your biometrics do not resolve. Attempts to identify you by face, gait, retina, print or genetic sample return a different person each time, always someone real and always someone inconvenient."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature examining such a result can spend 1 minute and succeed on an Intelligence (Investigation) check with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier to establish that the record has been tampered with. It still does not learn who you are."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Issue Credentials","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend one Favour die to issue a temporary credential to a creature you can see. For the next hour, automated systems, checkpoints and personnel treat it as authorised to be exactly where it is and doing exactly what it is doing."},{"type":"p","text":"An ally wearing a legend you built adds your Charisma modifier to Charisma (Deception) checks made to maintain it, and cannot be identified by automated means."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Attribution","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When an action taken by you or an ally within 60 feet is witnessed, recorded or investigated, you can spend one Favour die within the next 24 hours to attribute it to somebody else: a real person, credibly placed, with a motive. Investigators pursue them instead."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, when a creature correctly identifies or accuses you, you can use your reaction to force it to make an Intelligence saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier. On a failed save it becomes convinced it has made an error and cannot revisit the conclusion for 24 hours."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use the reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Corporate Person","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 8 hours you can incorporate: a shell company with premises, staffing records, credit history and a filing address that has existed, as far as anyone can determine, for years. It can hold property, sign contracts, employ your allies and apply for restricted licences."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, the entity can obtain lawful access for the party to one restricted site, shipment or system. You arrive as contractors, auditors or maintenance, with paperwork that checks out. You can maintain one entity at a time, and founding a new one dissolves the last."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Total Rewrite","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over 10 minutes, with access to any terminal, you can rewrite a person. Choose a creature you can see, or one whose full records you hold. In every system that checks, it becomes somebody else of your choosing: cleared, wanted, employed, deceased, or never born at all."},{"type":"p","text":"The change is real to every institution that matters, and reversing it takes weeks of legal work by somebody with standing. For 24 hours afterwards, a creature that personally knows the target and tries to act on that knowledge must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw with a DC of 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier or defer to the record instead."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a long rest. You can use it on yourself."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-method","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Method","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Has been four people this year. Two of them still get mail.","description":["Most Firebrands want a crowd to learn their name. The Method wants it to learn a name, and has spent three months making sure that name survives a background check. They work from a dossier rather than a script: a job history, a dentist, an overdue utility bill, a particular way of holding a cup. The performance does not stop when they leave the room, because there is no room."],"features":[{"name":"Working Identity","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You maintain a number of false identities equal to your proficiency bonus. Each has a name, a face you can hold, documents, and a history you have actually put in the ground. Assuming or dropping one takes 10 minutes somewhere unobserved."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are wearing an identity, you gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Credentials. You gain two skill or tool proficiencies chosen when you built the identity. They are proficiencies that person plausibly had.","Paperwork. Any attempt to check the identity's documents, employment record, medical file or credit history against public systems returns exactly what you put there.","Cover. A creature that suspects you must make a Wisdom (Insight) check contested by your Charisma (Deception) check. You add double your proficiency bonus to that check."]},{"type":"p","text":"Building a new identity from nothing takes three days of downtime and 2,000\u20b5."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Doubt Is Expensive","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within your Audience range accuses you of being someone other than who you say you are, you can use your reaction and spend 1 Signal. The creature must make a Charisma saving throw against your Signal DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, it accepts your account, cannot raise the accusation again for 24 hours, and every creature that heard the exchange has disadvantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks made against you for the rest of the scene."},{"type":"p","text":"On a successful save it is now certain, rather than suspicious, and will act on it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Paper Trail","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can write a person into the world. With 8 hours of work, a live connection and 5,000\u20b5, one of your identities acquires a verifiable corporate footprint: an employer, a clearance, a lease, references who answer their phones and remember them fondly. Systems and the people who read them treat that identity as a real employee up to mid-level rank."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also work the other direction. Once per long rest, as an action, you can hang something you did on a creature you have studied for at least 1 hour. Records, witnesses and footage place that creature at the scene instead of you. Undoing it takes a funded forensic investigation and about a week, by which time the arrest has already happened."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Under the Face","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can wear a living person. After studying a humanoid for 1 hour, watching how it moves and where it hesitates, you can take its identity as though it were one of your own. Its colleagues, its building and its biometrics accept you."},{"type":"p","text":"Only a creature that knows the original intimately gets a check to notice, and it makes that Wisdom (Insight) check with disadvantage against your Charisma (Deception) check."},{"type":"p","text":"While wearing someone's identity, you have advantage on Charisma checks made against any creature that works for them, reports to them or is afraid of them."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nobody By That Name","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can burn an identity. Every creature within your Audience range that knows you only as that identity must make a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature loses any usable memory of your face, your voice and where to find you. It retains the name and the strong sense that the name mattered, which is worse for it than forgetting entirely."},{"type":"p","text":"Over the following hour, records referencing that identity degrade on their own. Files corrupt, footage skips, two witnesses contradict each other under oath. Any pursuit of that identity stops, because there is no longer anything at the end of it. You can never use that identity again."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-revival","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Revival","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Runs a congregation out of a rented unit and takes the collection in favours.","description":["Revival preaches. The venue is a car park, a laundromat after closing, or the ninth floor of a building with no ninth-floor tenants. What the congregation believes varies enormously between preachers; that they believe it hard, in a room with this person at the front, does not. The faithful bring food, gossip, a van when one is needed, and on the bad nights their own bodies."],"features":[{"name":"The Faithful","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a congregation. In any district where you have preached for at least an hour, you can count on a meal, a bed, a lookout on the corner, and a consistent story told to anyone official who comes asking."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can call on them. Within 10 minutes, 2d4 congregants arrive. Each has AC 11, 9 hit points, a speed of 30 feet, and a +4 bonus to one skill check reflecting whatever they do for a living."},{"type":"p","text":"They will carry, drive, watch a door, crowd a corridor and lie to a badge. They will not fight, and they will not come back if you spend them carelessly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Testify","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, spend 1 Signal to name a creature within your Audience range and say something true about it out loud. That creature gains temporary hit points equal to your Inspiration die + your Charisma modifier, and it has advantage on the next saving throw it makes before the end of your next turn."},{"type":"p","text":"If at least five other creatures heard you say it, the temporary hit points are doubled. This is the entire reason the congregation sits so close together."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Articles","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you finish a long rest, you can set a tenet for the day: one prohibition or one obligation, stated plainly enough to be obeyed under fire. Any ally who hears it may accept it, and may drop it at any time by saying so."},{"type":"p","text":"An ally who has accepted your tenet adds your Inspiration die to saving throws against being charmed or frightened."},{"type":"p","text":"When an ally keeps the tenet at a real and visible cost to themselves, you regain 1 Signal. You can regain Signal this way a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Witnessed","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Belief holds you up in a way you have stopped trying to explain. While at least one creature that has accepted your creed can see you, you can spend 2 Signal as a reaction when you fail a saving throw to succeed on it instead."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Healing","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 3 Signal. Every ally within your Audience range who can hear you regains hit points equal to your Firebrand level + your Charisma modifier, and ends one condition affecting them from this list: blinded, deafened, frightened, paralysed or poisoned."},{"type":"p","text":"You have never once claimed it was a miracle. It works anyway, which is a harder problem and one you have stopped raising in public."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Altar Call","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you make the ask. Every creature within your Audience range that can hear you must make a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature joins the congregation for 24 hours. It obeys instructions that do not require it to die, treats your allies as its own, and puts itself between you and harm without being told to. A creature that fails by 5 or more will die for you, and sometimes does."},{"type":"p","text":"When it ends, the congregation is larger than it was and it wants something. The DM decides what, and you do not get a say."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-main-event","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Main Event","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Fights in front of people, because the fight is only half of the work.","description":["The Main Event sells tickets. Pit bouts, sponsored duels, a grudge settled on a freight platform with six hundred people leaning over the rails and betting. They train for the fight and then rehearse the walk to it. A blow that lands quietly is worth less than one that lands where the cameras are, and their entire style is built around the difference."],"features":[{"name":"Fight Night","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with martial melee weapons."},{"type":"p","text":"While at least one creature that is neither you nor your ally can see you fight, you add your Charisma modifier to the damage rolls of your melee weapon attacks."},{"type":"p","text":"The room pays you back. The first time on each of your turns that you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack in front of such an audience, you gain 1 Signal. You cannot gain more Signal this way during a single combat than your proficiency bonus."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sell It","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take damage from an attack you can see, you can use your reaction and spend 1 Signal to make a meal of it: the stagger, the spray, the hand up for quiet. Reduce the damage by your Inspiration die + your Charisma modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"One ally within your Audience range who saw it gains temporary hit points equal to the amount you reduced. Getting hit properly is a service you provide."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Finish","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once on each of your turns, when you hit a creature that is below half its hit point maximum with a melee weapon attack, you can spend 2 Signal to end it where everyone can see. The attack deals extra damage equal to twice your Inspiration die."},{"type":"p","text":"If that attack reduces the creature to 0 hit points, every hostile creature within your Audience range that saw it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC or be frightened of you until the end of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grudge Match","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, spend 3 Signal to call out one creature you can see within your Audience range. It must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your Signal DC or accept, whether or not it wants to."},{"type":"p","text":"For 1 minute, or until either of you drops to 0 hit points, that creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you and cannot willingly move more than 30 feet from you. For the same duration you have advantage on attack rolls against it and resistance to the damage it deals you."},{"type":"p","text":"Nothing else in the fight matters while this is running, and everyone watching knows it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ten Count","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when you are reduced to 0 hit points while at least one creature that is not your ally can see you, you drop to 1 hit point instead and regain Signal equal to your proficiency bonus. The noise does the rest."},{"type":"p","text":"For the next minute, your melee weapon attacks deal one extra die of their damage, and each hostile creature that can see you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC at the start of its turn or be unable to take reactions until the start of its next turn."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-squatter","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Squatter","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Wearing a body that still gets recognised on the wrong streets.","description":["This sleeve was not bought and was not issued. Somebody else grew up in it, learned a trade in it, and was still using it when the Squatter moved in. The hands know things the person behind them never studied. So do the people who spot the face across a bar and come over smiling, holding two drinks."],"features":[{"name":"Previous Occupant","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The body you are wearing belonged to someone and has not finished being them. Choose two skill or tool proficiencies the previous owner had. You have those proficiencies while you wear this sleeve, in addition to your imprints."},{"type":"p","text":"You automatically pass any biometric scan, facial match or records check that the previous owner would have passed, and any creature that knew them accepts you as them until you give it a reason not to."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per short or long rest, when you fail an ability check using one of those two proficiencies, the hands remember better than you do. Reroll the check and use the new result."},{"type":"p","text":"You also know when a creature that knew the previous owner is within 60 feet of you. You do not know which one, or what they are owed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Flinch","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The sleeve reacts before you have finished deciding anything. When you are hit by an attack you can see, or when you fail a Dexterity saving throw, you can use your reaction to add your proficiency bonus to your Armour Class against that attack or to that saving throw, potentially turning a hit into a miss or a failure into a success."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Peel","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can move house without a clinic. Over 1 minute, you can transfer your stack into the body of a humanoid that died within the last hour, provided its neck is intact. You resleeve with no downtime and no cost, arriving with half your hit point maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"The new sleeve has its own appearance and biometrics and one sleeve package of your choice. You gain two skill or tool proficiencies from its previous owner as described in Previous Occupant, replacing the two you had."},{"type":"p","text":"This is illegal everywhere that has an opinion on the matter, and is generally prosecuted as two separate crimes."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Let Them Drive","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per short or long rest, as a bonus action, you can stop steering for 1 minute and let the reflexes underneath take it."},{"type":"p","text":"For the duration you have advantage on attack rolls and Dexterity saving throws, your walking speed increases by 10 feet, and you cannot be surprised. You also have disadvantage on Wisdom and Charisma checks, because whoever is answering questions is not you."},{"type":"p","text":"When it ends, make a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save you take 3d6 psychic damage and lose the last minute entirely, including anything anyone said to you during it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Skin","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can spend 3 Stack Charge to rewrite the sleeve you are wearing. Over the following 10 minutes it restructures to match any humanoid you have physically touched in the last 24 hours: face, build, voice, gait, prints, retinas, blood chemistry. It lasts 8 hours, or until you end it as an action."},{"type":"p","text":"Any creature that knew the original must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw with a DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier or accept you as them without reservation. No scanner, sample or medical record disagrees."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature that succeeds knows only that something is wrong. It does not know what, and saying so out loud rarely goes well for it."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-parallel","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Parallel","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Runs in more than one place and keeps every appointment.","description":["A stack is a file, and files copy. The Parallel treats that as a scheduling solution rather than a philosophical emergency, and spends most jobs in two rooms at once. The instances share everything up to the moment of the split and compare notes afterwards. They almost never argue, which some people find more disturbing than if they did."],"features":[{"name":"Instance","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can spend 1 Stack Charge to run a partial copy of yourself in a prepared shell within 1 mile: a vat body on a rack, a service frame, a rented sleeve left switched on in a locker. The instance wakes in that shell and lasts 10 minutes, until it drops to 0 hit points, or until you dismiss it as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"An instance has your ability scores, skills, imprints and proficiency bonus, an Armour Class of 12, hit points equal to your Stackborn level, and a walking speed of 30 feet. It takes its own turn on your initiative, immediately after yours, and can take any action except the Attack action."},{"type":"p","text":"You can see and hear through an instance at will, and you gain everything it learned when it ends. If it is destroyed rather than dismissed, you take 2d6 psychic damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Threaded","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can run two instances at once, and starting one costs a bonus action rather than an action."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also consult them. When you make an Intelligence or Wisdom check, you can use your reaction to add your proficiency bonus to the result, provided one of your instances is somewhere that could plausibly help: a terminal, a records office, a rooftop with a view of the street you are asking about."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Running Hot","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your instances stop being partial. An instance now has an Armour Class equal to yours and hit points equal to half your hit point maximum, and it can take the Attack action, making one weapon attack using your attack bonus and damage."},{"type":"p","text":"It attacks with whatever its shell is holding, which means the shells have to be armed in advance. Most of the job is arranging that, and most of the expense."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Merge","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When an instance ends for any reason, including being destroyed, you take no psychic damage from it and you regain 1 Stack Charge."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can also pull an active instance back into yourself as a bonus action. You regain hit points equal to five times your proficiency bonus and end one condition affecting you, as a version of you that did not have the problem writes over the version that does."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No Single Point","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can run up to three instances at once, and each active instance can take a reaction on your behalf in addition to your own."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as a bonus action, you can synchronise for 1 minute. For the duration, every active instance takes a full turn on your initiative, including a bonus action, and all of you share senses and know what the others know as it happens."},{"type":"p","text":"If the body holding your stack is destroyed while an instance is running, you do not die. Control passes to the nearest instance at the start of your next turn and the job carries on from there, one body short."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-quorum","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Quorum","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Backed up so often that the copies now hold meetings about it.","description":["Somewhere between the eleventh restore and the nineteenth, the versions stopped matching. The Quorum keeps all of them running quietly in cold storage and asks them things. They disagree, constantly and in detail. That turns out to be the useful part, although it does make ordering food take a while."],"features":[{"name":"The Committee","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep a set of divergent copies of yourself in storage, each restored from a different backup and none of them quite you. Consulting them takes a moment and a high tolerance for being contradicted."},{"type":"p","text":"When you make an ability check or a saving throw, you can put it to the committee. Roll three d20s instead of one and use the middle result. You must decide to do this before you roll."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"The committee is cautious by nature. You will fumble far less often, and you will stop having the sort of luck people write songs about."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No Consensus","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"There is no single mind in here for anything to take hold of. You have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened, or compelled to speak truthfully, and any effect that would read, copy or edit your memories fails unless it can defeat every stored copy of you at the same time."},{"type":"p","text":"Wisdom (Insight) checks made to read you have disadvantage, because the tells contradict one another."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Dissent","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One of them has almost always seen this before. You can use your reaction to let a copy object when a creature you can see makes an attack roll against you, or when you make an ability check to recall information about a place, an organisation or a person."},{"type":"p","text":"Against the attack, the attacker has disadvantage. Against the check, you automatically succeed at any task the DM judges some competent version of you could have known."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ratified","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can spend 10 minutes in session and put a single objective to a vote, stated in one plain sentence that all of you will agree to."},{"type":"p","text":"For the next 24 hours, or until the objective is met or formally abandoned, you have advantage on ability checks and saving throws made directly in service of it, and you cannot be deceived about anything material to it. A lie on the subject registers as a lie, though not as what the truth is."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Casting Vote","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Committee feature now uses the highest of the three dice rather than the middle one. The cautious ones have been outvoted."},{"type":"p","text":"You also no longer need a clinic to come back. If your body and your stack are both destroyed, the committee convenes, elects the copy with the best claim, and installs it in a prepared sleeve within 1 hour. You return as that copy, with its memories, which end 1d4 days before your death."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do this three times. Each time, the DM tells you one opinion you now hold that you did not hold before, and you do not get to argue about it."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-hadal","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Hadal","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Rated for pressures that fold a person. Uncomfortable at sea level.","description":["Salvage at four thousand metres, hull work in hard vacuum, the flooded levels under a district that sank in the nineties and was written off. The Hadal strain is grown for jobs that kill an unmodified person inside a minute. On the surface they are slow, heavy and slightly deaf, and they spend most conversations waiting to go back down."],"features":[{"name":"Pressure Rated","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to breathe, and you are immune to the effects of depth, pressure change and vacuum. You have resistance to cold damage and you ignore the effects of extreme cold."},{"type":"p","text":"You gain a swimming speed equal to your walking speed, and you can move your full speed in freefall or zero gravity without an ability check."},{"type":"p","text":"You also have blindsight out to 60 feet while submerged, and out to 20 feet otherwise. It works on pressure and sound rather than light, so darkness and smoke are irrelevant to it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rated Grip","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your hands were grown to hold a plate steady against a current. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike or a natural weapon, you can grapple it as a bonus action, and you can grapple creatures one size larger than a creature of your size normally could."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature grappled by you takes bludgeoning damage equal to 1d10 + your Constitution modifier at the start of each of your turns, and it has disadvantage on ability checks made to escape the grapple."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Equalise","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 2 Biomass to vent the differential through your skin. Each creature within 15 feet of you must make a Constitution saving throw against your Graft DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage, is pushed 10 feet away from you, and is deafened until the end of its next turn. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and is neither pushed nor deafened."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Torpor","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can switch most of yourself off. As an action you enter torpor: you are unconscious, you appear dead to any examination short of surgery, and you need no air, food, water or warmth. You can stay that way for up to a week and wake at a time you set beforehand or when you take damage, restoring all your hit points and half your spent Hit Dice."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also do it quickly. When damage would reduce you to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to drop to 1 hit point and enter torpor instead. You are paralysed and convincingly dead for 1 minute, then wake with half your hit point maximum. You can use this second option once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crush Depth","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 4 Biomass. For 1 minute, the pressure within 20 feet of you is wrong in a way that bodies understand before minds do."},{"type":"p","text":"A hostile creature that starts its turn in the area takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage and has its speed halved until the start of its next turn. Ranged attack rolls made into or through the area have disadvantage, and a creature inside it cannot speak above a whisper or hear anything that is not touching it."},{"type":"p","text":"You are unaffected. You have worked in considerably worse."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-antibody","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Antibody","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Its immune system treats other people as a diagnosis.","description":["The Antibody strain was licensed as a plague response: a body that identifies a pathogen and manufactures the counter faster than a laboratory can. It works. It also draws no careful distinction between a pathogen and a person standing close enough to breathe on. Hosts run a low fever permanently and are not allowed in clean rooms."],"features":[{"name":"Acquired Response","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature damages you, you can use your reaction to sample it. For the next hour you have advantage on saving throws against that creature's attacks and abilities, and your unarmed strikes and natural weapons deal an extra 1d6 necrotic damage against it and against any creature of the same kind."},{"type":"p","text":"You can hold one sample at a time, two at 10th level and three at 17th level."},{"type":"p","text":"You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sterile Field","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anything small enough to be outvoted does badly near you. You and any ally within 10 feet of you have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can touch a creature and end one disease affecting it, or end the poisoned condition on it. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Inflammation","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, spend 1 Biomass to run hot for 1 minute. While it lasts, a creature that hits you with a melee attack takes necrotic damage equal to 1d8 + your Constitution modifier, and you have advantage on Constitution saving throws."},{"type":"p","text":"Your core temperature during this is medically alarming and shows up on every thermal sensor in the building."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rejection","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can teach a body to refuse its own upgrades. As an action, spend 2 Biomass and choose a creature you can see within 30 feet. It must make a Constitution saving throw against your Graft DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, it takes 4d8 necrotic damage and, for 1 minute, every piece of cyberware, augment and graft it carries stops working: no bonuses, no linked weapons, no sensors, and any chromed limb hangs off it as dead weight. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and its ware keeps running."},{"type":"p","text":"A creature carrying no installed ware ignores the second part entirely, and is usually insufferable about it afterwards."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Transfusion","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your blood does work that normally needs a clinic. As an action, spend 1 Biomass and open a vein for a willing creature. It regains 4d8 hit points, ends one disease or poison affecting it, and has advantage on Constitution saving throws for the next hour."},{"type":"p","text":"It can also be administered against the patient's wishes. If you have a creature grappled, you can use your action to force a transfusion. The creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your Graft DC or take 6d6 necrotic damage and be poisoned for 1 minute. Your blood is not compatible with anyone."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Immune Storm","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you stop regulating. For 1 minute, everything within 30 feet of you is inside your response."},{"type":"p","text":"At the start of each of its turns, a hostile creature in the area must make a Constitution saving throw against your Graft DC. On a failed save it takes 4d6 necrotic damage and has disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of its next turn. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect."},{"type":"p","text":"An ally that starts its turn in the area instead regains 2d6 hit points. Your system has decided they are yours, and does not take questions."},{"type":"p","text":"When it ends you have disadvantage on Constitution saving throws until you finish a short or long rest, and you sleep for twelve hours at the first opportunity."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-bloom","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Bloom","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Does not stop at the skin. The floor is part of it within the hour.","description":["Most cultured ware has the decency to stay inside the host. This strain never learned where the edge was. Left alone in a room overnight, a Bloom puts pale root mats down through the flooring and grows a nervous system into the building. Landlords have opinions about this. The Bloom has a rent-free warehouse and knows the weight of everyone who walks across it."],"features":[{"name":"Seeding","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action, spend 1 Biomass to seed a 15-foot square of ground you can see within 30 feet. Over the next round it grows a mat of pale root and feeder tissue. A growth lasts 1 hour, or until you dismiss it as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"A growth is difficult terrain for any creature you choose. You have blindsight within any of your growths and for 10 feet around them, and you know the size, direction and weight of anything moving across one."},{"type":"p","text":"You can maintain a number of growths at once equal to your proficiency bonus. Seeding another beyond that limit ends the oldest one."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rootfed","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are standing in one of your growths, you regain hit points equal to your proficiency bonus at the start of each of your turns, and you cannot be moved against your will unless the creature or effect moving you succeeds on a Strength check against your Graft DC."},{"type":"p","text":"A hostile creature that ends its turn in one of your growths takes 1d6 piercing damage as the feeder roots take their cut."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grasp","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 2 Biomass to make every growth you are maintaining close at once. Each hostile creature standing in one must make a Strength saving throw against your Graft DC."},{"type":"p","text":"On a failed save, a creature takes 4d8 piercing damage and is restrained. A restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength check against your Graft DC, freeing itself on a success. On a successful save it takes half as much damage and is not restrained."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Standing Crop","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Growths you plant no longer expire. They spread slowly on their own, thread themselves through whatever is underneath, and cannot be removed without taking up the floor and most of the wall."},{"type":"p","text":"You know the location of any creature in contact with one of your permanent growths anywhere within a mile of you, and you can speak through any of them at roughly a whisper."},{"type":"p","text":"As an action while touching one, you can pass through it. You sink into that growth and rise out of another permanent growth of yours within a mile. The journey takes 1 minute and is unpleasant for everyone involved, including the growth."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Colonise","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you commit everything you have to the ground. Every surface within 60 feet of you becomes your growth for 1 hour: floors, walls, parked vehicles, the underside of the ceiling."},{"type":"p","text":"For the duration, the area is difficult terrain for creatures you choose, you and your allies have half cover anywhere inside it, and a hostile creature takes 2d10 piercing damage at the start of each of its turns while it remains in the area. You can use Grasp anywhere in the area without spending Biomass."},{"type":"p","text":"When the hour is up, the growth dies back to a stain and a smell that lasts months. The building it grew through is structurally compromised, and the block has a story about it now."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null}],"feats":[{"name":"Chrome Junkie","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have rebuilt yourself past the point most bodies tolerate, and yours keeps accepting the load. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You gain a 15-point Humanity tolerance buffer, spent only after your Humanity reaches zero.","The Humanity cost of any cyberware you install is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 1.","You have advantage on saving throws made to resist the Fraying state's hostility."]}],"prerequisite":"At least one installed cyberware implant"},{"name":"Clean Baseline","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have never let anyone put anything inside you, and it shows in ways people find difficult to name. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You are immune to EMP effects, hacking, and any effect that targets cyberware.","You have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) and Wisdom (Insight) checks made with a creature that is itself heavily chromed, they find you restful, and slightly sad."]}],"prerequisite":"No installed cyberware or augments"},{"name":"Icebreaker's Instinct","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been burned by enough black ICE to feel it coming. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You gain proficiency with hacking tools, or expertise if you already have it.","When ICE would damage you, you can use your reaction to halve that damage."]}],"prerequisite":"Proficiency with hacking tools"},{"name":"Drone Whisperer","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Machines take instruction from you more readily than they should. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can issue a command to any friendly drone or construct as a free action once on each of your turns.","You have advantage on checks made to repair, override or reprogram a drone or vehicle."]}]},{"name":"Street Legend","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"People have heard the story. Some of it is even true. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Your Street Cred increases by 2.","Once per long rest, you can invoke your reputation to make one hostile creature that recognises you hesitate: it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier) or be frightened of you for 1 minute."]}]},{"name":"Fast Draw","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your hand is moving before the decision reaches your mouth. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can draw or stow two firearms whenever you could normally draw or stow one.","When you roll initiative and are not surprised, you can immediately make one attack with a one-handed firearm you are holding or can draw."]}]},{"name":"Neural Firewall","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Something in your head bites back. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would read your mind, control your implants, or force you out of a remote body.","A creature that attempts to hack your cyberware and fails takes psychic damage equal to twice your proficiency bonus."]}]},{"name":"Rated for Trauma","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been declared dead at least twice and found the paperwork premature. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on death saving throws.","When you regain hit points from an ally's ability while at 0 hit points, you regain an additional 1d10."]}]},{"name":"Chem Tolerance","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your liver has opinions and no authority. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on saving throws against addiction, and you take no penalty from withdrawal.","The beneficial effects of any drug or ampule last twice as long for you."]}]},{"name":"Second Skin","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You wear armour the way other people wear clothes. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You gain proficiency with medium armor and shields, or heavy armor if you already have both.","Wearing armour imposes no disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.","While wearing armour you have resistance to bludgeoning damage from falls, vehicles and explosions."]}]},{"name":"Wall Runner","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The city is a surface and you treat all of it as floor. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed.","You can move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling, as long as you end your turn on solid ground.","You take half damage from falls and can reduce fall damage further by the usual means."]}]},{"name":"Corporate Ghost","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Whatever file they pull on you is thin and mostly wrong. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence or Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Biometric and records searches for you return nothing, or return someone else.","You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks made to pass as an employee, official or licensed professional, and you always have plausible documentation."]}]},{"name":"Grafted","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have had cultured tissue seated into you by someone who knew what they were doing. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You gain one graft of your choice from the Bioforged graft list. It costs you no Essence and no Humanity.","You have advantage on saving throws against disease."]}]},{"name":"Stack Tapped","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Somebody fitted you with a cortical stack, and you are still deciding how you feel about it. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You have a cortical stack, as the Stackborn class feature. If your body dies with the stack intact, you can be resleeved given a clinic, 25,000\u20b5 and 24 hours.","You gain one imprint: a skill or tool proficiency from a life that was not yours.","You have disadvantage on saving throws against effects that target your stack specifically, it is an off-the-shelf model and everyone knows the model."]}]},{"name":"Crowd Sense","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know what a room is about to do before the room does. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can never be caught in a stampede, crush or riot against your will, and you always find the exit.","Once per short rest you can redirect a crowd's attention, causing every creature that is not hostile to you within 60 feet to look somewhere of your choosing for 6 seconds."]}]},{"name":"Black Market Contacts","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know which door to knock on, and what to bring. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can buy restricted, illegal or military-grade equipment at double its listed price, given 24 hours in any settlement of reasonable size.","You can sell stolen goods at 60% of value rather than the usual pittance, and nobody asks where they came from."]}]},{"name":"Smartlinked","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your weapons are wired into your optic nerve and they no longer feel like tools. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity or Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You ignore half cover and three-quarters cover with firearm attacks.","Attacking at long range with a firearm does not impose disadvantage on your attack rolls."]}],"prerequisite":"Proficiency with at least one firearm"},{"name":"Overclocked Metabolism","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You burn hot, heal fast, and will probably not see forty. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Your speed increases by 10 feet.","When you finish a short rest you regain hit points equal to your level without spending Hit Dice. Once per long rest.","You require twice as much food and water as normal, and you age at twice the usual rate."]}]}],"systems":[{"name":"Humanity","tagline":"Every piece of chrome is a piece of you that used to be meat.","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Chrome is not free. The genre this book lives in has always charged for it, an implant buys you speed, reach or a second set of eyes, and takes back some measure of the person you were. Humanity is the ledger."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Humanity score is your Charisma score multiplied by 5, to a maximum of 100. A character with Charisma 12 starts at 60 Humanity. This is your baseline: the distance between you and the thing that walks out of a back-alley clinic with nothing human left behind its eyes."},{"type":"p","text":"Installing cyberware costs Humanity permanently, by tier. Augments, the smaller, less invasive grade of ware, cost 1 each. Removing an implant refunds its full Humanity cost after a week of convalescence, which is why so many operators run light before a job that needs a human touch."},{"type":"table","title":"Humanity Cost by Tier","headers":["Installed Ware","Humanity Cost"],"rows":[["Augment (any)","1"],["Cyberware, tier 1","2"],["Cyberware, tier 2","5"],["Cyberware, tier 3","9"],["Cyberware, tier 4","14"]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Humanity is measured against your starting score as a percentage, so a naturally warm character has further to fall than a cold one. As it drops you pass through states, and each one takes something from you."},{"type":"table","title":"States of Humanity","headers":["Remaining","State","Effect"],"rows":[["60% or more","Baseline","No effect. You still flinch at the right things."],["40\u201359%","Dissociated","You have disadvantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks against anyone who can see your chrome, and on Wisdom (Insight) checks to read emotion."],["20\u201339%","Fraying","When you take a critical hit or drop to 0 hit points, make a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, until the end of your next turn you must move toward and attack the nearest creature, making no distinction between friend and target."],["1\u201319%","Flatlining","You have disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws. A long rest restores only half your spent Hit Dice, rounded down. You no longer dream."],["0","Cyberpsychosis","Your character is lost. They become an NPC under the DM's control. Only sustained therapy and the removal of ware can bring them back, and the person who returns is not quite the person who left."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Therapy. Between jobs you can commit to treatment: 7 days of downtime and 5,000\u20b5 per day restores 1 Humanity per day, to a maximum of your starting score minus the cost of ware still installed. A Streetdoc with the Counsellor's Licence feature halves the cost and doubles the rate."},{"type":"p","text":"A note for the table. Humanity is a horror dial, not a morality one. It does not measure whether a character is good, a saint with four limbs of surgical steel is still a saint. It measures how far they have drifted from the baseline their own nervous system expects, and how much that drift costs them when they need to look someone in the eye. Groups who want the chrome without the dread should treat the whole track as optional; nothing else in this expansion breaks without it."}]},{"name":"Street Cred","tagline":"What the city thinks you are, before you open your mouth.","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Street Cred is a shared track that runs from 0 to 10 and answers one question: does the street know your name? It rises when you do something the street can see, a job that made the feeds, a corp embarrassed in public, a debt paid in front of witnesses, and falls when you are seen to fold."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Cred is a bonus you can add to a Charisma check made against someone who has heard of you, once per scene. It is also a liability: every point of Cred is a point of description in somebody's file on you."},{"type":"table","title":"Street Cred","headers":["Cred","Standing","What It Buys"],"rows":[["0","Nobody","You get searched at the door."],["1\u20132","Known face","+1 to Charisma checks with fixers and gangs. A fixer will take your call."],["3\u20134","Somebody","+2. You can call in a minor favour once per job without spending a Favour die."],["5\u20136","Name","+3. Doors open. So do files, corps now run your face on sight."],["7\u20138","Legend","+4. Rivals inherit your enemies. One faction actively wants you dead."],["9\u201310","Myth","+5. Strangers do favours unasked, and the price on your head funds a small army."]]},{"type":"p","text":"The DM awards Cred, usually 1 point per job that ended loudly, and takes it back for a public humiliation. A Fixer or a Firebrand generates it faster than anyone; a Wirewalker who does the job properly generates none at all, which is the point of doing the job properly."}]}],"origins":{"name":"Origins","tagline":"Where you were standing when the world happened to you.","intro":["A background says what you did for money. An origin says what was done to you first. Choose one, or roll a d12. An origin grants one small mechanical perk and a hook the DM can pull on. It stacks with your background, they answer different questions."],"table":{"type":"table","title":"Origins","headers":["d12","Origin","Perk"],"rows":[["1","Arcology Born","You have never touched unfiltered soil. You know corporate procedure cold: advantage on Intelligence checks to recall how a corporation's internal systems or hierarchies work."],["2","Combat Zone Raised","You grew up where the police stopped going. You can always find a defensible position: once per short rest, take the Dodge action as a bonus action."],["3","Debt Indentured","You were born owing. You start with an extra 5,000\u20b5 of gear and a creditor who knows exactly where you sleep."],["4","Orbital Drop","Raised in low gravity, rebuilt for this one. You ignore difficult terrain caused by rubble, wreckage or low visibility."],["5","Nomad Convoy","The road was the address. You gain proficiency with one type of vehicle and can sleep soundly anywhere that moves."],["6","Lab Product","You have a serial number where a birth certificate should be. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease, and someone owns your patent."],["7","Church of the Signal","You were raised to believe the NET is listening. You can always tell when a room is under electronic surveillance with a DC 13 Wisdom (Perception) check."],["8","Corporate Legacy","Your family name still opens one door. Once per job, you can invoke it for access, and the person you invoke it with reports the contact upward."],["9","Gutter Clinic","You were stitched back together by someone unlicensed. You stabilise at 1 hit point instead of 0 the first time you would drop each long rest."],["10","Ex-Military","Someone trained you properly and then discarded you. You gain proficiency with martial firearms and one set of artisan's tools used for maintenance."],["11","Ghost Identity","Officially you do not exist. Biometric and records searches for you fail, which is useful until you need a bank account, a clinic or a lawyer."],["12","Rebuilt","You died once already and something put you back. You have advantage on death saving throws, and you remember nothing from before the table."]]}}};
